\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US auto workers strike escalates as \uc2 UAW\uc2  president calls on 38 more plants to join\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 579 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2023\par 20:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain announces additional strikes as contract talks remain far apart on economic issues, and invites Biden to join picket line\par \par \uc2 The historic US autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 strike escalated on Friday as the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, called on 38 additional plants across 20 states to join the strike.\par \par \uc2 During a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/uaw.union/videos/2065835110423564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live stream update}}}\uc2  on Friday morning, Fain announced the additional strikes at automaker plants as contract negotiations with the big three automakers remain far apart on economic issues.\par \par \uc2 The strike is the first to hit all three of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest vehicle manufacturers at the same time and is becoming increasingly political. Fain invited Joe Biden to the picket line on Friday and, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/09/22/uaw-strike-updates-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2 , Biden will visit the picket lines next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe invite and encourage everyone who supports our case to join us on the picket line, from our friends and families all the way up to the president of the United States. We invite you to join us in our fight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain.\par \par \uc2 Fain noted there had been some real progress in negotiations with Ford, including eliminating a lower wage tier, additional job security, conversion for all temporary workers, reinstating cost of living adjustment that was eliminated in 2009, and the right to strike over plant closures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe companies know how to make this right,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain during the live stream. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 GM\uc2  in particular are going to need some serious pushing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is watching, and the people are on our side. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen poll after poll come out saying the American people support what we are doing,\u8221\'20\'1D added Fain.\par \par \uc2 Politicians on both sides have seized on the dispute. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will make a speech in Detroit next Wednesday, a day after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit, where he will attempt to woo \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers. Other Republicans have thrown their support behind the strikers despite the party\u8217\'20\'19s long-term antipathy towards organized labor.\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott, a presidential hopeful, has maintained the traditional party line and said striking workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/09/22/uaw-tim-scott-complaint-strike-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be fired}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrats have already come out in support of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and on Sunday, \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio Cortez\uc2  and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1704951720550215740"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set}}}\uc2  to appear in Wentzville, Missouri, at a solidarity rally where \uc2 General Motors\uc2  autoworkers have been on strike.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/15/auto-workers-strike-ford-gm-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began striking}}}\uc2  on 15 September through a \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up\u8221\'20\'1D strike strategy with walkouts at targeted plants to keep the automakers guessing. Three plants with about 13,000 workers walked out last Friday, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant in Toledo, Ohio, a Ford plant in Wayne, Michigan, and a \uc2 General Motors\uc2  plant in Wentzville, Missouri.\par \par \uc2 The surprise strategy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/09/19/uaw-strike-auto-plants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  caused the automakers to prepare for strikes at the wrong plants, causing further disruptions. The automakers have responded to the strikes with temporary layoffs, with \uc2 Stellantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.freep.com%2Fstory%2Fmoney%2Fcars%2F2023%2F09%2F20%2Fuaw-strike-update-day-6-includes-new-stellantis-offer-plant-layoffs%2F70911560007%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing}}}\uc2  300 layoffs at three plants, \uc2 General Motors{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/09/20/1200626587/uaw-strike-gm-job-cuts-layoffs-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing}}}\uc2  2,000 temporary layoffs in Kansas, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsnationnow.com/business/layoffs-begin-at-michigan-ford-plant-as-strike-enters-sixth-day/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 600 layoffs }}}\uc2  announced at the Ford plant in Wayne, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Autoworkers have called for substantial wage increases and the return of benefits conceded during the 2008 economic recession but never reinstated once the automakers returned to profitability. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/20/this-fight-is-for-everybody-us-autoworkers-strike-to-restore-the-middle-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  the multibillion-dollar profits reported by the big three automakers in the past decade, including exorbitant executive salaries and billions funneled to Wall Street through stock buybacks and dividends. The automakers have characterized the union\u8217\'20\'19s asks as \u8220\'20\'1Cunsustainable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230922ej9m0023f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*