\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is the next biggest union target in the United States. Sorry, \uc2 Elon Musk\b0\par\par\uc2 Hamilton Nolan \par \uc2 1,046 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2023\par 14:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The carmaker is now US labor\u8217\'20\'19s most important target. If Musk doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like that, he\u8217\'20\'19s welcome to settle it with an auto worker by cage match\par \par \uc2 The massive \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike against the big three automakers is, first and foremost, an awesome demonstration of labor power \u8211\'20\'13 the act of a powerful, longstanding industrial union, with newly radical leadership, determined to wage one big fight to reset a playing field that has been slowly tilting in the wrong direction for years. It is also, like a disturbing number of things in America today, a case in which the grotesque specter of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  looms like a silent villain over the entire proceedings.\par \par \uc2 Here is what I mean. The big three \u8211\'20\'13 Ford, \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have long had workforces that are unionized with the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . The robust contracts that the union has been negotiating with the thriving industry since the middle of the 20th century played a large part in the creation of the unprecedented shared prosperity of the post-second world war middle class.\par \par \uc2 The American auto industry thrived, and the workers thrived along with it, and millions of families were able to live the \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Dream\u8221\'20\'1D on a blue-collar salary. That success story was eventually complicated by globalization and the offshoring of American jobs, but its legacy still exists today. The current strike, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mlive.com/public-interest/2023/09/a-simultaneous-big-three-strike-would-be-a-first-in-uaw-history-what-would-that-look-like.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first}}}\uc2  in \uc2 UAW\uc2  history to target all of the big three simultaneously, is to a large degree an attempt to ensure that \u8220\'20\'1Cshared prosperity\u8221\'20\'1D persists as a genuine thing in the profitable auto industry.\par \par \uc2 But there is a spoilsport sitting on the sideline, licking its chops: \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . Though it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t sell as many cars in America as the big three, the total value of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  (thanks to an army of cult-like investors) is more than five times the value of the Big Three companies combined. Despite years of effort from the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is not unionized.\par \par \uc2 The company has been found guilty of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/31/business/tesla-union-musk-twitter.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illegal}}}\uc2  union-busting tactics, including firing workers who were trying to organize. Such tactics are fully in line with the attitude of Musk himself, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/03/03/1084366833/elon-musk-dares-united-autoworkers-to-try-to-unionize-tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 routinely}}}\uc2  made anti-union statements and publicly threatened to take away employees\u8217\'20\'19 stock options if they unionized. Despite having a net worth of $270bn, Musk does not believe that the workers who make his products should be able to get together and negotiate a fair contract for themselves. He\u8217\'20\'19s greedy. He\u8217\'20\'19s ignorant. He\u8217\'20\'19s a crumb.\par \par \uc2 When the large majority of an industry is unionized, big strikes can raise standards for everyone, raising the floor for union and non-union workers alike. When only part of an industry is unionized, though, the non-union companies will always feel like they have an economic advantage \u8211\'20\'13 and, as a consequence, the unionized companies will fight harder against union demands, because they fear being undercut by their non-union competitors. The fact that unionized workers have higher job satisfaction, lower turnover and a better quality of life doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean much to the balance sheet-obsessed corporate executives who sit at the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 This dynamic is playing out in the auto strike right now. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  already pays its workers significantly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uaw-strike-shawn-fain-ford-gm-stellantis-tesla-80eeb202?mod=hp_opin_pos_1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less}}}\uc2  than the big three, and as long as Musk has no union to answer to, he will sit back and savor a \uc2 UAW\uc2  win against his competitors that widens that gap.\par \par \uc2 There is a straightforward solution to this: unionize \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . It is no exaggeration to say that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is now one of the most important union targets in America, given its structural role in undermining everything that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is fighting for. The only alternative solution \u8211\'20\'13 the one preferred by billionaires and executives who understand capitalism perfectly \u8211\'20\'13 is to break the backs of unions and purge them from the industry altogether.\par \par \uc2 This is exactly what auto companies are trying to do every time they move a factory into a poor, anti-union southern state, where they can run it without any pesky interference from anyone trying to empower the people working the line.\par \par \uc2 So yes, this is a fairly simple choice. We can have a profitable American auto industry that provides good quality union jobs to hundreds of thousands of workers and helps resurrect the beleaguered middle class; or, we can have a profitable American auto industry that provides billions of dollars to people like Musk and pushes wages as low as the most desperate worker in rural South Carolina will accept.\par \par \uc2 What we cannot have, in the long term, is a situation in which the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest conspiracy-addled \uc2 Twitter\uc2  addict uses the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s gains at the Big Three as a chance to increase his market share by sticking it to his own underpaid non-union workforce.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  knows damn well that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers need a union. But organizing an $800bn company run by a union buster with infinite money is not easy\par \par \uc2 Even inside the labor movement, many people see \u8220\'20\'1Cstrikes\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Corganizing new unions\u8221\'20\'1D as two separate things. They\u8217\'20\'19re not. They are, in reality, two pieces of a single {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hamiltonnolan.com/p/everything-were-doing-is-not-enough"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strategy}}}\uc2  for maintaining the delicate balance of power between labor and capital. Unless unions can organize all of the major competitors in an industry, they will always find the power of their strikes leaking out one side or another.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  knows damn well that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers need a union. But organizing an $800bn company run by a union buster with infinite money is not easy. The public, the politicians and every \uc2 Tesla\uc2  owner who would prefer not to be complicit in Gilded Age-style plutocratic inequality all need to lean on the big billionaire baby who can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine having to share.\par \par \uc2 Not even Musk can hide from the labor movement forever. It\u8217\'20\'19s been around a lot longer than he has. If he can\u8217\'20\'19t bear to have a free union election in his plant, I\u8217\'20\'19m sure that we could arrange a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/aug/16/elon-musk-mark-zuckerberg-cage-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cage match}}}\uc2  for him with an auto worker to settle this issue once and for all.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hamiltonnolan.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamilton Nolan}}}\uc2  is a writer on labor and politics, based in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230921ej9l001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
