\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US autoworkers to expand strikes amid contract stalemate: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re not messing around\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 425 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2023\par 11:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  to launch additional strikes if agreements with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford are not reached by 22 September\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 looks set to escalate strike actions against US car plants on Friday as the union struggles to reach a deal with the automakers \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, announced last week that the union would launch a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up\u8221\'20\'1D strikes at individual car plants after failing to reach agreement over a new union contract with the car companies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t make serious progress by noon on Friday, September 22nd, more locals will be called on to stand up and join the strike,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said this week. \u8220\'20\'1CAutoworkers have waited long enough to make things right at the big three. We\u8217\'20\'19re not waiting around and we\u8217\'20\'19re not messing around, so noon on September 22nd is a new deadline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  represents nearly 150,000 autoworkers at the manufacturers but has chosen to select local unions to strike rather than staging a mass walkout.\par \par \uc2 The strategy preserves the union\u8217\'20\'19s strike fund and aims to leave the companies guessing as to which sites will walk out, building pressure to come to an agreement. The strike is the first time the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has walked out at all three automakers at once.\par \par \uc2 Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have rebuffed the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposals as \u8220\'20\'1Cunsustainable\u8221\'20\'1D. Ford {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.ford.com/content/fordmedia/fna/us/en/news/2023/09/14/ford-update-on-uaw-negotiations.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  their last offer before the strike was \u8220\'20\'1Chistorically generous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFord remains absolutely committed to reaching an agreement that rewards our employees and protects Ford\u8217\'20\'19s ability to invest in the future as we move through industry-wide transformation,\u8221\'20\'1D Ford said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The union has emphasized the billions of dollars in profits the big three automakers have made since the 2008 economic recession and federal bailouts of the auto industry, where workers accepted numerous concessions that were never restored once the corporations returned to profitability.\par \par \uc2 The expanding strike is making political waves. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/09/18/biden-uaw-strike-picket-line/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressure}}}\uc2  from Democratic colleagues to join workers on the picket line. Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to hold a rally next week in Detroit with autoworkers during the Republican primary debate.\par \par \uc2 Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/biden-address-us-auto-negotiations-friday-white-house-2023-09-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on the automakers to increase their wage proposals to reach a deal with the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe they should go further to ensure record corporate profits mean record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said last week.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230921ej9l001pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
