\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike: union to resume contract negotiations on Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Johana Bhuiyan (now) and Maya Yang and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 7,779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par 23:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Plans to restart negotiations come after about 13,0000 workers walked out of three factories run by Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and StellantisBernie Sanders at rally: \u8216\'20\'18A fight against corporate greed\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for our live coverage of the strike today. Stay tuned for more news and stories from my colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 About 13,000 \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers from \uc2 GM\uc2  , Ford and Chrysler-parent company \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  went on strike after walking away from the contract bargaining table. The existing contract expired at midnight on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  CEO hit back at strikers for rejecting \u8216\'20\'18most significant offer\u8217\'20\'19 in 115 years saying she was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely frustrated and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President Joe Biden dispatched two aides, Gene Sperling and acting labor secretary Julie Su to Detroit to help move along negotiations and he urged both sides to return to the bargaining table. In remarks given from the White House, Biden said that \u8220\'20\'1Cno one wants a strike\u8221\'20\'1D but he believed \u8220\'20\'1Crecord corporate profits... should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThe companies have made some significant offers. But I believe that should go further to ensure record corporate profits mean record contracts,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account was briefly stripped of its blue verification check shortly after the the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikes began, a \uc2 UAW\uc2  official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/09/15/uaw-strike-twitter-verification-elon-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  the Intercept. The Intercept reports that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s blue check was restored once again after its initial story of the removed verification began circulating online.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers got wide-ranging support from members of congress including Bernie Sanders, \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  , Elizabeth Warren and Ohio senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  . \u8220\'20\'1CIt is totally reasonable for autoworkers to finally receive a fair share of the record breaking profits,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tensions from the strike escalated after \uc2 GM\uc2  announced it expected to idle a non-striking plant because it would soon run out of parts produced by a striking plant and give 2,000 workers temporary unemployment. Ford also said it would temporarily layoff 600 workers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  announced it would resume bargaining talks on Saturday, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  plans to return to bargaining table on Saturday\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  said it plans to resume contract negotiations on Saturday after 12,700 workers walked out of three factories run and owned by \uc2 GM\uc2  , Ford, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , the Chrysler parent company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/us-auto-union-strike-three-detroit-three-factories-2023-09-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Reuters }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The previous contract between the union and the automakers expired at midnight on Thursday. Speaking from the White House, President Biden urged both sides to return to the bargaining table. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/uaw-president-lot-work-remaining-reach-auto-labor-deals-2023-09-13/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 automakers\u8217\'20\'19 previous contract expired }}}\uc2  at 11:59pm ET on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  said it expects to temporarily pause operations at a non-striking plant in Kansas and put 2,000 non-striking workers on temporary unemployment because the plant is expected to run out of parts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/09/15/uaw-strike-updates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Washington Post }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GM\uc2  said the workers will not get the full slate of unemployment benefits they would typically get because they are working on an expired contract. Ford also expects to temporarily lay off 600 workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have said repeatedly that nobody wins in a strike and that effects go well beyond our employees on the plant floor and negatively impact our customers, suppliers and the communities where we do business,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 GM\uc2  told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images coming through the newswires of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  rally in Detroit, Michigan, where union representatives and lawmakers including senator Bernie Sanders and governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  took the stage:\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  members attend a rally in Detroit. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is conducting a strike against Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  . Photograph: Paul Sancya/AP United Auto Workers from Louisville, Kentucky, rally in support of striking \uc2 UAW\uc2  members, in Detroit, Michigan. Photograph: Rebecca Cook/Reuters Senator Bernie Sanders speaks to hundreds of \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  members at a rally. Photograph: Eric Cox/Reuters The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is conducting a strike against Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  . Photograph: Paul Sancya/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders at \uc2 UAW\uc2  rally: "We refuse to live in an oligarchy."\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is totally reasonable for autoworkers to finally receive a fair share of the record breaking profits,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe time is long overdue to end the disastrous two-tier system. It means finally ending the use of temporary workers and very importantly, it means that every auto worker receives a decent pension so they can retire with dignity,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, explaining the significance of the strikes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt means as we combat climate change, the existential threat of climate change, you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to make sure that this planet is healthy and habitable for our kids. That when the auto industry builds new electric vehicles and battery plants, it means that the workers in those plants become part of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and receive the same wages and benefits as union members.\par \par \uc2 Brothers and sisters, the CEOs of \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and their major stockholders on Wall Street have got to understand, they cannot have it all.\par \par \uc2 We refuse to live in an oligarchy. We refuse to accept a society in which so few have so much and so many have so little. Brothers and sisters, enough is enough!\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI read a lot in the media about how a strike is going to be bad for the economy. Well let me tell you something about the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you have auto workers who cannot afford to buy the cars, that is bad for the economy.\par \par \uc2 When you have auto workers who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to take out a mortgage to buy a modest home, that is bad for the economy.\par \par \uc2 When you have auto workers who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford childcare or to save up to send their kids to college, that is bad for the economy.\par \par \uc2 When you have auto workers who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford prescription drugs, can\u8217\'20\'19t afford healthcare, that is bad for the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not accept that over the last 20 years, the average wage for American auto workers has decreased by 30% after adjusting for inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re wanting to know why you\u8217\'20\'19re out on strike right now, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reason,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders also addressed Ford CEO \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  , saying:\par \par \uc2 Mr Farley, last year, you made nearly $21m in total compensation and my guess is that when you retire from your job, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a great compensation \u8230\'20\'26 and all kinds of benefits.\par \par \uc2 Do you have any clue as to what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to be a worker getting older, having worked your entire life and not having any money in the bank as you prepare for retirement?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders also addressed the CEO of \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2  , saying:\par \par \uc2 Do you know, Mr Tavares, what it is like to be classified as a temp and despite working year after year, you\u8217\'20\'19ll remain a temp, receiving wages and benefits significantly lower than your brothers and sisters doing the same exact work?\par \par \uc2 Mr Tavares, do you have any clue what that is about?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you have any clue clue what it\u8217\'20\'19s like for one of your workers to try and survive on $17 an hour, which is the average starting wage of an automobile worker?\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said in his remarks, addressing \uc2 General Motors\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you know, Miss Barra, what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to try and raise a family, put food on the table and pay rent when you\u8217\'20\'19re making $20 bucks an hour?\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last 50 years, there has been a massive redistribution of wealth. The problem is it\u8217\'20\'19s gone in the wrong direction,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of going from the top down to the bottom, it\u8217\'20\'19s going from the bottom up to the top \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19re going to reverse that trend,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the ruling class of this country wants a redistribution of wealth, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to give it to them,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders at \uc2 UAW\uc2  rally: 'The average American worker today is worse off than he or she was 50 years ago'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite record breaking corporate profits, despite corporate America spending hundreds of billions on dividends and stock buybacks, the average American worker today is worse off than he or she was 50 years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBrothers and sisters, that is exactly what this strike is all about,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders has taken the stage in Detroit where he is addressing \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers currently on strike against auto companies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight that you are waging here is not only about decent wages, decent benefits and decent working conditions in the automobile industry.\par \par \uc2 It is a fight to take on corporate greed and tell the people on top this country belongs to all of us, not just a few,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  also made an appearance at the rally during which she addressed the crowd of \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers, telling them:\par \par \uc2 We all want the same thing \u8230\'20\'26 our chance at a good life, a fair shot. We all want to be able to make it in Michigan, for us and our families and we are all on team Michigan.\par \par \uc2 We will continue to fight to ensure that every worker is treated with dignity and respect and that Michigan continues to lead the world. I am here with you my brothers and sisters from the \uc2 UAW\uc2  . I love you. I respect you and I stand with you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state made an appearance at the rally and pledged her support to \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers at the rally, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand with you. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to win. No matter how long it takes, no matter how long we need to stand together, we will lock arms and say, \u8216\'20\'18Solidarity wins.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  members to hold rally at Ford site in Detroit, with Bernie Sanders set to appear\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  members are set to host a rally at the UAW-Ford National Programs Center in Detroit at 5pm ET where Vermont senator and vocal union supporter Bernie Sanders is set to make an appearance.\par \par \uc2 We will have a live feed of the rally and will bring you the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 enltrUAW members, supporters and media gather for the Stand Up Rally at the UAW-Ford National Programs Center in Detroit. If you're in the area, join us and wear red if possible!\par \par \uc2 Program starts at 5 PM ET {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1PtpaRjzhz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1PtpaRjzhz }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1702780005506253291?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@UAW)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator JD Vance of Ohio has issued a letter to White House advisor Gene Sperling who president Joe Biden dispatched to Detroit as part of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s liaising efforts in the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Vance, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vance.senate.gov/press-releases/senator-vance-bidens-forced-transition-to-electric-vehicles-is-crushing-uaw-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  in a separate press statement that he supports the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s demands for higher wages, told Sperling that his involvement \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserves further scrutiny\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vance.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/UAW-Strike-Letter-9.15.23.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused }}}\uc2  Sperling of seeking political gain by steering the strikes in traditionally Republican states, saying:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s planned strikes have targeted just three plants, including two in the deeply Republican states of Ohio and Missouri. Only one strike affects Michigan, where the bulk of \uc2 UAW\uc2  members live and work. This pattern seems hardly coincidental.\par \par \uc2 A major, multi-plant strike in Michigan could be costly to one of the president\u8217\'20\'19s closest gubernatorial allies. It might create economic reverberations across a state that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won in 2016. Perhaps these are mere coincidences, but your involvement supplies a different explanation and raises questions about the work President Biden enlisted you to do.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear whether your purpose was to facilitate negotiations and avert a strike or to shield President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies from scrutiny and protect his and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 political fortunes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to accuse Sperling of exploiting the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UAW\uc2  to protect your boss at the expense of American workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats throw their support behind striking auto workers\par \par \uc2 Other politicians that are voicing their support for \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers include Massachus etts\u8217\'20\'19s senator Elizabeth Warren, representative Ayanna Pressley and New Jersey senator Cory Booker.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Warren wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C@Ford, @GM and @\uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have raked in record profits for years. I stand in solidarity with @UAW workers striking for wages and benefits that reflect the work they do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ford?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Ford }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GM?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GM }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Stellantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Stellantis }}}\uc2  have raked in record profits for years. I stand in solidarity with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UAW }}}\uc2  workers striking for wages and benefits that reflect the work they do.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1702703912002691145?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Pressley said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COrganized power is realized power & our movement for workers\u8217\'20\'19 justice is stronger than ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSolidarity with our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UAW }}}\uc2  siblings as they strike for a fair & just contract.\par \par \uc2 Organized power is realized power & our movement for workers\u8217\'20\'19 justice is stronger than ever. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yW0W3EOLbh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yW0W3EOLbh }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ayanna Pressley (@AyannaPressley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AyannaPressley/status/1702747531275542791?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 Booker, who said that his grandfather used to work on an assembly line in Detroit, said that he is confident that \uc2 UAW\uc2  will achieve a deal with auto companies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy grandfather worked on an assembly line in Detroit, and fought for his fellow workers as a \uc2 UAW union\uc2  rep. He would be proud of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  members striking today. I stand with them & am confident they will achieve a deal that lifts up workers, their families, and their communities,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy grandfather worked on an assembly line in Detroit, and fought for his fellow workers as a \uc2 UAW union\uc2  rep. He would be proud of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  members striking today. I stand with them & am confident they will achieve a deal that lifts up workers, their families, and their communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cory Booker (@CoryBooker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoryBooker/status/1702706277149733092?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  chief Shawn Fain hit back at Ford CEO\u8217\'20\'19s claim that \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s demands would bankrupt the company.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Fain called Ford CEO \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments \u8220\'20\'1Ca joke\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 They could double our wages and they could not raise the price of vehicles and they would still make billions of dollars. It\u8217\'20\'19s a lie like everything else that comes out of their mouth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThey could double our wages and they could not raise the price of vehicles and they would still make billions of dollars. It's a lie like everything else that comes out of their mouth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  chief Shawn Fain on Ford CEO's claim that \uc2 UAW\uc2  's demands would bankrupt the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iLm6I0TppL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iLm6I0TppL }}}\uc2 's demands would bankrupt the company\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1702700068959035734?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  , Democratic congresswoman from Michigan, backs striking workers\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  , a Democratic representative of Michigan, has also thrown her support behind \uc2 UAW\uc2  auto workers, many of whom are striking in her state.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Friday, Tlaib wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers are asking to be valued. They shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to beg BCBS MI. They are making billions and shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t leave their workers struggling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJoin Joshua (just 2 years old!) and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UAW }}}\uc2  workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BCBSM?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BCBSM }}}\uc2  who are on strike to address the extreme outsourcing and pay inequity.\par \par \uc2 Workers are asking to be valued. They shouldn't have to beg BCBS MI. They are making billions and shouldn't leave their workers struggling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8KWGTbwNnd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8KWGTbwNnd }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  (@RashidaTlaib) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RashidaTlaib/status/1702694686870184141?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@RashidaTlaib)\par \par \uc2 In an earlier message to Congress, Tlaib said, \u8220\'20\'1CThey have record profits and that should result in record contracts\u8221\'20\'1D and urged for stronger contracts for auto workers.\par \par \uc2 enltrComrade congresswoman and Detroit DSA member {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RashidaTlaib?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RashidaTlaib }}}\uc2  stands with autoworkers and the entire working class! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/standupUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #standupUAW }}}\uc2  stands with autoworkers and the entire working class! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AO6x2GvxEu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/AO6x2GvxEu }}}\uc2  stands with autoworkers and the entire working class!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Detroit DSA ?? (@detroitdsa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/detroitdsa/status/1702362216823963950?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an essay that Senator Bernie Sanders wrote for the Guardian about why Americans should support the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , prior to Friday\u8217\'20\'19s strike declaration.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  members will be fighting not only for themselves but against a corporate culture of arrogance, cruelty and selfishness causing massive and unnecessary pain for the majority of working families throughout the country. Their fight against corporate greed is our fight. Their victory will resonate all across the economy, impact millions of workers from coast to coast and help create a more just and equitable economy.\par \par \uc2 What are some of the issues that are pushing \uc2 UAW\uc2  members to strike? At the top of the list is the extraordinary level of corporate greed shown by industry leaders.\par \par \uc2 In the first half of 2023 the big three automakers made a combined $21bn in profits \u8211\'20\'13 up 80% from the same time period last year. Over the past decade, these same companies made some $250bn in profits in North America alone.\par \par \uc2 Yet last year, the big three spent $9bn \u8211\'20\'13 not to improve the lives of their workers, not to make their factories safer, but on stock buybacks and dividends to make their wealthy executives and stockholders even richer.\par \par \uc2 Read the full essay {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/sep/12/bernie-sanders-support-united-auto-workers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/sep/12/bernie-sanders-support-united-auto-workers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The United Auto Workers may soon strike. Every American should support them | Bernie Sanders }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  joins strikers in Toledo\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  showed up at the auto strikes outside the Toledo Jeep plant on Friday in a show of solidarity with the striking workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ratio of CEO pay to average worker pay in this plant is 365 to 1, and they\u8217\'20\'19re telling workers to keep making these concessions?\u8221\'20\'1D Brown told reporters.\par \par \uc2 enltr"The ratio of CEO pay to average worker pay in this plant is 365 to 1, and they're telling workers to keep making these concessions?"\u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSherrodBrown?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSherrodBrown }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FI3WE1xv0o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FI3WE1xv0o }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1702732858211607025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@UAW)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care what they\u8217\'20\'19re paid, as long as workers here are paid well. \u8221\'20\'1D Brown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wtol.com/video/life/automotive/jeep/us-sen-sherrod-browns-visits-with-striking-jeep-workers-friday/512-9216bc94-a7e1-4715-8a7f-84c21de19566"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said, }}}\uc2  referring to the auto companies\u8217\'20\'19 CEOs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCEOs make that kind of money, 20 or 30 million a year, but you know, they\u8217\'20\'19re making that kind of money and not only won\u8217\'20\'19t settle \u8211\'20\'13 I know negotiations are tough \u8211\'20\'13 but they won\u8217\'20\'19t even offer a serious legitimate proposal for a contract to this union,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders says workers' 'fight for a just economy is our fight'\par \par \uc2 Vermont senator Bernie Sanders has voiced his support for the striking auto workers across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stand with courageous @UAW workers as they go out on strike. Their fight for a just economy is our fight. Solidarity forever,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders tweeted on Friday.\par \par \uc2 enltrI stand with courageous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UAW }}}\uc2  workers as they go out on strike. Their fight for a just economy is our fight. Solidarity forever. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K5bjOrgIph"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/K5bjOrgIph }}}\uc2  workers as they go out on strike. Their fight for a just economy is our fight. Solidarity forever.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@BernieSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders/status/1702666628658291157?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI really applaud the courage of Shawn Fain and the workers of at the \uc2 UAW\uc2  for standing up and saying, \u8216\'20\'18You know what? Enough is enough.\u8217\'20\'19 We need an economy that works for everybody. Not just the people on top,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders added.\par \par \uc2 Sanders is set to appear at a rally alongside \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain at the UAW-Ford National Programs Center in Detroit this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ford CEO stops briefly to meet with picketers outside Michigan plant\par \par \uc2 Ford CEO \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  briefly stopped by to meet with picketers outside the Wayne, Michigan plant.\par \par \uc2 Several workers near retirement weren\u8217\'20\'19t particularly impressed by the gesture. He makes $29m a year, they noted, while hourly workers are \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting to get money to survive after we leave here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many years do we even have left to live after we retire? 10 years?\u8221\'20\'1D asked worker Stu Jackson, who highlighted the toll factory work exacts on workers\u8217\'20\'19 bodies and health.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  gave up major concessions during the 2009 recession, but executives like Farley have yet to repay the union now that the industry is once again booming, said Terrance Pope.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey forgot about us and it is time for them to give back,\u8221\'20\'1D Pope added.\par \par \uc2 Until that happens, Farley\u8217\'20\'19s presence is meaningless and perhaps insulting, they said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid you see Farley in his tailored European suit? Wasn\u8217\'20\'19t he sharp?\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson asked. \u8220\'20\'1CHe looks like the $29m dollar man. Those nice shoes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd look at us,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson added indignantly, motioning to the small group dressed in jeans, t-shirts and sweatpants. \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t fair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The responses among picketers to Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments on the strike and plans to travel to Detroit to help negotiate a deal varied.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s on our side because he needs the \uc2 UAW\uc2  support when the election comes \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why he\u8217\'20\'19s on our side,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stu Jackson, who is nearing retirement. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he says he\u8217\'20\'19s a union man, so we\u8217\'20\'19re going to give him a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need him to come and tell us what\u8217\'20\'19s good for us because we already know what we need, but he probably needs to talk with the CEOs and get them to cooperate and give us what we\u8217\'20\'19re entitled to,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden already gave them a bunch of money for those battery plants, so now he\u8217\'20\'19s got to take care of us and go to bat for us,\u8221\'20\'1D added Reggie Kirkland, who said he is striking to protect his retirement.\par \par \uc2 Yvette Lenardo, who joined the picket even though she works at a nearby plant, said she was unsure whether the president has the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s back. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is supposed to be with us, but is he?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked, adding that she needs to hear more about his position on the strike.\par \par \uc2 Another worker simply guffawed when asked if the president supported the union. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s all I have to say,\u8221\'20\'1D he said as he composed himself.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images coming through the newswires on the auto strikes in Michigan:\par \par \uc2 Members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  (\uc2 UAW\uc2  ) gather in front of the Ford Michigan Assembly Plant during the first day of a strike called in response to failed contract negotiations with the Big Three automakers - \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , Ford, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , the parent company of \uc2 Jeep\uc2  and Chrysler - in Detroit, Michigan, USA, 15 September 2023. Photograph: Dieu-Nali Chery/\uc2 EPA\uc2  Members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  (\uc2 UAW\uc2  ) gather in front of the Ford Michigan Assembly Plant during the first day of a strike called in response to failed contract negotiations with the Big Three automakers - \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , Ford, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , the parent company of \uc2 Jeep\uc2  and Chrysler - in Detroit, Michigan, USA, 15 September 2023. Photograph: Dieu-Nali Chery/\uc2 EPA\uc2  Members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  (\uc2 UAW\uc2  ) gather in front of the Ford Michigan Assembly Plant during the first day of a strike called in response to failed contract negotiations with the Big Three automakers - \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , Ford, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , the parent company of \uc2 Jeep\uc2  and Chrysler - in Detroit, Michigan, USA, 15 September 2023. Photograph: Dieu-Nali Chery/EPA UAW (\uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  ) president Shawn Fain speaks with members of the media and members of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  outside of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 900 headquarters across the street from the Ford Assembly Plant in Wayne, Michigan on September 15, 2023. Photograph: Matthew Hatcher/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\uc2  Members of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  (\uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  ) picket and hold signs outside of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 900 headquarters across the street from the Ford Assembly Plant in Wayne, Michigan on September 15, 2023. Photograph: Matthew Hatcher/AFP/Getty Images Local 900 headquarters across the street from the Ford Assembly Plant in Wayne, Michigan on September 15, 2023. Photograph: Matthew Hatcher/AFP/\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Tom Perkins\u8217\'20\'19 report from outside Ford\u8217\'20\'19s plant in Wayne, Michigan where striking workers are voicing their concerns:\par \par \uc2 Mike Duneske is a 29-year plant veteran who says he is picketing outside the sprawling plant, which employs 2,800 hourly workers, for the \u8220\'20\'1Cyounger generation that isn\u8217\'20\'19t earning enough money to make it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When he started in 1994, his wage was $12.56 an hour, equal to nearly $26 an hour when adjusted for inflation in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Workers start at about $16 an hour at Michigan Assembly, and that\u8217\'20\'19s generating a huge amount of turnover.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a turnstile in there, they can\u8217\'20\'19t keep anyone working in the plant,\u8221\'20\'1D Duneske added.\par \par \uc2 When asked why the \uc2 UAW\uc2  was forced to strike, Duneske responded, \u8220\'20\'1CTwo words: corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  's \uc2 Twitter\uc2  verification stripped amid strikes\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account was stripped of its blue verification check shortly after the the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikes began, a \uc2 UAW\uc2  official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/09/15/uaw-strike-twitter-verification-elon-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  the Intercept.\par \par \uc2 According to the official, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s verified account, which the union paid for, was verified until Friday morning when the blue verification check was no longer there.\par \par \uc2 A screenshot of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account showed the missing blue icon next to \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  handle.\par \par \uc2 enltrElon put the blue check back up. Maybe the Big Three will fold this fast too. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tnHY6Zzomd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tnHY6Zzomd }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan Grim (@ryangrim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryangrim/status/1702721056190980574?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 The Intercept reports that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s blue check was restored once again after its initial story of the removed verification began circulating online.\par \par \uc2 As of Friday afternoon, the verification icon can be seen alongside the union\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handle }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClass solidarity among the nation\u8217\'20\'19s elite has long been a feature of the American political economy, and the move by Musk, the richest man on the planet, is in line with that sense of allegiance, even as he promotes himself as a populist friend of the working man,\u8221\'20\'1D the Intercept reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMusk is also the owner of a non-union automaker, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  . Wage increases won by union workers often trickle down, so to speak, to non-union workers, requiring even bosses like Musk to pay workers more from his share of profits. That gives Musk a direct financial incentive to help break the strike, even beyond whatever ideological affinity he may have with the capitalist class,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 Musk, a vocal opponent of unions, previously dared the \uc2 UAW\uc2  to try and unionize \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 Last March, the billionaire CEO tweeted, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d like hereby to invite \uc2 UAW\uc2  to hold a union vote at their convenience. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  will do nothing to stop them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOur real challenge is Bay Area has negative unemployment, so if we don\u8217\'20\'19t treat and compensate our (awesome) people well, they have many other offers and will just leave!\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d like hereby to invite \uc2 UAW\uc2  to hold a union vote at their convenience. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  will do nothing to stop them.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1499249339671089152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 3, 2022 }}}\uc2  (@elonmusk)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Companies should go 'further' in strike negotiations\par \par \uc2 In brief remarks on Wednesday, Joe Biden said that auto companies should \u8220\'20\'1Cgo further\u8221\'20\'1D in their negotiations with striking workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe companies have made some significant offers. But I believe that should go further to ensure record corporate profits mean record contracts,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRecord corporate profits, which they have, should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden reiterated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust as we\u8217\'20\'19re building an economy of the future, we need labor agreements for future,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/05/joe-biden-labor-day-speech-wisconsin-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared }}}\uc2  himself as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-union president,\u8221\'20\'1D said during his remarks that \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong unions are critical to growing the economy and growing from the middle out, bottom up, not the top down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that transition should be fair and a win-win for auto workers and auto companies. But I also believe contract agreements must lead to a vibrant\u8230\'20\'26America\u8230\'20\'26that promotes good strong middle class jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden also announced that he is dispatching deputy labor secretary Julie Su and White House senior advisor Gene Sperling to Detroit as part of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s effort to continue its \u8220\'20\'1Cactive engagement\u8221\'20\'1D in the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden said that in efforts to continue the White House\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cactive engagement,\u8221\'20\'1D he is dispatching two members of his team to Detroit which include deputy labor secretary Julie Su and White House senior advisor Gene Sperling.\par \par \uc2 Biden said that both Su and Sperling \u8220\'20\'1Coffer their full support for the parties in reaching a contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is that autoworkers help create America\u8217\'20\'19s middle class. They deserve a contract that sustains them in the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'Record corporate profits... should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  '\par \par \uc2 Biden appeared to support the strikers in strong comments made during his White House address:\par \par \uc2 The president said: \u8220\'20\'1CRecord corporate profits... should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also expressed regret that the strike had not been averted but urged both parties to return to the negotiating table:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one wants a strike but I respect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to use their options under the collective bargaining system and understand their frustrations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do appreciate that the parties have been working around the clock \u8230\'20\'26 It is my hope that the parties can return to the negotiating table to forge a win-win agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has started speaking.\par \par \uc2 We will bring you the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Joe Biden to deliver remarks on the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikes, here is what industry experts and lawmakers are saying about the strikes, Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Arthur Wheaton, director of labor studies at the Cornell School of Industrial and Labor Relations says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a devastating hit to the communities. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a devastating hit for the strike fund. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a devastating hit on the balance sheet for any of the automakers but it starts to raise the stakes, which was the intent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think they are making progress at the table... the initial (automaker) offers were much lower, like 9% (wage) increases and now you\u8217\'20\'19re up to 20% for increases. So that\u8217\'20\'19s more than double. You\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the \uc2 UAW\uc2  come down. You\u8217\'20\'19re no longer hearing anything about the 32-hour work week from the \uc2 UAW\uc2  ,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Sam Fiorani\uc2  , a production forecaster at Auto Forecast Solutions says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is more of a symbolic strike than an actual damaging one... If the negotiations don\u8217\'20\'19t go in a direction that [\uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn] Fain thinks is positive, we can fully expect a larger strike coming in a week or two.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dan Ives\uc2 , an analyst at Wedbush believes a potentially prolonged strike may be good news for electronic vehicle manufacturer \uc2 Tesla\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the strike lasts longer than three to four weeks, it will be moderately detrimental to \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford\u8217\'20\'19s EV strategy in 2024... While the Detroit stalwarts battle with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , there\u8217\'20\'19s a bottle of champagne that\u8217\'20\'19s being iced at \uc2 Tesla\uc2  headquarters,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Elissa Slotkin, a Democratic representative from Michigan voiced her support towards the strikes, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to joining our auto workers on the picket line this weekend. For the sake of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s economy and our working families, I hope this strike is short-lived... I hope the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and the Big Three continue to negotiate in good faith to reach a fair agreement as quickly as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 While we wait for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike, here\u8217\'20\'19s more on picketing happening at one auto plant from Tom Perkins for the Guardian, reporting from Wayne, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Under blue skies in Wayne, Michigan, a half hour outside Detroit, the mood is festive but defiant as hundreds of autoworkers picket at the entrances to the Ford\u8217\'20\'19s Michigan Assembly Plant, which produces the Ranger and Bronco.\par \par \uc2 A chorus of horns blares in support from Michigan Avenue, a busy highway running through the nation\u8217\'20\'19s automotive heartland. Strikers here turned away semi-truck after semi-truck trying to deliver parts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHell no you\u8217\'20\'19re not coming in here, keep it moving,\u8221\'20\'1D a worker yelled.\par \par \uc2 The strikers\u8217\'20\'19 message: they\u8217\'20\'19re no longer accepting the automakers\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Ccorporate greed\u8221\'20\'1D. They point to the companies\u8217\'20\'19 record profits in recent years and massive stock buyback programs that are enacted as workers struggle to make ends meet.\par \par \uc2 Domonique Hicks, a young mother of three who lives in Detroit, said the $16.67 an hour wage is not feeding her children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to take back what Ford took from us,\u8221\'20\'1D Hicks said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to bargain with us so we\u8217\'20\'19re making a statement \u8211\'20\'13 if you can make millions and billions, then we deserve something. We build those cars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike will go on for as long as Ford \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to keep their checkbook in their pocket,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikers picket outside an auto-plant in Wayne, Michigan. Photograph: Tom Perkins/The Guardian\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to begin speaking shortly on auto worker strike\par \par \uc2 Biden will soon give remarks about the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Biden will make his remarks on the strike from the White House\u8217\'20\'19s Roosevelt room, which were originally scheduled for 11.30 am ET.\par \par \uc2 A live stream of the speech will be available on this blog.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for coming updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden aides will travel to Detroit to help with \uc2 UAW\uc2  contract negotiations, WSJ reports\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to send aide Gene Sperling and acting labor secretary Julie Su to Detroit given the auto strike, the Wall Street Journal reports.\par \par \uc2 Sperling and Su are expected to help aid in negotiations between \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers and auto manufacturers, as workers began a historic strike on Friday at midnight, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/autos/uaw-strikes-gm-ford-stellantis-plants-69b04c95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  WSJ reported }}}\uc2  citing two people familiar with the plan.\par \par \uc2 Per the WSJ:\par \par \uc2 Sperling and Su, who have been in daily touch with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and auto companies in recent weeks, won\u8217\'20\'19t be directly involved in the negotiations or playing the role of a mediator, the people said.\par \par \uc2 The trip comes as Biden is expected to give remarks on Friday about the strike from the White House, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  have aligned their wage increase demands of 40% to the similar salary increases the CEOs at Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have seen in recent years.\par \par \uc2 CEO pay at the big three {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased 40%  }}}\uc2  from 2013 to 2022, while US auto worker hourly wages have fallen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 19.3% }}}\uc2  since 2008 with inflation taken into account.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asyousow.org/press-releases/uaw-strike-ceo-pay-risk-companies-shareholders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data  }}}\uc2  compiled by the non profit foundation As You Sow, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 CEO to median worker pay ratio is 362 to 1 and Ford\u8217\'20\'19s is 281 to 1. CEO pay at the big three automakers in the US is substantially higher compared to CEO pay of foreign automakers, including ones with much higher revenues.\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  reported 2022 revenue at $295.7bn and paid their CEO $9.1m, \uc2 Toyota\uc2  reported a revenue of $256.6bn with their CEO pay at $5m, \uc2 Daimler\uc2  (\uc2 Mercedes Benz\uc2  ) reported 2022 revenue at $158.3bn with CEO pay at $3.17m, and Honda reported a revenue of $124.2bn with CEO pay at $1.48m.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, Ford\u8217\'20\'19s revenue in 2022 was $136.3bn, with CEO pay at $22.8m and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 revenue was $127bn with CEO pay at $29.1m. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 revenue was $127bn with CEO pay at $29.1m. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/business/autos/chrysler/2023/02/22/stellantis-full-year-2022-earnings-profit-share/69927399007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  a 2022 revenue of $191.4bn in 2022 with CEO pay at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/chrysler/2023/02/25/stellantis-ceo-carlos-tavares-2022-compensation-sec-mike-manley/69942226007/#:~:text=Stellantis%20CEO%20Carlos%20Tavares%20had,Exchange%20Commission%20filing%20Friday%20evening."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $24.8m }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UAW\uc2  members see the CEO pay disparity as a measurement of how they are undervalued. Skyrocketing CEO pay is linked to worker dissatisfaction and lower profits, making excessive pay a distinct material risk that shareholders must take seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rosanna Landis Weaver, director of wage justice and executive compensation at As You Sow, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asyousow.org/press-releases/uaw-strike-ceo-pay-risk-companies-shareholders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  CEO hits back at strikers for rejecting 'most significant offer' in 115 years\par \par \uc2 The CEO of \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  , has come out with fighting words over the start of the auto workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike, saying she is \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely frustrated and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D that industrial action has begun and warning that the walkout would harm employees, their families and the economy.\par \par \uc2 Speaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SquawkCNBC/status/1702645886797414898"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to CNBC }}}\uc2 , Barra, who has headed \uc2 GM\uc2  since 2014, called the concessions being offered by the Detroit three carmakers targetted by the strike \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D. They amounted to over 20% wage increases, she said, on top of job security and \u8220\'20\'1Cworld-class health care\u8221\'20\'1D which combined was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant offer we\u8217\'20\'19ve had in our 115-year history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Se added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Some 3,600 \uc2 GM\uc2  workers belonging to the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  walked out of the carmaker\u8217\'20\'19s Wentzville, Missouri plant at midnight on Thursday, part of the total of 12,700 who are out across three plants in the first stage of the strike. The Wentzville plant builds the Chevrolet Colorado and GMC Canyon midsize trucks as well as cargo vans, which are among \uc2 GM\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s most popular models.\par \par \uc2 Sounding a gloomy note, Barra told CNBC that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is not going to be positive from an industry perspective or for \uc2 GM\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. She said that she thought the strike could be resolved quickly, but warned that its impact could be felt immediately, with painful consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get there fast because this is not good for our employees, for the communities and their families. For every \uc2 GM\uc2  job there are six other jobs in the economy that depend on us running, so we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get back to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  have shared images and videos coming from Friday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of a strike at three major auto-plants.\par \par \uc2 Autoworkers chanted, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the union! Mighty, mighty union,\u8221\'20\'1D while holding \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike signs, as seen in a video {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1702536708825231584"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared by UAW on X }}}\uc2 , formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 enltr"WE ARE THE UNION! MIGHTY MIGHTY UNION! ALL THE WORKERS UNION! ASS-KICKING UNION!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SolidaritySeason?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SolidaritySeason }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Local900?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Local900 }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eWUIjXYYRb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eWUIjXYYRb }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1702536708825231584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@UAW)\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  member Eric Heggie shared video of workers leaving the Jeep Toledo Assembly Complex plant in Ohio as Friday\u8217\'20\'19s strike began.\par \par \uc2 enltrTOLEDO IS STANDING UP!!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZezD933Y1O"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZezD933Y1O }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eric Heggie (@EricHeggie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricHeggie/status/1702533915536203817?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain previously wrote about autoworkers deserving a wage increase as automakers receive record profits. Fain detailed how an increase in manufacturing electric vehicles should also include an increase in workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages.\par \par \uc2 Read his essay for the Guardian, written with California congressman Ro Khanna.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26[Here] we are in the 11th hour of \uc2 UAW\uc2  -big three negotiations, and corporate greed stands as the barrier preventing movement and a fair and good contract for autoworkers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/ford"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ford }}}\uc2 , \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have made a quarter trillion dollars over the last 10 years. Those profits, and the very existence of the big three today, were only possible through the sacrifices made by \uc2 UAW\uc2  members when American taxpayers bailed out the industry. Those same workers were never made whole after being forced to accept lower wages and were stripped of cost-of-living adjustments and retiree pensions.\par \par \uc2 Over the last four years, each big three CEO received on average a 40% pay raise on top of their multimillion-dollar salaries. Autoworkers saw their pay increase by a mere 6% in that same period of time, falling behind in inflation like the rest of American workers.\par \par \uc2 Since 2003, the big three have closed 65 auto plants. Plant closures ruin lives, rip apart families and wreck entire communities . For too long, the auto companies have treated these plants and workers as disposable for their bottom line. If allowed, they will continue to leave entire towns and communities behind.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s also at stake in these contract negotiations is the very future of the auto industry itself \u8211\'20\'13 and workers\u8217\'20\'19 place in it. The electric vehicle transition must be as much about workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights as it is about fighting the climate crisis. We will not let the EV industry be built on the backs of workers making poverty wages while CEOs line their pockets with government subsidies. There is no good reason why EV manufacturing can\u8217\'20\'19t be the gateway to the middle class. But the early signs of this industry are worrying. We will not let corporate greed manipulate the transition to a green economy into a roll back of economic justice.\par \par \uc2 Read the essay {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/sep/14/record-auto-profits-inequality-climate-crisis-ford-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/sep/14/record-auto-profits-inequality-climate-crisis-ford-general-motors-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Record auto profits should be used to address inequality and climate crisis | Shawn Fain and Ro Khanna  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Explained: Why is strike happening?\par \par \uc2 The latest \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike is the largest auto strike to happen in decades. But why is it happening now?\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an explainer from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Michael Sainato.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Why is it happening?\par \par \uc2 The union argues that autoworkers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/21/uaw-big-three-automakers-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never been fully compensated }}}\uc2  for the sacrifices they made after the 2008-09 financial crisis when they agreed to a raft of cuts to save the industry. The automakers received huge bailouts and soon returned to record profits.\par \par \uc2 Workers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/21/uaw-big-three-automakers-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing }}}\uc2  for at least a 40% wage increase over four years in a new contract, an end to two-tier wage systems in which new hires are paid significantly less for doing the same work, an increase to benefits for retirees and return of a defined pension instead of a 401k, reinstatement of cost of living adjustment raises, a 32-hour workweek, job security protections and protections for workers affected by plant closures.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, was elected to head the union as part of a reform campaign within its ranks, aimed particularly at taking a more aggressive approach toward bargaining with automakers after workers had taken concessions amid auto bankruptcies during the 2008 economic recession and have yet to regain those concessions and share in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox2detroit.com/news/uaw-rejects-offer-by-ford-files-unfair-labor-practice-against-gm-stellantis#:~:text=%22What%27s%20driving%20members%27%20expectations%20are,aiming%20low%20and%20settling%20lower.%22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quarter of a trillion dollars }}}\uc2  in profit the big three automakers have made in the last decade.\par \par \uc2 How did the strike begin?\par \par \uc2 In late August, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , which represents the workers at the big three automakers in the US, announced membership voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/08/25/uaw-strike-authorization-vote-passes/70658043007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 97% }}}\uc2  in favor of the strike authorization. The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/08/business/economy/uaw-autos-gm-stellantis-ford.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never gone }}}\uc2  on strike at the big three automakers simultaneously\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/13/uaw-strike-explainer-ford-stellantis-gm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/13/uaw-strike-explainer-ford-stellantis-gm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Biggest auto strike in generations\u8217\'20\'19 is here \u8211\'20\'13 but why is it happening? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 13,000 auto workers on strike\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 About 13,000 members of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/15/auto-workers-strike-ford-gm-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/15/auto-workers-strike-ford-gm-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  began striking on Friday }}}\uc2  at 12.00am ET after automakers failed to negotiate a new contract to meet worker demands.\par \par \uc2 The amount of workers on strike is only a fraction of the 150,000 total members of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , but \uc2 UAW\uc2  officials say the strike could expand if negotiation talks continue to fail.\par \par \uc2 The strike is the first one in the 88-year history of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  , after negotiations around wage increases, pension, and other union demands broke down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we need to go all out, we will,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain said, adding that company-wide strikes are not off the table if new contracts cannot be negotiated, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/detroit/news/uaw-president-shawn-fain-provides-update-on-contract-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the historic picket:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  told CNBC on Friday that she was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely frustrated and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D by the walkout, adding that the company was ready to keep negotiations open.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The automakers on strike come from three major Midwest-based plants owned by \uc2 General Motors\uc2  , Ford, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  , the parent company of Chrysler.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden will speak on the strike later today. Biden spoke with Fain and autoworkers before the strike deadline, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-09-14/biden-speaks-with-uaw-president-auto-executives-as-strike-looms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230915ej9f001uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
