\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Biden says record profits warrant record contracts as historic auto worker strike starts\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and Maya Yang \par \uc2 1,055 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par 20:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  unable to agree deal with Ford, \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , who have seen profits and executive pay soar\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden on Friday spoke out in support of auto workers as they launched a historic series of strikes after their union failed to reach an agreement with the US\u8217\'20\'19s three largest vehicle manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one wants a strike, but I respect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to use their options under the collective bargaining system, and [I] understand their frustrations,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said in a brief, unscheduled appearance at the White House.\par \par \uc2 The disagreement over a new contract saw workers at select plants called out from the shop floor to the picket lines shortly after midnight on Friday, kicking off the most ambitious industrial labor action in decades.\par \par \uc2 The deadline for talks between Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 expired at two minutes to midnight on Thursday, with the sides still far apart on the union\u8217\'20\'19s new contract priorities.\par \par \uc2 The strike \u8211\'20\'13 which marks the first time all three of the Detroit carmakers have been targeted by strikes at the same time \u8211\'20\'13 is being coordinated by the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain. He said he intended to launch a series of limited and targeted \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1702083943174897746"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 standup}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D strikes to shut individual auto plants around the US.\par \par \uc2 The first walkouts were at a \uc2 General Motors\uc2  plant in Wentzville, Missouri, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant in Toledo, Ohio, and a Ford assembly plant in Wayne, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 They involve a combined 12,700 workers at the plants, which are critical to the production of some of the Detroit Three\u8217\'20\'19s most profitable vehicles including the Ford Bronco, the Jeep Wrangler and the Chevrolet Colorado.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our defining moment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/uaw.union/videos/1047762633322736/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live stream}}}\uc2  on Thursday night, less than two hours before the strike was set to begin.\par \par \uc2 Fain did not rule out broadening the strikes beyond the initial three targets. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf we need to go all out, we will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, who had repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/05/joe-biden-labor-day-speech-wisconsin-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared that}}}\uc2  he takes pride {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in being}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-union president\u8221\'20\'1D in US history, urged the corporations to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo further\u8221\'20\'1D, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CRecord corporate profits... should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI do appreciate that the parties have been working around the clock \u8230\'20\'26 It is my hope that the parties can return to the negotiating table to forge a win-win agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president also on Friday dispatched two of his top aides to Detroit to help try to resolve the dispute: the labor secretary, Julie Su, and senior adviser on economics Gene Sperling.\par \par \uc2 Fain later took issue with Biden saying in his brief speech at the White House that union-company negotiations \u8220\'20\'1Cbroke down\u8221\'20\'1D on Thursday night. Bargaining is now set to resume on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 chief executive, \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2 , said on Friday morning on CNBC she was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely frustrated and disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D and that the strike \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not be good for the economy overall\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She called for a deal to be made quickly and added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready to keep negotiations going.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has a $825m {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/strike-faq-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike fund }}}\uc2  that is set to compensate workers $500 a week while out on strike and could support all of its members for about three months.\par \par \uc2 Economists and politicians fear the damage resulting from a widespread, lengthy shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  has more than 90 days\u8217\'20\'19 worth of Jeeps in stock, and has been building SUVs and trucks on overtime, according to \uc2 Cox Automotive\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But a week-long shutdown at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jeep plant in Toledo could cut revenue by more than $380m, based on the company\u8217\'20\'19s financial reports.\par \par \uc2 Among union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-auto-bargaining/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands }}}\uc2  are: a 40% pay increase; an end to tiers, where some workers are paid at lower wage scales than others; the restoration of concessions from previous contracts such as medical benefits for retirees; more paid time off; and rights for workers affected by plant closures.\par \par \uc2 Workers have cited past concessions and the carmakers\u8217\'20\'19 immense profits in arguing in favor of their demands. The automakers\u8217\'20\'19 profits jumped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/?mc_cid=0adf49ae7e&mc_eid=131a3ffbe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 92%}}}\uc2  from 2013 to 2022, totaling $250bn. During this same time period, chief executive pay increased 40%, and nearly $66bn was paid out in stock dividends or stock buybacks to shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Barra, the highest-paid CEO of the Detroit big three, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/09/13/1198938942/high-ceo-pay-inequality-labor-union-uaw-workers#:~:text=General%20Motors%20CEO%20Mary%20Barra%2C%20the%20highest%2Dpaid%20chief%20executive,nearly%20%2429%20million%20in%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earned almost}}}\uc2  $22m last year.\par \par \uc2 Top pay for a \uc2 UAW\uc2  assembly-line worker based on the 2019 contract was $32 an hour. Workers now start at $18 and temporary workers receive $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 The industry is also set to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/04/17/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-announces-new-private-and-public-sector-investments-for-affordable-electric-vehicles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  receive}}}\uc2  record taxpayer incentives for transitioning to electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Despite these financial performances, hourly wages for workers have fallen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/?mc_cid=0adf49ae7e&mc_eid=131a3ffbe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 19.3%}}}\uc2 , with inflation taken into account, since 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/uaw-strike-looms-biden-admin-considers-aid-small-suppliers-source-2023-09-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  considering emergency aid for smaller supply firms to the automaker manufacturers due to the strike. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/detroit-three-strike-deadline-nears-sides-remain-far-apart-2023-09-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  to Fain on the status of negotiations on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Ford said the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest proposals would double its US labor costs. A walkout could mean that \uc2 UAW\uc2  profit-sharing checks for this year will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdecimated\u8221\'20\'1D, the company said.\par \par \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  declined to comment ahead of the midnight strike deadline.\par \par \uc2 In an earlier video, \uc2 GM\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top manufacturing executive, \uc2 Gerald Johnson\uc2 , said the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wage and benefits proposals would cost the automaker $100bn \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than twice the value of all of \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and absolutely impossible to absorb\u8221\'20\'1D. He did not detail how the union proposals would result in that cost, or over what time frame.\par \par \uc2 And in an appearance on CNBC on Thursday evening, Ford\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2 , said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no way we can be sustainable as a company\u8221\'20\'1D if it were to meet the union\u8217\'20\'19s wage demands.\par \par \uc2 Barra also said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/general-motors/2023/09/14/gms-barra-reveals-latest-record-offer-to-the-uaw-urges-deal/70854980007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter }}}\uc2  to employees: \u8220\'20\'1CRemember: we had a strike in 2019 and nobody won.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The contract fight has garnered significant support from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/analysis/uaw-strike-public-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public}}}\uc2  and US labor movement. Drivers represented by the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/09/14/uaw-strike-contract-negotiations-teamsters/70836748007/?utm_campaign=snd-autopilot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledged}}}\uc2  not to cross the picket line, halting deliveries of vehicles from the automakers throughout the strike. Several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/2023/9/13/service-solidarity-spotlight-are-you-all-uaw-members"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor unions}}}\uc2 , environmental, racial and social justice groups have publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.labor4sustainability.org/uaw-solidarity-letter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  support for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  in their fight for new contracts.\par \par \uc2 Reuters and\par \par \uc2 the Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230915ej9f000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
