\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Auto worker strike explained: the pay gap, the talks and what Biden is doing\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,150 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par 19:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Key questions answered after \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers at Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  walked off the job\par \par \uc2 Industrial action billed as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hoytOtuopyI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the biggest auto strike in generations}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D got under way late on Thursday night for 150,000 US autoworkers, with employees at Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  walking off the job at 11.59pm after contract negotiations failed to reach a deal.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the latest in a series of strikes called or threatened by workers in industries including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ups-teamsters-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shipping and logistics}}}\uc2 , TV and movie production and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/02/southern-california-hotel-workers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hotel and leisure}}}\uc2 . Given its scale, the strike could deal a significant blow to the US economy as well as the auto industry.\par \par \uc2 Why is it happening?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  says workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/21/uaw-big-three-automakers-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never been fully compensated}}}\uc2  for the sacrifices they made after the 2008-09 financial crisis, when they agreed to a raft of cuts to save the industry. The carmakers received huge bailouts and soon returned to record profits.\par \par \uc2 Workers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/21/uaw-big-three-automakers-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2  for at least a 40% wage increase over four years in a new contract; an end to two-tier wage systems in which new hires are paid significantly less for doing the same work; an increase to benefits for retirees and return of a defined pension instead of a 401k; reinstatement of cost-of-living adjustment raises; a 32-hour working week; job security protections; and protections for workers affected by plant closures.\par \par \uc2 How big is the pay gap?\par \par \uc2 The vast disparity in pay between workers and their bosses is one of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s biggest bones of contention.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  made $29m in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 362 times the median wage of $80,034 at the company.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ford CEO \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  made $21m in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 281 times the median worker of $74,691.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  CEO \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2  made $24.8m in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 365 times the average worker\u8217\'20\'19s $67,789 wage.\par \par \uc2 CEO pay at the big three companies jumped by 40% between 2013 and 2022. Meanwhile, auto manufacturing workers have seen their average real hourly earnings fall 19.3% since 2008, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/uaw-automakers-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economics Policy Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Starting wages at \uc2 GM\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ultium Cells\uc2  battery plant in \uc2 Lordstown\uc2 , Ohio, are just $16.50, according to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . Meaning it would take 16 years for a full-time worker to earn what Barra earns in a week.\par \par \uc2 Who\u8217\'20\'19s leading the charge?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, was elected to head the union as part of a reform campaign within its ranks, aimed at taking a more aggressive approach towards bargaining after workers had accepted concessions amid bankruptcies during the 2008 economic recession. Workers have yet to regain those concessions, or a share in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox2detroit.com/news/uaw-rejects-offer-by-ford-files-unfair-labor-practice-against-gm-stellantis#:~:text=%22What%27s%20driving%20members%27%20expectations%20are,aiming%20low%20and%20settling%20lower.%22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $250bn}}}\uc2  profits the big three automakers have raked in over the past decade.\par \par \uc2 How did the strike begin?\par \par \uc2 In late August, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  announced members voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/08/25/uaw-strike-authorization-vote-passes/70658043007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 97%}}}\uc2  in favor of the strike authorization. The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/08/business/economy/uaw-autos-gm-stellantis-ford.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never gone}}}\uc2  on strike at the big three automakers simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 A minute before midnight on Thursday, after their contracts expired, \uc2 UAW\uc2  members walked out at three assembly plants in Michigan, Missouri and Ohio. The union said that about 13,000 workers were affected.\par \par \uc2 The Detroit Free Press reported that the \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  complex in Toledo, Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/09/15/uaw-cant-reach-deal-with-gm-ford-stellantis-strikes-at-3-plants/70858771007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 erupted in cheering}}}\uc2  and honking of horns as the strike began.\par \par \uc2 When did the \uc2 UAW\uc2  last strike?\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 General Motors\uc2  last went on strike in 2019. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2023/09/04/uaw-president-shawn-fain-audacious-contract-demands-ford-gm-stellantis-46-pay-rise-32-hour-workweek/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lasted}}}\uc2  40 days and cost the carmaker $3.6bn. In 2019, contracts were reached with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/12/11/uaw-members-approves-deal-with-fiat-chrysler-ending-2019-negotiations.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fiat-Chrysler}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a35254008/fiat-chrysler-peugeot-become-stellantis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now Stellantis}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-ford-members-ratify-contract/#:~:text=UAW%20Ford%20members%20ratified%20the,of%20the%20UAW%20Ford%20Department."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ford}}}\uc2  without a strike occurring.\par \par \uc2 What happened to talks?\par \par \uc2 Talks are going on, \u8220\'20\'1Cin good faith\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  said on Friday morning. But management and workers failed to reach an agreement by the midnight deadline when current contracts expired and so the strike began. Fain has previously posted video updates on negotiations in which he has thrown copies of proposals from the automakers in the bin, criticizing the companies\u8217\'20\'19 offers.\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n5-h9fa2HH0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recent negotiation update}}}\uc2 , Fain criticized the counteroffers from Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 GM\uc2 , saying they keep in place two-tiered wages for workers; rejected their retirement and pension proposals; called wage proposals from Ford and \uc2 GM\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful and insulting\u8221\'20\'1D; and characterized \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s offer as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply inadequate\u8221\'20\'1D. The union has called for significant wage increases that reflect the salary increases of the companies\u8217\'20\'19 CEOs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make up for inflation, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make up for decades of falling wages and it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t reflect the massive profits we generated for this company,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain.\par \par \uc2 The automakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/08/business/economy/uaw-autos-gm-stellantis-ford.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  the union\u8217\'20\'19s proposals and claimed they are not \u8220\'20\'1Cfeasible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 How serious could it get?\par \par \uc2 In the first instance, the \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/standup/?fbclid=IwAR195tZTFjEdQtxK2QeeyV0-qn4tqqtbI04LV4Q6oOCaKiCXTxfQPG8bej0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planned \u8220\'20\'1Cstandup\u8221\'20\'1D strikes}}}\uc2  aimed at individual auto plants, with members from three plants walking out overnight after talks failed.\par \par \uc2 Under this strategy, a strike flares without warning at targeted, individual plants. Then additional locations follow \u8211\'20\'13 ramping up the pressure on the companies. \uc2 UAW\uc2  says as time goes on, more locals may be called on to join the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis gives us maximum leverage and maximum flexibility in our fight to win a fair contract at each of the big three automakers.\u8221\'20\'1D The option to strike across all facilities is \u8220\'20\'1Cstill on the table\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What are the costs?\par \par \uc2 The automotive industry contributes about 3-3.5% of the US gross domestic product (GDP), the broadest measure of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Vehicle supply \u8211\'20\'13 just recovering from pandemic shortages \u8211\'20\'13 would be hit hard. A month-long strike at the three automakers could cut output by as many as 500,000 vehicles, according to \uc2 Sam Fiorani\uc2 , vice-president of global vehicle forecasting for AutoForecast Solutions.\par \par \uc2 Ten-day strikes at all three automakers could cost manufacturers, workers, suppliers and dealers more than $5bn, according to economic consulting firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/price-strike-detroit-automakers-5-billion-study-2023-08-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anderson Economic Group}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Is the White House getting involved?\par \par \uc2 Biden appeared to support the strikers when he spoke at a press briefing hours after the strike began on Friday. The president said in his White House address: \u8220\'20\'1CRecord corporate profits \u8230\'20\'26 should be shared by record contracts for the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also expressed regret that the strike had not been averted but urged both parties to return to the negotiating table. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one wants a strike but I respect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to use their options under the collective bargaining system and understand their frustrations,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do appreciate that the parties have been working around the clock. It is my hope that the parties can return to the negotiating table to forge a win-win agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His comments came after business groups had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/09/biden-uaw-strike-labor-00114867"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2  the White House to intervene to avert a strike. Hours after the strike began, the president also reportedly said he would send aides to Detroit to mediate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230913ej9d001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
