\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \u8216\'20\'18Defining moment\u8217\'20\'19 as auto workers strike after talks fail with car giants\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,358 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par 10:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Deadline expires with sides still far apart on union\u8217\'20\'19s contract priorities. Plus, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  indicted on federal charges\u8226\'20\'22 Don\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Auto workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/15/auto-workers-strike-ford-gm-stellantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a series of strikes}}}\uc2  after their union failed to reach agreement with the US\u8217\'20\'19s three largest manufacturers over a new contract, kicking off the most ambitious industrial labor action in decades.\par \par \uc2 The deadline for talks between Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 expired at midnight on Thursday, with the sides still far apart on the union\u8217\'20\'19s new contract priorities.\par \par \uc2 The strike, which marks the first time all three of the \u8220\'20\'1CDetroit Three\u8221\'20\'1D carmakers have been targeted by strikes at the same time, is being coordinated by the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain. He said he intended to launch a series of limited and targeted \u8220\'20\'1Cstandup\u8221\'20\'1D strikes to shut individual auto plants around the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our defining moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \uc2 UAW\uc2  is staggering the strikes, rather than having all 150,000 members walk out at once, to allow the union to stretch resources.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many workers are employed at the first plants on strike? Strikes kicked off at midnight at three plants of a combined 12,700 workers (a \uc2 General Motors\uc2  plant in Wentzville, Missouri, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  plant in Toledo, Ohio, and a Ford assembly plant in Wayne, Michigan).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do workers demand? Among the demands are a 40% pay increase, an end to tiers \u8211\'20\'13 where some workers are paid at lower wage scales than others \u8211\'20\'13 and the restoration of concessions from previous contracts such as medical benefits for retirees, more paid time off and rights for workers affected by plant closures.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How much is the strike fund? The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has a $825m strike fund that is set to compensate workers $500 a week while out on strike, and could support all of its members for about three months.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  indicted on gun charges after plea deal falls apart\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  was indicted by federal prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/14/hunter-biden-gun-charges-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on gun charges on Thursday}}}\uc2 , after a plea deal with the president\u8217\'20\'19s son fell apart in July. His lawyer said prosecutors were \u8220\'20\'1Cbending to political pressure\u8221\'20\'1D by filing the indictment.\par \par \uc2 A court filing in the US district court in Delaware alleged Biden, 53, illegally obtained and possessed a Colt revolver in October 2018 after falsely declaring that he was not a user of, or addicted to, narcotic drugs.\par \par \uc2 This is the first time the son of a sitting US president has been indicted on federal criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 The surprise indictment was brought by David Weiss, a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointee as US attorney for Delaware, who was named by the attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , as a special counsel last month after the collapse of the plea deal that included two misdemeanor tax charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How long could he face in prison if convicted? Up to 25 years. Biden faces up to 10 years in prison on each of two counts of making false statements to a Delaware gun dealer who sold him the gun, and five for possessing it as someone with drug addiction.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  to visit Biden as Congress debates $24bn in aid\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/14/volodymyr-zelenskiy-ukraine-visit-joe-biden-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected at the White House and on Capitol Hill}}}\uc2  next week as he visits the US during the United Nations general assembly.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s trip comes as Congress is debating President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s request to provide as much as $24bn in military and humanitarian aid for Ukraine as it fights the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 Congress is increasingly divided over providing additional funding for Ukraine as the war is well into its second year, with conservative Republican lawmakers pushing for spending cuts looking to stop money to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on the frontlines, the general staff of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s armed forces has reported that it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-zelenskiy-to-visit-washington-kim-and-putin-give-each-other-rifles?page=with:block-650406738f0844ae3ac04a80#block-650406738f0844ae3ac04a80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized the village of Andriivka}}}\uc2  from Russian forces in the partially occupied Donetsk region, and that it shot down 17 drones launched at Ukraine by Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , continues to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-zelenskiy-to-visit-washington-kim-and-putin-give-each-other-rifles?page=with:block-6503ddd88f083f8242cdc20e#block-6503ddd88f083f8242cdc20e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 host}}}\uc2  the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, and the pair visited a far-eastern Russian city on Friday that builds fighter jets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How much is Biden seeking to aid Ukraine? Biden has sought a package of $13.1bn in additional military aid for Ukraine and $8.5bn for humanitarian support. It also includes $2.3bn for financing and to catalyze donors through the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 When was the last time Zelenskiy visited Washington, DC? In December 2022, he delivered an impassioned address to a joint meeting of Congress, thanking Americans for their \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestment\u8221\'20\'1D in global security and democracy.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Libya\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general has been asked by senior politicians to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/14/libya-call-for-inquiry-fury-death-toll-catastrophic-floods"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launch an urgent inquiry}}}\uc2  into the catastrophic floods that killed thousands of people, including into allegations local officials imposed a curfew on the night Storm Daniel struck.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 British television channels agreed to let Buckingham Palace censor television coverage of \uc2 King Charles\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronation, according to the former boss of Sky News, including demanding the \u8220\'20\'1COrwellian\u8221\'20\'1D right to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/sep/14/british-tv-allowed-monarchy-to-censor-king-charles-coronation-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retrospectively ban footage}}}\uc2  after it had been broadcast.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court has sentenced a far-right fanatic to 17 years in prison for his role in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/14/far-right-fanatic-sentenced-17-years-coup-attempt-brazil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed attempt}}}\uc2  to topple the country\u8217\'20\'19s leftwing government on 8 January this year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Spanish police have arrested three unnamed reserve players at the soccer giant Real Madrid for allegedly distributing a sexual video featuring a minor. The arrests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/sep/14/three-real-madrid-players-arrested-for-alleged-sexual-video-involving-minor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow an ongoing furore}}}\uc2  about misogyny and entrenched sexism in Spanish football.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three artworks by Egon Schiele believed stolen\par \par \uc2 from a Jewish art collector during the Holocaust have been seized by New York law enforcement authorities. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2023/sep/15/egon-schiele-artworks-believed-stolen-holocaust-seized-us-museums"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 art was seized}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Art Institute of Chicago\uc2 , the Carnegie Museums of Pittsburgh and the Allen Memorial Art Museum at \uc2 Oberlin College\uc2  in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18I survived rabies\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2004, when I was 15, I watched a petrified little bat flap around inside my church in Wisconsin during a Sunday service. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know it, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/sep/15/experience-i-survived-rabies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that bat would change my life}}}\uc2 . It clamped down hard on my finger. The puncture mark was no bigger than a pinprick, but it oozed blood and was very painful. Three weeks later, I started feeling unbelievably tired. My mom mentioned the bat bite to a paediatrician and his face went white. The next day, the rabies diagnosis was confirmed. My parents were told this was a near-guaranteed death sentence. No one had survived rabies without a vaccination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check: New files shed light on \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to undermine climate science\par \par \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2  executives privately sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/14/exxonmobil-documents-wall-street-journal-climate-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undermine climate science}}}\uc2  even after the oil and gas giant publicly acknowledged the link between fossil fuel emissions and climate change, according to previously unreported documents revealed by the Wall Street Journal. The documents were subpoenaed by New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general as part of an investigation into the company announced in 2015. Many of the documents date back to the 2006-16 tenure of former chief executive \uc2 Rex Tillerson\uc2 . \uc2 Exxon\uc2  publicly accepted that the climate crisis posed risks in 2006 yet continued to bolster climate denial.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Reanimated spiders and smart toilets triumph at Ig Nobel prizes\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s Ig Nobel prizes \u8211\'20\'13 a satire of the more stately Nobel prizes that awards achievements to unusual or trivial scientific phenomenon since 1991 \u8211\'20\'13 has celebrated using dead spiders to grip objects and smart toilets that monitor stool. This year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/sep/14/reanimated-spiders-and-smart-toilets-triumph-at-ig-nobel-prizes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ig Nobel prize for public health}}}\uc2  was awarded to researchers for the development of a smart toilet that uses various technologies to monitor human waste for signs of disease and an anal-print sensor as part of its system to identify the user, Nicola Davis writes.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230915ej9f001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
