\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war: conflict is most \u8216\'20\'18acute threat\u8217\'20\'19 to international order, says Blinken \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang (now); Yohannes Lowe, Martin Belam and Helen Livingstone (earlier) \par \uc2 10,492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2023\par 20:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US secretary of state says \u8216\'20\'18Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war of aggression\u8217\'20\'19 threatens order \u8216\'20\'18enshrined in \uc2 UN\uc2  charter\u8217\'20\'19Ukrainian missiles strike Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea fleet in Crimea\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It is slightly past 11pm in Kyiv. Here is a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Romania has found new fragments of a drone similar to those used by the Russian army near its border, according to its officials. Helicopters from the Romanian air force were deployed to the eastern county of Tulcea with specialist teams where the fragments were spread over an area of \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral dozen meters\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 Romanian defense ministry\uc2  said. Reuters reports preliminary analyses of the first two drone fragments have shown they did not explode in Romania, a Nato member, and were not carrying explosives.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  visited jailed US citizen Paul Whelan on Wednesday and reiterated Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support to bring him back to the US, the state department said on Wednesday. Whelan, a former marine, was arrested in 2018 in Russia. In 2020, he was convicted on espionage charges and was sentenced to 16 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US state department on Wednesday said that the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate\u8221\'20\'1D to impose additional sanctions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  and North Korea if they establish further new arms deals. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have taken a number of actions already to sanction entities that brokered arms sales between North Korea and Russia and we won\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate to impose additional sanctions if appropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D state department spokesperson Matthew Miller said during a briefing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During a White House press briefing on Wednesday, national security council spokesperson John Kirby expressed concerns over the upcoming talks between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  and North Korea. \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to urge North Korea to meet its public commitments not to support Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 There will certainly be repercussions,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An award-winning Russian journalist living in exile in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  was hacked using Israeli spyware made by NSO Group, according to a joint investigation by the Citizen Lab and \uc2 Access Now\uc2 . \uc2 Galina Timchenko\uc2  was hacked on or around 10 February, at a time when she was based in Berlin, Germany, marking the first time that an independent Russian journalist \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jan/26/russia-outlaws-meduza-in-attempt-to-stamp-out-independent-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whose media outlet has been targeted by Moscow and declared an \u8220\'20\'1Cundesirable organisation\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is known to have been hacked with spyware.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-6501d3b08f0893e8a8a024f0#block-6501d3b08f0893e8a8a024f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a speech delivered to the Johns Hopkins School of Advanced International Studies}}}\uc2 , the US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2 , said that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cis the most immediate and acute threat to the international order enshrined in the \uc2 UN\uc2  charter and its core principles of sovereignty, territorial integrity, and independence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Russian-installed court in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Donetsk region jailed two Ukrainian soldiers for 29 years each, \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s investigative committee\uc2  said on Wednesday, after it accused them of killing three civilians. Moscow has repeatedly sentenced captured Ukrainian soldiers to long jail terms, in court proceedings that Kyiv does not recognise on Russian-occupied territory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un on Wednesday discussed the possibility of sending a North Korean cosmonaut into space, the RIA news agency quoted Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov as saying. Speaking after the Russian president and North Korean leader concluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6501498d8f0873945374e536#block-6501498d8f0873945374e536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks at the Vostochny cosmodrome in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far east}}}\uc2 , Peskov also said that the foreign ministers of the two countries would meet next month in North Korea.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 100 port infrastructure facilities have been damaged in Russian attacks on Ukrainian ports since 18 July, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure minister, \uc2 Oleksandr Kubrakov\uc2 , said on Wednesday. He also said Ukrainian grain exports had fallen by almost 3m tonnes a month since 18 July \u8211\'20\'13 one day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/20/what-was-the-black-sea-grain-deal-and-why-did-it-collapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  after Russia quit the UN- backed Black Sea grain export deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Russian defence minister, \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2 , said on Wednesday that his forces were maintaining \u8220\'20\'1Cactive defence\u8221\'20\'1D in the face of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/02/ukraine-counter-offensive-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s counteroffensive}}}\uc2  and that Moscow had no choice but to win. Shoigu said the autumn campaign was now under way and acknowledged in comments to a reporter for Rossiya-1 state TV that the situation on the front was difficult in places.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , said a major series of policy reviews will be launched to ensure the 27-nation bloc can still function properly as it invites in new members in coming years. \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said that the \uc2 EU\uc2  must prepare to grow to more than 30 members, the Associated Press reports. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , Moldova and countries in the western Balkans are among those in line.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un has pledged to support all of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s decisions as he met \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  during a rare trip outside North Korea. Speaking at Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Vostochny cosmodrome, Kim said \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has risen to a sacred fight to protect its sovereignty and security. We will always support the decisions of President Putin and the Russian leadership \u8230\'20\'26 and we will be together in the fight against imperialism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. Here is a parting piece by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Andrew Roth on the significance of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s bilateral meeting between North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kim Jong Un\uc2  and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/13/nothing-left-to-lose-putin-embraces-role-of-spoiler-with-kim-jong-un-summit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Nothing left to lose\u8217\'20\'19: Putin embraces role of spoiler with Kim Jong-un summit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Romania has found new fragments of a drone similar to those used by the Russian army near its border, according to its officials.\par \par \uc2 Helicopters from the Romanian air force were deployed to the eastern county of Tulcea with specialist teams where the fragments were spread over an area of \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral dozen meters\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 Romanian defense ministry\uc2  said, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe crew of an IAR 330 Puma helicopter of the Romanian air force... [identified] fragments that could have come from a drone, dispersed over an area of several dozen metres,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports preliminary analyses of the first two drone fragments have shown they did not explode in Romania, a Nato member, and were not carrying explosives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one has attacked us,\u8221\'20\'1D Romanian prime minister Marcel Ciolacu told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CSome pieces of a drone that was hit by the Ukrainian army fell. It did not have explosives or anything damaging,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 A Nato spokesperson said that Romania\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador has updated its allies about the findings and that there is no indication of \u8220\'20\'1Cany intentional attack by Russia against allied territory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNato stands in solidarity with our ally Romania,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 US ambassador visits jailed US citizen Paul Whelan\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador to Russia visited jailed US citizen Paul Whelan on Wednesday and reiterated Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support to bring him back to the US, the state department said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Whelan, a former marine, was arrested in 2018 in Russia. In 2020, he was convicted on espionage charges and was sentenced to 16 years in prison. Whelan and the \uc2 US government\uc2  have repeatedly denied the charges and maintained his innocence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe Paul continues to show tremendous courage in the face of his wrongful detention. Ambassador Lynne Tracy reiterated to him that president Biden and Secretary Blinken are committed to bring him home,\u8221\'20\'1D state department spokesperson Matthew Miller said at a press briefing.\par \par \uc2 Tracy has also made three visits to \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , a Wall Street Journal reporter who was arrested by Russian officials in March and is currently facing spying charges. The White House has designated both Whelan and Gershkovich as \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongfully detained\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 US 'won't hesitate' to impose more sanctions on Russia and North Korea\par \par \uc2 The US state department on Wednesday said that the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate\u8221\'20\'1D to impose additional sanctions on Russia and North Korea if they establish further new arms deals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have taken a number of actions already to sanction entities that brokered arms sales between North Korea and Russia and we won\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate to impose additional sanctions if appropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D state department spokesperson Matthew Miller said during a briefing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you see what looks to be increased cooperation and probably military transfers, that is quite troubling and would potentially be in violation of multiple \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolutions,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 During a White House press briefing on Wednesday, national security council spokesperson John Kirby expressed concerns over the upcoming talks between Russia and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to urge North Korea to meet its public commitments not to support Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine \u8230\'20\'26 There will certainly be repercussions,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got to see what shakes out of this meeting \u8230\'20\'26 We obviously have concerns about any burgeoning defence relationship between North Korea and Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Kirby also said that it is a concern that Russia could be \u8220\'20\'1Cactively promoting\u8221\'20\'1D the improvement of North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s missile program.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 An award-winning Russian journalist living in exile in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  was hacked using Israeli spyware made by NSO Group, according to a joint investigation by the Citizen Lab and \uc2 Access Now\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Galina Timchenko\uc2  was hacked on or around 10 February, at a time when she was based in Berlin, Germany, marking the first time that an independent Russian journalist \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jan/26/russia-outlaws-meduza-in-attempt-to-stamp-out-independent-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whose media outlet has been targeted by Moscow and declared an \u8220\'20\'1Cundesirable organisation\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is known to have been hacked with spyware.\par \par \uc2 The attack occurred shortly before a meeting in Berlin of the main independent Russian media in exile, in which participants including Timchenko discussed the pressure they were under and how to respond to it. It was organised by a Russian organisation called Redkollegiya.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/sep/13/exiled-russian-journalist-galina-timchenko-reportedly-hacked-using-nso-group-spyware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exiled Russian journalist hacked using NSO Group spyware}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far...\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-6501d3b08f0893e8a8a024f0#block-6501d3b08f0893e8a8a024f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a speech delivered to the Johns Hopkins School of Advanced International Studies}}}\uc2 , the US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2 , said that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cis the most immediate and acute threat to the international order enshrined in the \uc2 UN\uc2  charter and its core principles of sovereignty, territorial integrity, and independence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 100 port infrastructure facilities have been damaged in Russian attacks on Ukrainian ports since 18 July, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure minister, \uc2 Oleksandr Kubrakov\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-6501ae6c8f0893e8a8a022c4#block-6501ae6c8f0893e8a8a022c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Wednesday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Russian defence minister, \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2 , said that his forces were maintaining \u8220\'20\'1Cactive defence\u8221\'20\'1D in the face of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/02/ukraine-counter-offensive-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s counteroffensive}}}\uc2 , and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-6501a0de8f0893e8a8a02203#block-6501a0de8f0893e8a8a02203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moscow had no choice but to win}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un has offered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vladimir-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin}}}\uc2  his support for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csacred fight\u8221\'20\'1D against the west during talks that also touched on possible Russian help with North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s space programme. The North Korean and Russian leaders met on Wednesday at a space base in the far east of Russia amid warnings that Kim was poised to offer the Kremlin artillery shells and other munitions for the war in Ukraine. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/13/kim-jong-un-putin-weapons-talk-russian-space-base-amur"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Putin reportedly offered Russian help with the Pyongyang regime\u8217\'20\'19s troubled satellite programme}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has made \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat strides\u8221\'20\'1D to join the \uc2 EU\uc2  since being granted candidate status in 2022, the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , has said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-650170c58f0873945374e676#block-650170c58f0873945374e676"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s enduring support}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-650189cd8f08cf50e1613c5f#block-650189cd8f08cf50e1613c5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She also said}}}\uc2  a major series of policy reviews will be launched to ensure the 27-nation bloc can still function properly as it invites in new members in coming years.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fragments of a possible drone were found in Nato member Romania on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016#block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the defence ministry said}}}\uc2 , after a new Russian attack on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Danube ports across the border. Ukraine said the attack early on Wednesday had struck the ports of Reni and Izmail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine said it struck Russian naval targets and port infrastructure early on Wednesday in the Crimean city of Sevastopol, in what appeared to be the biggest attack of the war on the home of the Russian navy\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea Fleet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian military intelligence agency official said on Wednesday that a large Russian landing ship and a submarine struck in an overnight attack on the Crimean port of Sevastopol were likely to have been damaged beyond repair (see post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-65016ae28f0873945374e654#block-65016ae28f0873945374e654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 08.58}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose are significant damages. We can now say that with a high probability they are not subject to restoration,\u8221\'20\'1D Andriy Yusov, the official, said in televised comments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  has nearly completed repairs of its power systems after Russian airstrikes on energy infrastructure last winter, and is ready for the coming winter, a senior energy official said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have installed all the equipment we planned and we are ready for the winter loads,\u8221\'20\'1D Volodymyr Kudrytskiy, head of state-owned Ukrenergo power grid operator, told national television.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s campaign of frequent missile and drone attacks resulted in power cuts and scheduled blackouts to limit energy use, leaving towns and cities in darkness for hours at a time over winter.\par \par \uc2 Kudrytskiy said there was a \u8216\'20\'18high risk\u8217\'20\'19 of new attacks on the county\u8217\'20\'19s energy system this winter, but that Ukrainian air defences were much stronger now, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 We know what it looks like (to be attacked) and it will be very difficult for the enemy to surprise us after the 1,200 missiles they fired at the power system last winter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Russian-installed court in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Donetsk region jailed two Ukrainian soldiers for 29 years each, \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s investigative committee\uc2  said on Wednesday, after it accused them of killing three civilians.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has repeatedly sentenced captured Ukrainian soldiers to long jail terms, in court proceedings that Kyiv does not recognise on Russian-occupied territory.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s investigative committee\uc2  said the two soldiers belonged to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Azov regiment \u8211\'20\'13 a branch of the Ukrainian army considered \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist\u8221\'20\'1D in Russia.\par \par \uc2 It said that the two \u8220\'20\'1Cshot at a car with two unarmed civilians using automatic firearms, as a result of which the men in the car died on the spot from their injuries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The men then \u8220\'20\'1Cshot at two other unarmed civilians\u8221\'20\'1D on the street, killing one while the other managed to escape, the committee said, according to AFP.\par \par \uc2 Both soldiers fought in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2023/feb/23/mariupol-the-ruin-of-a-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Ukrainian city of Mariupol}}}\uc2 , which was captured by Russian forces last May after a devastating, three-month long siege that left the city in ruins.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the committee said earlier that another Azov soldier was sentenced in absentia to 24 years in prison for \u8220\'20\'1Cshelling a humanitarian aid distribution point\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Romania \u8217\'20\'19s ministry of foreign affairs said after Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s drone findings that it \u8220\'20\'1Creiterates its firm protest against the violation, once again, of Romania\u8217\'20\'19s airspace\u8221\'20\'1D and that it will summon the head of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic mission, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Nato member Romania found new fragments of a drone deemed similar to those used by the Russian army near its border with Ukraine on Wednesday, in the third such finding in a week, defence officials said (see earlier post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016#block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10.51}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine war is most 'acute threat' to international order enshrined in \uc2 UN\uc2  charter - Blinken\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2  , has tweeted the comments he delivered to the Johns Hopkins School of Advanced International Studies.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, he wrote:\par \par \uc2 We find ourselves at another hinge point in history grappling with the fundamental question of strategy as Nitze defined it: \u8220\'20\'1CHow do we get from where we are to where we want to be, without being struck by disaster along the way?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What we are experiencing now is more than a test of the post-cold war order. It\u8217\'20\'19s the end of it. Decades of relative geopolitical stability have given way to an intensifying competition with authoritarian, revisionist powers.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war of aggression in Ukraine is the most immediate and acute threat to the international order enshrined in the \uc2 UN\uc2  charter and its core principles of sovereignty, territorial integrity, and independence.\par \par \uc2 Blinken added that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2  poses a more \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant long-term challenge\u8221\'20\'1D due to its desire to carve out a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew international order\u8221\'20\'1D and the fact that it has the technological, economic, diplomatic and military power to do so.\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  speaks at Johns Hopkins School of Advanced International Studies, in Washington. Photograph: Cliff Owen/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 India and Russia will explore the possibility of using new transport corridors such as the Northern Sea Route and the Eastern Maritime Corridor to widen maritime cooperation, the Indian government said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A decision to work towards this was made during a meeting between minister from the two countries in Russia, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has more information on the fragments of a possible drone being found in Nato member Romania on Wednesday (see earlier post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016#block-650185318f0893e8a8a02016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10.51}}}\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the defence ministry said:\par \par \uc2 The crew of an IAR 330 Puma helicopter of the Romanian Air Force \u8230\'20\'26 (identified) fragments that could have come from a drone, dispersed over an area of several dozen metres.\par \par \uc2 It said that the fragments were found near the villages of Nufarul and Victoria in Tulcea county.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, it would be the third time that such fragments have been found on Romanian territory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/06/romania-says-possible-drone-debris-found-on-its-territory-near-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in recent days}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Preliminary analyses of the first two drone fragments have shown they did not explode in Romania and were not carrying explosives, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one has attacked us,\u8221\'20\'1D prime minister Marcel Ciolacu told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CSome pieces of a drone that was hit by the Ukrainian army fell. It did not have explosives, or anything damaging.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The defence ministry has started building two bomb shelters in the small border village of Plauru, where the first two fragments were found.\par \par \uc2 It said it would deploy additional troops in the area, and increase patrols and observation points, while local residents will receive notification alerts to take shelter.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/06/romania-says-possible-drone-debris-found-on-its-territory-near-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato pledges \u8216\'20\'18strong solidarity\u8217\'20\'19 with Romania over likely Russian drone debris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un on Wednesday discussed the possibility of sending a North Korean cosmonaut into space, the RIA news agency quoted Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov as saying.\par \par \uc2 Cosmonauts are people specifically trained by the \uc2 Russian Space Agency\uc2  to work in space.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after the Russian president and North Korean leader concluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6501498d8f0873945374e536#block-6501498d8f0873945374e536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks at the Vostochny cosmodrome in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far east}}}\uc2 , Peskov also said that the foreign ministers of the two countries would meet next month in North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Peskov added that there were no plans for Putin himself to visit Pyongyang, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 A senior Ukrainian official has described the overnight strike on Sevastopol as a \u8220\'20\'1Cprofessional and meaningful \u8216\'20\'18statement\u8217\'20\'19. Ukraine claims to have damaged a large landing ship and a submarine in a strike on the base of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea fleet in occupied Crimea.\par \par \uc2 Mykhailo Podolyak\uc2 , adviser to the head of the office of the president of Ukraine, posted to social media to say:\par \par \uc2 The demilitarisation of the Russian Black Sea fleet is a real long-term guarantee of security for regional trade routes and the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrain corridor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This is the only correct response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to turn hunger into a weapon and the only way to ensure uninterrupted grain supplies to the countries of the east and Africa.\par \par \uc2 The way to do this is to build up the capacity of the armed forces of Ukraine, including by expanding the range of weapons. We can already see the results of this in Sevastopol. A professional and meaningful \u8220\'20\'1Cstatement\u8221\'20\'1D...\par \par \uc2 enltrThe demilitarization of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russian}}}\uc2  Black Sea fleet is a real long-term guarantee of security for regional trade routes and the "grain corridor". This is the only correct response to Russia's attempts to turn hunger into a weapon and the only way to ensure uninterrupted grain\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lk6dZ52xhZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Lk6dZ52xhZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??????? ??????? (@Podolyak_M) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Podolyak_M/status/1701946426568114188?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier, \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  said in statement that Ukraine had attacked with ten cruise missiles and three uncrewed speedboats, damaging two vessels that had been undergoing repairs\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nato\uc2  has just issued a minimalist press alert announcing that tomorrow its secretary general, \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2 , will meet Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Olha Stefanishyna\uc2  at its Brussels headquarters. She is the minister for European and Euro-Atlantic Integration of Ukraine. The press release stipulates that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere will be no media opportunities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , said Ukraine had made \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat strides\u8221\'20\'1D in its attempt to join the \uc2 EU\uc2 . Ukraine has also requested to join \uc2 Nato\uc2 , which has expanded to include Finland since Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, with Sweden awaiting ratification of its membership of the alliance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kyiv says 105 Ukrainian port infrastructure facilities damaged in Russian attacks since 18 July\par \par \uc2 More than 100 port infrastructure facilities have been damaged in Russian attacks on Ukrainian ports since 18 July, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure minister, \uc2 Oleksandr Kubrakov\uc2 , said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 He also said Ukrainian grain exports had fallen by almost 3m tonnes a month since 18 July \u8211\'20\'13 one day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/20/what-was-the-black-sea-grain-deal-and-why-did-it-collapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  after Russia quit the UN- backed Black Sea grain export deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kubrakov wrote on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Since 18 July, due to Russian attacks on Ukrainian ports, 105 port infrastructure facilities have been damaged and partially destroyed. As a result of strikes on the ports of the Danube cluster and the blocking of seaports, grain exports to Asia, Africa and Europe were reduced by almost 3 million tons per month.\par \par \uc2 These claims are yet to be independently verified.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has been exporting grain through a Croatian port for over a year, says official\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has been exporting grain through a northern Croatian port for more than a year, an official told AFP on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports:\par \par \uc2 Despite being hundreds of miles from Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s western border, Croatia has become an unlikely transit point for the country\u8217\'20\'19s grains due to the ongoing Black Sea blockade by the Russians.\par \par \uc2 Approximately 100,000 tonnes of Ukrainian corn and wheat have been exported from northern Croatia\u8217\'20\'19s Rijeka port since May 2022, according to Marino Klaric, the head of the facility\u8217\'20\'19s grain terminal.\par \par \uc2 The grain travels to Croatia by rail via Hungary. The amount is a mere fraction of the millions of tonnes grain Ukraine produces annually.\par \par \uc2 To date, the Rijeka port\u8217\'20\'19s annual grain capacity is just one million tonnes. However, officials are scrambling to expand the facility\u8217\'20\'19s export capacity.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, prime minister \uc2 Andrej Plenkovic\uc2  repeated Zagreb\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to increase the export of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s grain through its ports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCroatia sees itself as the Mediterranean door for central Europe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Plenkovic.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s agriculture sector has come under mammoth pressure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/20/what-was-the-black-sea-grain-deal-and-why-did-it-collapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since the Kremlin pulled out of a UN- and Turkey-brokered grain deal in July}}}\uc2 , which aimed to ensure safe navigation for civilian ships.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is most alarmed by Putin\u8217\'20\'19s reported interest in North Korean weaponry, and said last week that Pyongyang would \u8220\'20\'1Cpay a price\u8221\'20\'1D if it supplied Russia.\par \par \uc2 South Korea and the US have said that any arms deal would violate \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolutions supported by Russia.\par \par \uc2 Russia was expected to use Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s talks to seek artillery shells and antitank missiles from Pyongyang, which wants advanced satellite and nuclear-powered submarine technology in return.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear whether Russia would be willing to share such sensitive technologies in exchange for what could be a limited amount of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Korean ammunition}}}\uc2  slowly delivered across the countries\u8217\'20\'19 small shared border.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story on the Kim-Putin talks here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/13/kim-jong-un-putin-weapons-talk-russian-space-base-amur"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kim Jong-un offers Putin \u8216\'20\'18full support\u8217\'20\'19 in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18sacred fight\u8217\'20\'19 with west}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia has 'no other options' but to win in Ukraine, defence minister says\par \par \uc2 The Russian defence minister, \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2 , said on Wednesday that his forces were maintaining \u8220\'20\'1Cactive defence\u8221\'20\'1D in the face of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/02/ukraine-counter-offensive-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s counteroffensive}}}\uc2 , and that Moscow had no choice but to win.\par \par \uc2 Shoigu said the autumn campaign was now under way and acknowledged in comments to a reporter for Rossiya-1 state TV that the situation on the front was difficult in places.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 The forces are maintaining active defence on the necessary, essential fronts. In some places it\u8217\'20\'19s harder, in others simpler.\par \par \uc2 But I can say that the lads and the commander are performing confidently, and reliably defending what we need to defend at the moment \u8211\'20\'13 those places, obviously, where the Ukrainian armed forces are trying to break through.\par \par \uc2 The main task was to knock out enemy weaponry, he added.\par \par \uc2 Russia controls nearly a fifth of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s territory after more than 18 months of war, but has been forced to pull back from large areas it seized in its initial invasion near the capital Kyiv and in the south and east.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine launched a long-anticipated counteroffensive in June that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/28/ukraine-confirms-capture-of-key-village-robotyne-zaporizhzhia-front"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recaptured more than a dozen villages}}}\uc2  but has been complicated by vast minefields and heavily entrenched Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Russia would win, Shoigu replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no other options\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  said two military vessels damaged in an overnight Ukrainian missile strike on Sevastopol in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/mar/18/putin-confirms-annexation-crimea-ukrainian-soldier-casualty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian-annexed Crimea}}}\uc2  would be repaired and continue in service, state news agency RIA reported.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine said it struck Russian naval targets and port infrastructure early on Wednesday, in what appeared to the biggest attack of the war on the home of the Russian Black Sea Fleet.\par \par \uc2 The attack on Crimea highlighted Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s growing missile capabilities as Russia continues to bombard Ukraine long-range missiles and assault drones.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe confirm a large landing vessel and submarine were hit. We do not comment on the means (used) for the strike,\u8221\'20\'1D Ukrainian military intelligence official Andriy Yusov told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  said in statement that Ukraine had attacked a Black Sea shipyard with 10 cruise missiles and three uncrewed speedboats in the early hours of Wednesday, damaging two vessels that had been undergoing repairs (see earlier post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-650138018f08cf50e16139a1#block-650138018f08cf50e16139a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 05.21}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Smoke rises from the shipyard that was reportedly hit by Ukrainian missile attack in Sevastopol, Crimea. Photograph: Reuters Tv/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Russian foreign minister, \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 , has said the geopolitical climate had changed completely since the \uc2 UN\uc2  imposed sanctions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/north-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Korea}}}\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Since 2006, North Korea has been under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/mar/12/north-korea-sanctions-un-investigating-possible-violations-in-about-20-countries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN sanctions}}}\uc2 , which Russia supported, over its banned nuclear weapons and missile programmes.\par \par \uc2 Lavrov told Russian TV reporter Pavel Zarubin:\par \par \uc2 Sanctions against North Korea were adopted in a completely different geopolitical situation when there were problems establishing dialogue (with Pyongyang), when there were quite serious debates in the security council.\par \par \uc2 He said the reason that Russia and China had blocked a further US-drafted sanctions resolution against North Korea last year was that the West had given a false promise at the time of the original sanctions on humanitarian aid for the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was another lie. We, the Chinese and the North Koreans were deceived,\u8221\'20\'1D Lavrov said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The west needs to prepare for a long war in Ukraine, army chief warns\par \par \uc2 The west needs to prepare for a long war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  and to deal with an increasingly hostile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  even after it is over, the Czech military chief Karel Rehka told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 After weeks in which some western military officials have been quoted expressing concern that Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s summer counteroffensive was proceeding too slowly, the chief of the general staff said during an interview at Czech military headquarters that he was not frustrated by the pace of progress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how a military offensive looks,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not like a world war two movie. It takes time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ukraine launched its counteroffensive in June and has so far captured only around a dozen small villages, though it says that in recent weeks it has pierced Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defensive line and expects to move more quickly. Moscow says Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s offensive has already failed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the overall picture, I think there is currently no capacity on either side to reach their ultimate declared objectives any time soon,\u8221\'20\'1D Rehka said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt won*t last a few weeks, it will last for long, probably. And it\u8217\'20\'19s important that we keep supporting Ukrainians for a long time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rehka, whose Nato member country has contributed ammunition, tanks, armoured vehicles, rocket launchers and howitzers to the Ukrainian war effort, said the Czech Republic still has arms in storage that it could provide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Russia sees prospects for cooperating with North Korea in space, says Kremlin spokesperson\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said Russia sees prospects for cooperating with North Korea in space, Russian state news agency Tass reported.\par \par \uc2 He was speaking after \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  held talks with the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, at a cosmodrome in far eastern Russia where Moscow conducts space launches.\par \par \uc2 In August, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/20/russia-luna-25-space-craft-crashes-into-the-moon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s first moon mission in 47 years failed after its Luna-25 spacecraft spun out of control and crashed into the moon}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It dealt a significant setback to the embattled Russian space programme\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to revive its Soviet-era prestige.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Russia will show Pacific Fleet capabilities to Kim Jong-un during visit, Putin says\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Wednesday that the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, would continue his tour of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far east with a visit to Vladivostok and to defence and other factories in Komsomolsk-on-Amur, RIA news agency reported.\par \par \uc2 Putin said Russia would demonstrate to Kim in Vladivostok the capabilities of its Pacific Fleet, adding that Russia also had something to offer North Korea in the area of agriculture, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Putin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65017bcb8f08cf50e1613ba8#block-65017bcb8f08cf50e1613ba8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who earlier held talks with Kim at the Vostochny cosmodrome}}}\uc2  and hosted a lunch for the North Korean leader, also said there were opportunities for bilateral military-technical cooperation, though he added that Russia would comply with its international obligations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s talks with Kim Jong-un were \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant and substantive\u8221\'20\'1D, Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said on Wednesday in comments quoted by the Interfax news agency.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after the two leaders held talks in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far east region, Peskov added that North Korea was interested in cooperation with Russia in the areas of aviation and transport.\par \par \uc2 Kim reportedly offered his full support for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cjust fight\u8221\'20\'1D and said the two reached an agreement to deepen their \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic and tactical cooperation and solidarity in the struggle to defend sovereign rights and security\u8221\'20\'1D (see earlier post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65017bcb8f08cf50e1613ba8#block-65017bcb8f08cf50e1613ba8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10.09}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am BST\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  chief announces major review saying the bloc should grow to over 30 members\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , said a major series of policy reviews will be launched to ensure the 27-nation bloc can still function properly as it invites in new members in coming years.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said that the \uc2 EU\uc2  must prepare to grow to more than 30 members, the Associated Press reports. Ukraine, Moldova and countries in the western Balkans are among those in line.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said the commission\u8217\'20\'19s reviews will examine how each policy sector in areas like the economy, energy, agriculture or migration would need to be adapted in the event of expansion.\par \par \uc2 She told \uc2 EU\uc2  lawmakers in Strasbourg, France:\par \par \uc2 We will need to think about how our institutions would work \u8211\'20\'13 how the (EU) parliament and the commission would look. We need to discuss the future of our budget \u8211\'20\'13 in terms of what it finances, how it finances it, and how it is financed.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  also has said that Ukraine has made \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat strides\u8221\'20\'1D to join the \uc2 EU\uc2  since being granted candidate status in 2022 (see earlier post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/13/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-sevastopol-shipyard-fire-crimea-missile-attack-injuries?page=with:block-650170c58f0873945374e676#block-650170c58f0873945374e676"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 09.26}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  reacts on the day of the annual State of the EU address to the European parliament, in Strasbourg, France. Photograph: Yves Herman/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un has pledged to support all of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s decisions as he met \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  during a rare trip outside North Korea. Speaking at Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Vostochny cosmodrome, Kim said \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has risen to a sacred fight to protect its sovereignty and security. We will always support the decisions of President Putin and the Russian leadership \u8230\'20\'26 and we will be together in the fight against imperialism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Putin welcomed Kim, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe, of course, need to talk about questions of economic cooperation and questions of a humanitarian nature. We have a lot of questions.\u8221\'20\'1D The US has suggested that Russia is seeking North Korean military hardware to aid in the invasion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 . North Korea has previously denied supplying weapons to Moscow. The two leaders made brief comments in public before holding private talks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has made \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat strides\u8221\'20\'1D to join the \uc2 EU\uc2  since being granted candidate status in 2022, the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , has said, offering the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s enduring support. She was addressing the European parliament as the bloc considers whether to grant a formal start of membership negotiations. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know this is not an easy road,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CAccession is merit-based. It takes hard work and leadership. But there is already a lot of progress. We have seen the great strides Ukraine has already made since. Our support to Ukraine will endure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An overnight attack on the port of Sevastopol, home to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea fleet in occupied {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/crimea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crimea}}}\uc2 , has struck a large Russian landing ship and a submarine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims it shot down 32 \u8220\'20\'1CShahed\u8221\'20\'1D drones out of 44 launched overnight in attacks on Odeshchyna and Sumy. The Ukrainian military has also claimed partial success near Klishchiivka in the Bakhmut direction.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2  confirmed on Wednesday that Papal envoy Cardinal Matteo Zuppi will visit China later in the week for talks on resolving the conflict in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  has protested to Azerbaijan over comments it made about the weekend regional elections held in areas of Ukraine which are claimed to be annexed by Moscow. Kyiv has declared the elections a sham.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hungary has agreed with Romania, Slovakia and Bulgaria that the four countries would impose national bans on Ukrainian grains imports if the \uc2 EU\uc2  does not extend an existing ban that expires on 15 September, Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s farm minister said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Romania condemns Russian attacks on Ukranian Danube ports, reports possible drone fragments found in Romania\par \par \uc2 Elements of a possible drone were identified on Romanian territory, Reuters reports the \uc2 Romanian defence ministry\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A Russian drone attack early on Wednesday damaged port infrastructure in the Izmail district of southern Ukraine, just across the border from Romania.\par \par \uc2 In a press statement the ministry said \u8220\'20\'1C[Romanian] forces remain on alert and will continue investigations in areas where risks may arise as a result of this situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mapn.ro/cpresa/18098_comunicat-de-presa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  went on to say:\par \par \uc2 The ministry of national defence strongly condemns the attacks carried out by the Russian Federation against some objectives and elements of civil infrastructure in the Ukrainian ports on the Danube. These attacks are unjustified and in serious contradiction with the rules of international humanitarian law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters is carrying that Kim Jong-un quote in full now, which was given in translation. He told his host \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I am deeply convinced that the heroic Russian army and people will brilliantly inherit the tradition of victory, confidently demonstrate invaluable dignity and honour on the fronts of the special military operation.\par \par \uc2 The Russian army and people will certainly win a great victory in the sacred struggle for the punishment of a great evil that claims hegemony and feeds an expansionist illusion.\par \par \uc2 Special military operation is the preferred term by Russian authorities for the full-scale invasion of Ukraine launched in February 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that a Kremlin spokseperson has confirmed that the meeting between \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un will conclude today. The location of the event, and even whether it would be happening at all, have been shrouded in mystery for much of the week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un says he is sure Russian army and people will win against 'evil'\par \par \uc2 North Korean leader Kim Jong-un told Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  via a translator on Wednesday that he was sure that the Russian army and people would triumph against \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As well as offering a toast to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s health, Kim also said the pair had agreed on a further deepening of strategic cooperation.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, Putin in turn proposed a toast for strengthening friendship and the wellbeing between the people of the two nations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Suspilne, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state broadcaster, reports that an 81-year-old woman has been taken to hospital with injuries after a Russian attack on Odradokamyanka in the Kherson region.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2 : Ukraine has made 'great strides' towards EU membership\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has made \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat strides\u8221\'20\'1D to join the \uc2 EU\uc2  since being granted candidate status in 2022, the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , has said, offering the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s enduring support.\par \par \uc2 She was addressing the European parliament as the bloc considers whether to grant a formal start of membership negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know this is not an easy road,\u8221\'20\'1D Reuters reports \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CAccession is merit-based. It takes hard work and leadership. But there is already a lot of progress. We have seen the great strides Ukraine has already made since.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur support to Ukraine will endure,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in her annual policy speech.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , is applauded after giving her annual state of the union address. Photograph: Frederick Florin/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  promised the bloc would extend special protections granted to Ukrainian citizens who fled Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war, and lawmakers gave a standing ovation as she recounted the fate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/07/victoria-amelina-obituary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Amelina}}}\uc2 , the Ukrainian writer and activist killed after having sent her son to safety in Prague.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some more of the images being released from the summit in Russia between \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un.\par \par \uc2 Members of the North Korean delegation attend the Russian-North Korean talks. Photograph: \uc2 Vladimir Smirnov\uc2 /SPUTNIK/KREMLIN POOL/EPA Russian minister of industry and trade \uc2 Denis Manturov\uc2  (L) and defence minister \uc2 Sergei Shoigu\uc2  (R) at the Vostochny cosmodrome. Photograph: \uc2 Vladimir Smirnov\uc2 /SPUTNIK/KREMLIN POOL/EPA Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  waits for the North Korean leader. Photograph: Mikhail Metzel/SPUTNIK/KREMLIN POOL/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine claims large Russian landing ship and submarine hit in Sevastopol strike\par \par \uc2 Andriy Yusov, a Ukrainian military spy agency official, said on Wednesday that an overnight attack on the port of Sevastopol, home to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea fleet in occupied Crimea, had struck a large Russian landing ship and a submarine.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports Yusov told it \u8220\'20\'1CWe confirm a large landing vessel and submarine were hit. We do not comment on the means (used) for the strike.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40am BST\par \par \uc2 On its Telegram channel, Tass has reported that the face-to-face meeting between Putin and Kim has now ended.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38am BST\par \par \uc2 China confirms Papal peace envoy visit for talks about Ukraine\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2  said on Wednesday that Papal envoy Cardinal Matteo Zuppi will visit China for talks on resolving the conflict in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports a spokesperson at the foreign ministry confirmed that China\u8217\'20\'19s special envoy for Eurasian affairs Li Hui will meet with Zuppi.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican had said on Tuesday that Zuppi will be in China from Wednesday to Friday as part of a diplomatic push to facilitate peace in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2  has also been giving a press conference this morning, and in it she lambasted Azerbaijan and Armenia.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports she accused Armenia of making \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable and harmful\u8221\'20\'1D statements that were damaging to the prospects for a peace settlement between Armenia and Azerbaijan over the breakaway territory of Nagorno-Karabakh.\par \par \uc2 She said the \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  has also protested to Azerbaijan over comments it made about the weekend regional elections held in areas of Ukraine which are claimed to be annexed by Moscow. Kyiv has declared the elections a sham.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the video clip of Kim Jong-un telling Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  that North Korea supports Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csacred battle with the west\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25am BST\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting that we may not actually get any kind of formal joint declaration or read out after the meeting between \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un today. RIA\u8217\'20\'19s unofficial Telegram channel for its Kremlin pool journalists points out that \u8220\'20\'1CThe DPRK, Russia, and China do not have such a procedure as the mandatory release of a joint document after a summit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Hungary signals it intends to retain Ukrainian grain ban\par \par \uc2 Hungary has agreed with Romania, Slovakia and Bulgaria that the four countries would impose national bans on Ukrainian grains imports if the \uc2 EU\uc2  does not extend an existing ban that expires on 15 September, Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s farm minister said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports the minister of agriculture, Istv\u225\'00\'E1n Nagy, saying in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post that the ban would apply to a wider range of Ukrainian products than the current measures.\par \par \uc2 Some eastern European countries have complained that Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s inability to export goods through its Black Sea ports has led to a flooding of local markets with cheap Ukrainian produce, which is affecting their own agricultural sectors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un pledges to support Putin and Russia 'in the fight against imperialism'\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un has pledged to support all of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s decisions as he met \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  during a rare trip outside North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Vostochny cosmodrome, Kim said \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has risen to a sacred fight to protect its sovereignty and security. We will always support the decisions of President Putin and the Russian leadership \u8230\'20\'26 and we will be together in the fight against imperialism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Putin welcomed Kim, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe, of course, need to talk about questions of economic cooperation and questions of a humanitarian nature. We have a lot of questions.\u8221\'20\'1D The US has suggested that Russia is seeking North Korean military hardware to aid in the invasion of Ukraine. North Korea has previously denied supplying weapons to Moscow.\par \par \uc2 A Kremlin spokesperson said the relationship between Russia and North Korea is not aimed at other countries, and should not be a worry for third countries. North Korea launched two ballistic missiles into the sea this morning as a demonstration of strength while Kim was out of the country. Japan has protested.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s President Putin and North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s leader Kim meet in Amur region. Photograph: SPUTNIK/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Putin and Kim have now begun face-to-face talks, which Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said would involve dialogue and cooperation in sensitive spheres, including the military.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has just published a full transcript of the remarks made by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Kim Jong-un in front of the media at the Vostochny cosmodrome. The Russian president welcomed North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s leader saying:\par \par \uc2 Dear Mr Chairman, I am very glad to see and welcome you again in Russia \u8211\'20\'13 this time, as we agreed, at our Vostochny cosmodrome.\par \par \uc2 We are proud of how this sector is developing here, and this is our new facility. I hope both you and your colleagues find this interesting.\par \par \uc2 Our meeting is taking place at a very special time, after all. Most recently, the Democratic People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of Korea celebrated 75 years of its creation and foundation. Seventy-five years of establishment of diplomatic relations between our countries. Let me remind you that it was our country that was the first to recognise the sovereign independent state \u8211\'20\'13 the Democratic People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of Korea.\par \par \uc2 Then very soon we will celebrate the 70th anniversary of the end of the War of independence and the victory of the Korean people in this war. This is a landmark date, because our country also helped our friends in the Democratic People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of Korea to fight for this independence.\par \par \uc2 We, of course, need to talk about questions of economic cooperation and questions of a humanitarian nature. We have a lot of questions. I want to say that I am very glad to see you. Thank you for accepting the invitation and coming to Russia.\par \par \uc2 Kim\u8217\'20\'19s response was as follows:\par \par \uc2 I express my gratitude to you for paying such attention to our visit to Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Soviet Union played a very big role in the liberation of our country. Our friendship has deep roots, and now relations with the Russian Federation are the first priority for our country I am sure that our meeting will be the next step to take relations to a new level.\par \par \uc2 Russia has risen to a sacred fight to protect its sovereignty and security \u8230\'20\'26 against the hegemonic forces. We will always support the decisions of President Putin and the Russian leadership \u8230\'20\'26 and we will be together in the fight against imperialism.\par \par \uc2 Reuters also notes that Kim wrote in a visitor book at the centre: \u8220\'20\'1CThe glory to Russia, which gave birth to the first space conquerors, will be immortal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29am BST\par \par \uc2 On the ground in Ukraine, Suspilne has this round-up of overnight news, posting to Telegram to report:\par \par \uc2 At night, the Russian army attacked Odeshchyna with drones: there is damage to the port and civil infrastructure. Seven people were injured.\par \par \uc2 Air defence forces destroyed 32 Shahed drones out of 44 launched. Russian troops attacked Odeshchyna and Sumy region with them at night.\par \par \uc2 Defence forces have partial success near Klishchiivka in the Bakhmut direction, said the spokesperson of the general staff.\par \par \uc2 In the last 24 hours three people were killed and three others were injured as a result of shelling by the Russian Federation in Donetsk region. Four people were injured in Kherson region. One person was injured in Zaporizhzhia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are a couple more of the official images being released to the press of Kim Jong-un \u8217\'20\'19s visit to meet \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s leader, Kim Jong-un, visit the Vostochny cosmodrome. Photograph: Mikhail Metzel/AFP/Getty Images Putin and Kim study a display at the Vostochny cosmodrome. Photograph: Mikhail Metzel/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Amid the flurry of diplomatic activity between Russia and North Korea today, Reuters reports that Russia has announced the Chinese foreign minister, Wang Yi, will visit Moscow on 18 September for talks with Russian counterpart, \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This is Martin Belam taking over the live blog in London. You can contact me at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:martin.belam@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 martin.belam@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11am BST\par \par \uc2 North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles into the sea off its east coast on Wednesday, just an hour before Kim Jong-un met \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Citing South Korean officials, Reuters reports the missiles were launched from near the North Korean capital of Pyongyang, and flew about 650km (404 miles).\par \par \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s joint chiefs of staff condemned the launch as a violation of \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolutions and Japan\u8217\'20\'19s chief cabinet secretary, \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2 , told reporters Japan had lodged a protest through diplomatic channels in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 It appeared to be the first such launch to occur while Kim was abroad.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00am BST\par \par \uc2 North Korea supports all Russia's decisions, Kim Jong-un tells Putin, and will join fight against imperialism\par \par \uc2 North Korea supports all Putin\u8217\'20\'19s decisions, Kim has told the Russian president according to Russian media, and it will always stand with Russia in the fight against imperialism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has risen to a sacred fight to protect its sovereignty and security... against the hegemonic forces,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim told Putin via a translator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will always support the decisions of president Putin and the Russian leadership... and we will be together in the fight against imperialism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said that he hoped today\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations would raise relations between their two countries to a new level.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53am BST\par \par \uc2 North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst priority\u8221\'20\'1D is its relations with Russia, Kim has told Putin according to Russian media.\par \par \uc2 Putin told Kim he was aware the North Korea leader was visiting \u8220\'20\'1Cat a special time\u8221\'20\'1D, noting that this year marks the 75th anniversary of the country\u8217\'20\'19s founding, Tass reported. Putin noted that it was the USSR that was the first to recognise it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46am BST\par \par \uc2 In case you\u8217\'20\'19re hungry for more information about the Vostochny Cosmodrome where Kim and Putin are meeting, Reuters has prepared a fact sheet about it \u8211\'20\'13 here are some of the highlights:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The cosmodrome, which came into service in 2016, is in the Amur region of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Far East, not far from the Russian border with China and about 1,500 km (930 miles) from the port of Vladivostok. In Russian, the name means simply \u8220\'20\'1CEastern Cosmodrome\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Putin ordered the construction of the cosmodrome to reduce reliance on the Baikonur Cosmodrome in Kazakhstan, which gained independence after the 1991 collapse of the Soviet Union.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There was once a Soviet intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) base known as Svobodny 18 just a few kilometres from the Vostochny complex. That base shut down in 1993.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vostochny cost billions of dollars, giving a boost to the local economy. But construction was mired by repeated delays and several corruption scandals.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/apr/28/putin-rocket-launch-cosmodrome-soyuz-delay-space"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first launch was in 2016}}}\uc2 , when a Soyuz-2 rocket blasted off. The most recent launch was a Soyuz rocket carrying the ill-fated Luna-25 moon spacecraft, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/20/russia-luna-25-space-craft-crashes-into-the-moon#:~:text=The%20Luna%2D25%20mission%20sought,human%20colony%20on%20the%20moon."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which crashed into the moon}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Luna-25 blasts off from Vostochny Cosmodrome in August. Photograph: \uc2 ROSCOSMOS\uc2 /Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Talks between Kim and Putin begin at cosmodrome\par \par \uc2 Formal negotiations between Putin and and Kim have begun at the Vostochny cosmodrome in Amur, Tass reports and include members of the delegations from each country.\par \par \uc2 The meeting is taking place \u8220\'20\'1Cin the meeting room on the first floor of the engineering building of the technical complex of the Soyuz-2 space rocket complex,\u8221\'20\'1D the Russian news agency writes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27am BST\par \par \uc2 While Ukraine was launching its attack on Sevastopol, Russia was attacking the Black Sea city of Odesa with drones that targeted port infrastructure, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air force has said. The north-eastern Sumy region was also targeted.\par \par \uc2 A total of 44 drones were recorded, the airforce said, with most aimed at Odesa. Thirty-two were shot down.\par \par \uc2 In Russia, a drone was shot down in the Konakovo district of the Tver region, north-west of Moscow, the news agency Ria reported citing regional authorities. No casualties were reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has some comment from Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov, who was asked whether Kim and Putin would discuss weapons supplies, as expected by western observers.\par \par \uc2 In response, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs neighbours, our countries implement cooperation in sensitive areas that should not become the subject of public disclosure and announcement. But this is quite natural for neighbouring states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08am BST\par \par \uc2 More pictures are coming through on the wires. Here Putin and Kim are enjoying a tour of the cosmodrome:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Kim\u8217\'20\'19s sister, \uc2 Kim Yo Jong\uc2 , who has become an influential figure in North Korean politics, has also been spotted at the cosmodrome talks:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45am BST\par \par \uc2 The North Korean and Russian leaders will \u8220\'20\'1Ctalk about all the issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said when asked whether military-technical cooperation would be on the agenda, Russian news agency Ria reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll talk about all the issues, slowly. There is time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 When asked whether Russia would help Pyongyang build satellites he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we came to the Vostochny Cosmodrome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe leader of the DPRK [North Korea] shows great interest in rocket technology, and they are trying to develop space,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36am BST\par \par \uc2 A bit of footage of Putin greeting Kim, from Russian news agency Ria:\par \par \uc2 rultr????? ? ??? ??? ?? ?????????? ?? ?????????? "?????????" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eQh5oCHSJu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eQh5oCHSJu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YwmmsaFeOs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YwmmsaFeOs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??? ??????? (@rianru) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rianru/status/1701815393084440711?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Putin welcomes Kim to cosmodrome\par \par \uc2 Russian media have posted video of Putin welcoming Kim to the cosmodrome, surrounded by officials and photographers.\par \par \uc2 Kim thanked Putin for the invitation to visit Russia, \u8220\'20\'1Cdespite being busy,\u8221\'20\'1D Tass reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am glad to see you,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said as he shook Kim\u8217\'20\'19s hand for around 40 seconds. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our new cosmodrome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine fired ten cruise missiles at the Sevastopol shipyard, \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  has said in a post on Telegram, and two ships undergoing repairs were hit and damaged. Three unmanned boats were also involved in the attack, it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAir defence systems shot down seven cruise missiles, and the patrol ship Vasily Bykov destroyed all unmanned boats,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un arrives at cosmodrome for meeting with Putin\par \par \uc2 The North Korean leader Kim Jong-un has arrived at the Vostochny Cosmodrome in Amur where he is expected to meet president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , Russian news agency Ria has reported.\par \par \uc2 His train had arrived at the railway station at the cosmodrone, it reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04am BST\par \par \uc2 US military expert Rob Lee suggests that it\u8217\'20\'19s a ship that has been struck in Sevastopol:\par \par \uc2 enltrMikhail Razvozhaev shared a photo that appears to show the port side of a Ropucha-class Project 775 large landing ship that sustained damage. 4/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PQ4XmUYxb0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PQ4XmUYxb0}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bU49kKn4GK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bU49kKn4GK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rob Lee (@RALee85) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RALee85/status/1701798722235965827?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Putin arrives at remote cosmodrome for expected meeting with Kim Jong-un\par \par \uc2 In other news, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has reportedly arrived at the Vostochny Cosmodrome in the remote region of Amur, the Russian news agency Tass has reported.\par \par \uc2 Putin had announced his trip to the cosmodrome while at an economic forum in Vladivostok, in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far east, where observers had initially expected him to meet Kim.\par \par \uc2 However, he refused to say what he would be doing in Vostochny, Tass reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have my own programme there, and when I get there, you\u8217\'20\'19ll find out ,\u8221\'20\'1D it quoted Putin as saying.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrHuge explosions as a result of a presumed Ukrainian attack in Sevastopol, the HQ of the Black Sea Fleet in Crimea. Russian authorities say the Sevmorzavod shipyard has been targeted. Ships based in Sevastopol frequently fire missiles at Ukrainian cities. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dKgb0CEtLr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dKgb0CEtLr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yaroslav Trofimov (@yarotrof) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/yarotrof/status/1701792907529748858?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Huge blaze at Sevastopol shipyard after Ukraine air attack, Russia says\par \par \uc2 A fire has broken out and 24 people have been injured after a Ukrainian missile attack on the Sevastopol shipyard in occupied Crimea, the Russia-installed governor of the port has said.\par \par \uc2 Mikhail Razvozhayev said the blaze was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot at a civilian facility\u8221\'20\'1D and that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno danger\u8221\'20\'1D to civilians in a post on Telegram. He also posted a picture of himself in front of what appeared to be a vessel or port infrastructure on fire.\par \par \uc2 Russian Telegram channels also posted videos of explosions and huge flames.\par \par \uc2 The shipyard on the Crimean peninsula, which was annexed by Russia in 2014, builds and repairs ships and submarines for the Russian Black Sea Fleet, which has launched drone and missile attacks on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has increased its attacks on the peninsula in recent months. It also said earlier this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/ukraine-regains-control-of-strategic-black-sea-oil-rigs-intelligence-service-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it had recaptured strategic Black Sea oil rigs}}}\uc2  that had been seized by Russia in 2015.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the war in Ukraine with me, Helen Livingstone.\par \par \uc2 Twenty-four people have been injured after a Ukrainian missile attack on Sevastapol Shipyard that sparked a fire, the Russia-installed governor of the port has said.\par \par \uc2 Mikhail Razvozhayev posted a picture of himself in front of what appeared to be a huge blaze at the shipyard, which builds and repairs vessels for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Black Sea fleet. He said there was no danger to civilians.\par \par \uc2 There were also reports of huge explosions at the port. Earlier traffic on the Kerch bridge, which connects Crimea with mainland Russia was temporarily halted, Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Ria news agency reported, without giving any further details.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/kim-jong-un-arrives-russia-vladivostok-vladimir-putin-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrived in Russia on his armoured train}}}\uc2  for a rare summit with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to discuss a possible deal to supply North Korean arms for the war in Ukraine. It had been thought the North Korean leader would meet the Russian president in Vladivostok but the exact date and location of the meeting remained unclear as of late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US could have the first Ukrainian pilots trained on F-16 fighter jets before the end of the year, though it will be longer than that before they are flying combat missions, the director of the US Air National Guard said. Ukrainian pilots are expected to arrive for training in Arizona by October and depending on their proficiency in English and previous flying experience could complete the training in three months.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nato member Romania said it had begun building air raid shelters for residents near the Ukraine border, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/06/romania-says-possible-drone-debris-found-on-its-territory-near-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after drone fragments were found there last week}}}\uc2 . Approximately 50 Romanian soldiers began building two shelters in the Plauru area on Tuesday, the defence ministry said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Poland said it would extend a ban on Ukrainian grain imports unilaterally, even if the current EU restrictions expire on Friday. In June, the \uc2 EU\uc2  agreed to restrict imports of grain from Ukraine to five member states, including Poland, seeking to protect their farmers who blamed those imports for the slump in prices on local markets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russian president Vladimir Putindirectly addressed the war in Ukraine during a Q&A session at the eastern economic forum in Vladivostok. He said that the Ukrainian counter-offensive had not made any progress and accused British secret services of being involved in the training of Ukrainian saboteurs to launch attacks on Russian infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Putin also appeared to rule out any further conscription or mobilisation to help the war effort, claiming that 1,000-1,500 Russians were signing voluntary contracts to join the military every day. The \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s Ministry of Defence\uc2  said in its daily intelligence briefing on Monday that Russia would probably seek to avoid a forced mobilisation before next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential elections, due to be held in March.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Foreign ministers from the \uc2 G7\uc2  group of major industrialised countries condemned the staging of what they called \u8220\'20\'1Csham elections\u8221\'20\'1D by Russia in occupied Ukrainian territories. \u8220\'20\'1CThese sham \u8216\'20\'18elections\u8217\'20\'19 will not alter our approach nor our support to Ukraine as it fights to reclaim its internationally-recognized territory,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Denmark will give Ukraine a further 5.8 billion kroner ($833m), mainly to finance air defences, ammunition and tanks, the defence ministry said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor Ukraine to be able to continue defending itself against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s illegal invasion, it is essential that countries like Denmark maintain their military and economic support,\u8221\'20\'1D defence minister Troels Lund Poulsen said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Russian warplane crashed during a training mission in southern Russia, the military said, without specifying what happened to its crew of two or what caused the crash. The defence ministry said that the Su-24 bomber went down in an unpopulated area in the Volgograd region.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Swedish government is considering donating Gripen fighter jets to Ukraine to help repel Russian forces, Swedish public radio (SR) reported. The government may formally ask the armed forces as early as Thursday to officially consider the issue, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230913ej9d000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
