\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US school bus drivers strike amid low pay and staff shortages\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 996 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par 10:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Driver shortages and lagging compensation have incited several strikes as huge school bus driver strike in New York City looms\par \par \uc2 The US is facing a series of school bus strikes as the new school year begins.\par \par \uc2 School bus driver shortages and lagging compensation have incited several strikes and raised the prospect of a huge school bus driver strike in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Every state in the US has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theweek.com/education/1026197/school-bus-driver-shortage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  at least one instance of a major school bus driver shortage, according to a recent USA Today analysis, with low driver pay, Covid-19 challenges, and inconvenient hours as some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/17/us/schools-bus-drivers-shortage-delays.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  contributing factors. School districts around the US have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gainesville.com/story/news/education/2023/08/21/driver-shortages-impacting-school-bus-schedules-in-alachua-county/70602442007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced delays}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fox17.com/news/crisis-in-the-classroom/tennessee-school-districts-take-steps-to-address-bus-driver-shortage-nashville-tennessee-education-bell-times-bus-routes-students-school?fbclid=IwAR2kLFR-96D0DiLSP1fU3ilNcX34weg9cdU1hO3IIQcyiVpttJj1nzR_9o4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed}}}\uc2  school schedules or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.edweek.org/leadership/a-districts-bus-disaster-highlights-a-nationwide-driver-shortage/2023/08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 canceled classes}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mynews13.com/fl/orlando/news/2023/08/08/-it-s-a-strain-on-everybody---orange-county-public-schools-doubling-back-bus-routes-as-it-struggles-to-fill-bus-driver-vacancies-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doubled routes}}}\uc2  for current bus drivers to try to alleviate driver shortages.\par \par \uc2 In New York City, school bus routes continued on Thursday 7 September and Friday 8 September, as new contract negotiations aimed at averting a strike continued between \uc2 Amalgamated Transit Union\uc2  Local 1181-1061 and school bus contractors.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Amalgamated Transit Union International\uc2  president, John Costa, argued the nationwide school bus driver shortage is being driven by the nature of the work, low pay and lack of benefits driven by privatization of school bus services where municipalities accept the cheapest contract bids.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what happens with privatization when there is a profit margin, that\u8217\'20\'19s what it\u8217\'20\'19s all about, greed and they take it off the workers\u8217\'20\'19 backs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Costa. \u8220\'20\'1CThe work is very hard. It\u8217\'20\'19s long hours, in the summer sometimes they lose their jobs. A lot of the contracts don\u8217\'20\'19t offer severance over summer like they do with teachers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the pandemic highlighted the precarious position of drivers. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were no Covid funds for the school bus industry so there were a bunch of layoffs when the shutdowns happened,\u8221\'20\'1D said Costa.\par \par \uc2 In New York City school bus drivers are working under a two-tier wage system due to concessions pushed on to drivers under the Mike Bloomberg administration, said Costa, and wages can vary widely for the same exact work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re in a situation now where they\u8217\'20\'19re working next to somebody else doing the same job and they get less pay, they get less holidays, they get less sick time, they get no severance for being out for summer. You\u8217\'20\'19re not helping morale by doing something like that, you\u8217\'20\'19re not helping your workforce,\u8221\'20\'1D said Costa. \u8220\'20\'1CMy members risked their lives, they died from Covid and now they go into contract negotiations and they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to talk about these things, they just want to put a small percentage on top. It isn\u8217\'20\'19t about the money. How do you have a system like this where half the workforce is getting more and the other half less?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tomas Fret, who assumed the role of president of the local union in 2022, is supporting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.laborpress.org/incoming-atu-1181-1061-head-backs-school-bus-bill-of-rights-calls-for-job-protections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school bus bill of rights }}}\uc2  that includes restoring employee protection provisions that were eliminated under Bloomberg in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The last school bus driver strike in New York City {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/16/nyregion/school-bus-drivers-union-in-new-york-considers-ending-strike.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occurred }}}\uc2  in 2013, lasting five weeks. The union is currently in negotiations as the possible strike looms next week.\par \par \uc2 On 5 September, school bus drivers in Coventry, Connecticut, represented by the same local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcconnecticut.com/news/local/back-to-school/school-bus-drivers-go-on-strike-in-bolton-and-coventry/3097861/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also went on strike}}}\uc2  and they may extend picket lines to Bolton, Willington, and Stafford, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 School bus drivers in the Lakota school district near Cincinnati, Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wcpo.com/news/local-news/lakota-parents-come-up-with-temporary-solutions-amid-bus-drivers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started striking }}}\uc2  on 1 September in a fight for a new union contract as a federal mediator intervened in trying to get the contractor and union, \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  Local 100, to reach an agreement. A tentative agreement was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wcpo.com/news/local-news/lakota-bus-drivers-to-resume-talks-wednesday-after-holiday-halt-in-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached}}}\uc2  on 6 September.\par \par \uc2 School bus drivers in Meriden, Connecticut, represented by Teamsters Local 671 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wtnh.com/news/connecticut/new-haven/meriden-school-bus-drivers-to-begin-strike-sept-1/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began }}}\uc2  striking on 1 September in a fight for a new union contract with their contractor, New Britain Transportation, that will bring their wages in line with other school bus contractors in the state. On 5 September, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courant.com/2023/09/05/meriden-school-bus-drivers-agree-to-temporary-contract-as-coventry-drivers-begin-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached }}}\uc2  a temporary agreement as the City of Meriden voided NBT\u8217\'20\'19s contract for failure to provide service during the strike and will work to replace the contractor. NBT did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Nick Frangiamore, field representative for local 671, said the contractor\u8217\'20\'19s final offer included several concessions and provided no paid holidays and inadequate wage increases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey had multiple routes to prevent this from happening,\u8221\'20\'1D said Frangiamore. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not trying to set industry standards, we just want drivers to get to what everyone else in the area is getting paid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the top rate for a 25-year school bus driver is $22.09 an hour, which is marginally above the starting rate in the area for a first-year bus driver at $21.50 an hour, with the median wage in the New Haven area is $22.90 with six to nine paid holidays as the standard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe starting wage for a school bus driver right now is about $21.50 an hour and the top rate is anywhere between $31 to $36 an hour and usually hit that top rate in about five or six years of service and NBT right now is $18.87 an hour to start and $22.09 at the top,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are the lowest paid, there is zero 401k, there\u8217\'20\'19s zero health benefits. It\u8217\'20\'19s by far the worst contract in the state and probably the worst one in the country for a bargained contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He explained due to the low wages and lack of benefits, school bus drivers have had to cover extra shifts and double runs to make up for the vacant bus routes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s supposed to be three hours in the morning, three hours in the afternoon, but they end up working 12-hour days and they\u8217\'20\'19re not compensated fairly for that,\u8221\'20\'1D added Frangiamore.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230908ej98000vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
