\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is psychological warfare\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers allege anti-union firings\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,217 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2023\par 10:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  has reinstated 28 of the more than 200 pro-union workers fired since late 2021\par \par \uc2 Alicia Flores had worked at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in Portland, Oregon, for seven years until June, when she received a voicemail from a manager \u8211\'20\'13 filling in for her usual boss, who was taking a leave of absence \u8211\'20\'13 who informed her she was being fired.\par \par \uc2 Flores is far from alone.\par \par \uc2 She is one of dozens of workers who have filed unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) against the coffee giant, alleging they were fired in retaliation for union organizing. Starbucks Workers United have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/17/business/starbucks-union-ruling.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  that more than 200 workers since December 2021 have been fired, and that several more have been pushed out in retaliation for union activity.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , decisions by board members, administrative law judges, federal district judges and federal appellate judges have ordered reinstatement of 28 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Flores got involved in a union campaign at her store. When \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  began enforcing work policies rigidly, she pushed back on management conduct that included removing union literature.\par \par \uc2 Flores said she had never received any corrective action until that day, in December 2022. She even demoted herself to a barista to try to protect herself from further disciplinary action.\par \par \uc2 Flores said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe documentation that I got fired \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s literally two sentences. It just states that I was under investigation, and due to the outcome of the investigation \u8211\'20\'13 and then it states what it was \u8211\'20\'13 it states it was sexual harassment, saying I sent an explicit picture to a co-worker. Which makes it sound like I sent a naked picture of myself! But I sent a picture of Lana Del Rey\u8217\'20\'19s album cover, so I got fired for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI got fired over voicemail. It was very dystopian. The manager said, \u8216\'20\'18Thank you, have a nice day.\u8217\'20\'19 How am I going to have a nice day after getting a voicemail where I just got fired?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s kind of ironic because the company prides itself on being pro-mental health\par \par \uc2 Alicia Flores\par \par \uc2 Flores recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/19-CA-323620"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , alleging her firing was retaliation for her union organizing activity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to try to get my job back. I know I\u8217\'20\'19m going to get my job back, but this is psychological warfare. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know what this is doing to people\u8217\'20\'19s mental health, and it\u8217\'20\'19s kind of ironic because the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stories.starbucks.com/emea/stories/2023/starbucks-partners-share-the-significance-of-our-mental-and-emotional-wellness-during-mental-health-awareness/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prides itself}}}\uc2  on being pro-mental health,\u8221\'20\'1D added Flores.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  unionizing campaign, starting in late 2021, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has fielded hundreds of unfair labor practice charges from workers and their union against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some 73 complaints are pending before administrative law judges, and regional \uc2 NLRB\uc2  offices have issued 100 complaints covering 357 unfair labor practice charges following investigations. A staggering 633 open or settled unfair labor practice charges have been docketed against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  by \uc2 NLRB\uc2  regional offices.\par \par \uc2 But the union drive goes on. The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has certified union election wins at more than 340 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  locations in 39 states plus Washington DC, representing more than 8,500 workers, though little progress toward a first union contract has been made.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has become the worst offender of federal labor law in modern US history, with 200+ violations and counting,\u8221\'20\'1D said Starbucks Workers United in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the court of public opinion and the court of law, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is beginning to pay a price for their actions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  continue to file unfair labor practice charges.\par \par \uc2 Haya Odeh worked as a barista for more than two years and helped to unionize her store in Wilmington, North Carolina. She said she was effectively fired after she attempted to transfer to one of the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  locations in the Chapel Hill area where she would be attending school.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was threatened, basically, that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to transfer if I organized, by my district manager, and I guess he kept his promise on his threat,\u8221\'20\'1D said Odeh. \u8220\'20\'1CI applied to three different stores separately. Two of those three, I\u8217\'20\'19ve talked to the store manager in person, and they were like, yes, we\u8217\'20\'19re hiring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTalking to these managers, they\u8217\'20\'19re saying they\u8217\'20\'19re looking for baristas, I give them my name and then suddenly, a day or two later, they\u8217\'20\'19ll call me back and tell me that when they were talking to their district manager, it seems that they\u8217\'20\'19re no longer needing any baristas for hire. And that\u8217\'20\'19s weird.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I was threatened, basically, that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to transfer if I organized\par \par \uc2 Haya Odeh\par \par \uc2 Odeh\u8217\'20\'19s transfer denial effectively ended her employment at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . She moved to Chapel Hill to finish her college degree, and wants to continue on to law school to become a labor attorney. Odeh {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/10-CA-323611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently filed }}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Celeste Cruz worked at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  as a shift supervisor in Montclair, New Jersey, for five years and filed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/22-CA-323456"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair labor practice charge}}}\uc2  last month over her exit from the company.\par \par \uc2 She said since her store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://montclairlocal.news/2022/08/montclairs-church-street-starbucks-votes-in-favor-of-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unionized}}}\uc2  last year, she faced retaliation from management for her role in the campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t take it any more. My store manager was making it very difficult for me, and I ended up finding a new job. I gave her my two weeks, respectfully, with a piece of paper, and I thanked her for the opportunity, and not too long afterward, they essentially terminated me and did not let me finish out my two weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cruz.\par \par \uc2 She claimed her role as an observer for the union during her store\u8217\'20\'19s union election ballot count, and her outspokenness in favor of the union, made her a target, and that she was made to feel uncomfortable and cornered by management. Despite her leaving, Cruz expressed solidarity with the union effort at her store and other stores nearby that have unionized, saying the movement will ultimately be successful for workers despite the company\u8217\'20\'19s opposition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a question for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 : if we are your partners, why are you so scared to sit down? Why are you running away from us when we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to just simply give you our proposals? I think that just speaks volumes about the bad-faith bargaining,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Cruz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 tactics are merely slowing us down. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to hit harder and faster, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to be quiet, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be loud about this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  disputed the allegations of unfair labor practices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the allegations made by Workers United are meritless, and that actions taken were both lawful and in alignment with long-established partner policies \u8211\'20\'13 not in retaliation for any partners\u8217\'20\'19 participation in, or support of, union activities,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CAs a company, we respect our partners\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize and to engage in lawful union activities without fear of reprisal or retaliation. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  trains managers that no partner will be disciplined for engaging in lawful union activity and that there will be no tolerance for any unlawful anti-union behavior.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230904ej94001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
