\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are burned out\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 UAW\uc2  ready to take on automakers in contract negotiations\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,701 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2023\par 11:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amid record profits, workers want to roll back concessions made to auto industry after the 2008 economic recession\par \par \uc2 For decades, the head of the powerful \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  has started negotiations with the CEOs of the US\u8217\'20\'19s top auto executives with a ceremonial handshake. Those days are over.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 UAW\uc2  members become the latest American workers to consider a massive strike over their union contract, newly elected \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain chose to mark the start of the talks by shaking hands with workers instead. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no point in having a big pomp and ceremony where we act like we\u8217\'20\'19re friends, and we\u8217\'20\'19re working together, when we\u8217\'20\'19re not,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain, while meeting with workers at a Ram truck factory in Sterling Heights, Michigan. \u8220\'20\'1CThe membership comes first. That\u8217\'20\'19s our job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was an aggressive move \u8211\'20\'13 ending a tradition that goes back to the 1960s \u8211\'20\'13 as the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 150,000 workers at Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  push for new union contracts ahead of the expiration of the current contracts on 14 September.\par \par \uc2 Tough talk has worked recently. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  threat to call a strike at UPS led to major concessions in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ups-teamsters-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contract negotiation}}}\uc2  last month. And Fain has taken a combative approach toward the automakers, emphasizing the immense profits of the corporations, multimillion-dollar executive salaries and the concessions workers took due to the 2008 economic recession that have yet to be repaid in subsequent contracts.\par \par \uc2 During a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  live stream on 8 August, Fain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/uaw.union/videos/2672183916277760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw}}}\uc2  a contract proposal from \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  in the trash, accusing the company of seeking concessions from workers. He has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/uaw-ford-gm-stellantis-labor-strike-eda3b48bfdfa04e0e7254ce7681972e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed}}}\uc2  the willingness of the union to strike if the automakers don\u8217\'20\'19t offer acceptable proposals to the union, though a strike authorization vote by members has yet to be called.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-auto-bargaining/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined}}}\uc2  numerous demands ahead of negotiations, including eliminating a two-tiered wage system in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-autos-usa-families/for-uaw-members-two-tier-wage-issue-is-personal-idUSKBN0OI0C420150602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new hires}}}\uc2  have been paid significantly lower wages for doing the same work, and significant wage increases, with the union citing automaker CEOs who have received on average 40% pay increases over the last four years.\par \par \uc2 Charles Mitchell, a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  worker for 11 years in Detroit, Michigan, said the ongoing contract negotiations reflected worsening wealth inequality between workers and corporate executives and shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Companies are becoming more profitable and making shareholders richer while forcing mandatory 60- to 70-hour work weeks\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  worker Charles Mitchell\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ability for an autoworker to provide for a family or even oneself has been more and more difficult. All the while companies are becoming more profitable and making shareholders richer while forcing mandatory 60- to 70-hour work weeks in assembly plants,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mitchell.\par \par \uc2 He also criticized the recent rigid attendance policies and mandatory overtime, issues that workers are pushing to address in the contract.\par \par \uc2 The union has also called for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=htOU-WtMA94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restoring}}}\uc2  cost-of-living adjustment pay that ties wages to inflation, medical benefits for retirees, a defined pension for all workers rather than 401(k) plans, increases to retiree pay, more paid time off, providing the right to strike to workers over plant closures, enacting a program to protect and support workers who lose their jobs due to plant shutdowns, and strong job security protections amid a transition to electric vehicle production.\par \par \uc2 Recent high-profile new union contract negotiations have successfully eliminated two-tier wage systems at other companies, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamstersjointcouncil10.com/breaking-teamsters-end-22-4-demolishing-two-tier-system-at-ups/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tentative agreement}}}\uc2  at UPS that members are currently voting on and an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.industryweek.com/talent/labor-employment-policy/article/21261869/caterpillar-ratifies-uaw-contract-that-eliminates-twotier-wages-prohibits-plant-closures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement }}}\uc2  at \uc2 Caterpillar\uc2  reached earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Long hours and broken promises\par \par \uc2 Since 2006, Dawnya Fernandinsen has worked for \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . But because she worked for a parts supplier subsidiary, Delphi, when she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/business/2023/02/02/congressmen-dan-kildee-michael-turner-make-new-effort-to-restore-lost-delphi-pension-benefits/69866538007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolled}}}\uc2  over her employment to work directly for \uc2 General Motors\uc2  in 2016, she lost 10 years of seniority and her entire pension, an issue facing many Delphi workers that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is seeking to address in bargaining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI ended up with no pension, I ended up losing all of my seniority, I ended up with nothing. So I ended up transferring to the \uc2 General Motors\uc2  plant that I\u8217\'20\'19m in now in Toledo, Ohio, and had to start all over,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fernandinsen. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 General Motors\uc2  has been coming out and saying they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to replace pensions lost or seniority loss, or whatever. But they owe that to us. We were deceived. We were lied to and somebody owes us to return that to us and make us whole again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She explained that all workers took concessions after the 2008 economic recession after being assured by \uc2 General Motors\uc2  that the takeaways were temporary until the company returned to profitability after bankruptcy, which it did, reaching {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://money.cnn.com/2012/02/16/news/companies/gm_earnings/index.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record profits}}}\uc2  in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  noted in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bi8wA4Xd1qE&embeds_referring_euri=https%3A%2F%2Fuaw.org%2F&embeds_referring_origin=https%3A%2F%2Fuaw.org&source_ve_path=Mjg2NjY&feature=emb_logo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  that the big three automakers have reported collective profits of nearly $250bn between 2013 and 2022 and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/president-fain-facebook-live-big-threes-record-profits-mean-record-contracts/#:~:text=Ford%2C%20General%20Motors%20and%20Stellantis,record%20contracts%2C%E2%80%9D%20Fain%20said."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 combined profit of $21bn}}}\uc2  in the first six months of 2023. The union also cited recent salaries of \uc2 GM\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  of $29m in 2022, Ford CEO \uc2 Jim Farley\uc2  of $21m in 2022 and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  CEO \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2  of $24m in 2022, contrasting the high executive pay to the lagging wages autoworkers have received since the 2009 concessionary contract.\par \par \uc2 Behind these immense profits, Fernandinsen argued, is a workforce that is being overworked with mandatory forced overtime and divided along different pay tiers and temporary statuses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe forced overtime \u8211\'20\'13 we are working to death. We are working 12-hour shifts, seven days a week, every day, week after week, month after month, year after year. We are burned out,\u8221\'20\'1D added Fernandinsen. \u8220\'20\'1CThese companies are profiting the way that they are and trying to convince the American people that they\u8217\'20\'19re hurting, but in the same breath coming out and bragging about it, and then telling us they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford everything that we\u8217\'20\'19re putting out there. They\u8217\'20\'19re forcing our hand to strike. It is not going to be on the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . What we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is everything that we lost, everything that they\u8217\'20\'19ve taken from us, everything that they betrayed us with. That\u8217\'20\'19s all we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for and they have the means to give it back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Big three retirees are hurting\par \par \uc2 Autoworker retirees are one group that is pushing hard for a new contract. There are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2019/11/13/gm-ford-retirees-bonus-payment-uaw-contract/2575731001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 300,000 retirees}}}\uc2  at the big three automakers who rely on retirement benefits.\par \par \uc2 Tony Candela, a retired autoworker since 2011 after working for decades at Chrysler (now \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 ), served in various roles in union leadership, including as president of UAW Local 136 in Missouri.\par \par \uc2 In 2009, Candela\u8217\'20\'19s Chrysler plant in Missouri was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timesnewspapers.com/southcountytimes/features/chrysler-to-end-all-production-at-fenton-plant/article_1f679ed1-7fc0-5add-b5ad-fd8a81ec7ba9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down}}}\uc2  as part of bankruptcy restructuring during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/cars/2014/12/30/auto-bailout-tarp-gm-chrysler/21061251/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2008 economic recession}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Amid the recession and in subsequent contracts, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  agreed to numerous concessions for retirees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2019/11/13/gm-ford-retirees-bonus-payment-uaw-contract/2575731001/#:~:text=The%202019%20contract%20ratified%20by,not%20include%20a%20retiree%20bonus."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including the elimination}}}\uc2  of inflation protection pay for retirees that provided lump sum payments at the end of the year to workers or widows based on inflation rates, elimination of healthcare for retirees and the takeaway of pensions for many workers, as they were replaced with 401(k)s for autoworkers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2009/04/24/business/24pensions.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreements}}}\uc2  in the wake of the 2008 recession .\par \par \uc2 [Automakers] are making money hand over fist off the backs of the workers and it\u8217\'20\'19s time that workers get their fair share\par \par \uc2 Retired autoworker Tony Candela\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe word \u8216\'20\'18suspended\u8217\'20\'19 does not mean permanent. It\u8217\'20\'19s a temporary situation, but as we speak, it has never been brought back from the big three automakers to membership. They\u8217\'20\'19re still working without a cost-of-living adjustment and retirees still have no protection from inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Candela. \u8220\'20\'1CThese people cannot live in this world without any type of protection from inflation. These people can\u8217\'20\'19t survive. They\u8217\'20\'19re living month to month barely on their pension without any protection from inflation and nobody seems to give a damn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Current employees also made concessions during the 2008 financial crisis that have yet to be reversed, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwidqNKE5NSAAxVzkIkEHeoTAHkQFnoECDEQAQ&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fid%2Fwbna33292381&usg=AOvVaw3iKkPUbEUZPBIhAL73ow8A&opi=89978449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elimination}}}\uc2  of cost-of-living adjustment raises, changes that limited overtime compensation and the enactment of a two-tiered wage system. Candela also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1987/06/26/us/bonuses-replace-wage-rises-and-workers-are-the-losers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  the use of bonuses and profit sharing that aren\u8217\'20\'19t negotiated with the union, but often used in lieu of wage increases.\par \par \uc2 Candela {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/politics/1982/07/21/uaw-meets-with-chrysler-on-contract-hopes-to-roll-back-1981-concessions/75026d59-e4cd-425d-8f22-fd6471e851cf/#:~:text=Under%20pressure%20from%20the%20federal,loans%20to%20save%20the%20company."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that in the 1980s, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  granted Chrysler concessions during financial turmoil, but those were returned in later contracts. In the case of the 2008 economic recession, however, those losses to workers have yet to be remedied despite the immense profits US automakers have reported in recent years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe union has bent over backwards to make these companies successful. They can no longer cry \u8216\'20\'18Well, we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford it, we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford this.\u8217\'20\'19 They are making money hand over fist off the backs of the workers and it\u8217\'20\'19s time that workers get their fair share,\u8221\'20\'1D added Candela. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time somebody cares. It\u8217\'20\'19s time somebody takes the bull by the horns and starts negotiating a living wage contract for all members, active and retirees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to the contract demands issued by the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , a spokesperson for \uc2 General Motors\uc2  said the \u8220\'20\'1Cbreadth and scope\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s demands, \u8220\'20\'1Cat face value, would threaten our ability to do what\u8217\'20\'19s right for the long-term benefit of the team. A fair agreement rewards our employees and also enables \uc2 GM\uc2  to maintain our momentum now and into the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Ford added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to working with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  on creative solutions during this time when our dramatically changing industry needs a skilled and competitive workforce more than ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  criticized Fain and claimed the union\u8217\'20\'19s demands were not feasible: \u8220\'20\'1CThe theatrics and personal insults will not help us reach an agreement that continues our proud history of providing good wages and benefits to our employees and maintaining \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 ability to be competitive in the market \u8230\'20\'26 We are committed to working with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  to reach an agreement based on economic realism, one that supports the long-term health and viability of our operations while responsibly rewarding your contributions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230821ej8l001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
