\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Los Angeles: hotel workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike ignites backlash among academics\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Yang \par \uc2 903 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2023\par 18:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Academics are boycotting their annual meeting after they say leadership spurned a union request to move online or cancel\par \par \uc2 The union representing thousands of hotel workers on strike in Los Angeles is clashing with a group of political scientists over a request to move its gathering out of the city. It has sparked tensions within the professional group, as members \u8211\'20\'13 experts in power and politics \u8211\'20\'13 are dissenting over how they ought to respond.\par \par \uc2 About 6,000 political scientists were to descend on downtown Los Angeles for days of paper reviews, networking events and off-site happy hours at their flagship annual convention by the \uc2 American Political Science Association\uc2  (APSA) in late August. It would be the largest conference happening in the city over Labor Day weekend, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 The city has essentially become a picket line. Thousands of unionized southern California hotel workers have been on strike, demanding higher wages and better benefits, since the beginning of July. They joined Hollywood writers and actors occupying streets in a separate part of the city, many of whom have been striking since May.\par \par \uc2 After the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://politicalsciencenow.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Unite_Here_Local_11_letter_to_the_American_Political_Science_Association.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked the organization to cancel}}}\uc2  its event, originally planned for the downtown JW Marriott Los Angeles LA Live, a hotel with its workers on strike, in mid-July, the group\u8217\'20\'19s executive council voted overwhelmingly, 19-4, to keep the convention in Los Angeles while moving in-person events to the convention center down the street.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a second letter requesting the move, the group said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to be clear that we are in compliance with this request. We are holding all our events at the [Los Angeles convention center], which does not have a labor dispute,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a statement by the organization\u8217\'20\'19s presidents.\par \par \uc2 Members of the political science association \u8211\'20\'13 including tenured professors, junior faculty and graduate students \u8211\'20\'13 criticized the leadership\u8217\'20\'19s response.\par \par \uc2 Leaders of the association\u8217\'20\'19s Latino caucus said they were \u8220\'20\'1Cwithdrawing\u8221\'20\'1D from this year\u8217\'20\'19s annual conference \u8220\'20\'1Cin solidarity with the union and hotel workers\u8221\'20\'1D. About one in 15 of the association\u8217\'20\'19s members identify as \u8220\'20\'1CLatino or Hispanic American\u8221\'20\'1D, whereas around two out of three identify as \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-Hispanic White or Euro-American\u8221\'20\'1D, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apsanet.org/RESOURCES/Data-on-the-Profession/Dashboard/Membership"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 membership data as of August 2022}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to stand in solidarity with the heavily Latina and immigrant hotel workers of Los Angeles and southern California,\u8221\'20\'1D said a statement posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now called X.\par \par \uc2 Others also flocked to the platform to express their frustration, saying the decision to keep the meeting in Los Angeles leaves members in the lurch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust the idea of trying to find someplace else is overwhelming,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lindsay Mayka, the chair of Latin American studies at Colby College, who is choosing to skip this year\u8217\'20\'19s conference because the hotel she had originally booked is on strike and she does not support the event. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s kind of being presented as, you know, everyone has to do what\u8217\'20\'19s right for themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maria Hernandez, a spokesperson for the union, told the Guardian it contacted \u8220\'20\'1Chundreds of organizations and thousands of individuals\u8221\'20\'1D and confirmed the political science group was the largest it asked to cancel.\par \par \uc2 The meeting is going to be a disaster, I would argue. It is going to be very unpleasant for their membership\par \par \uc2 Kurt Petersen of \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  11\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe meeting is going to be a disaster, I would argue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kurt Petersen, a co-president of \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  11. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is going to be very unpleasant for their membership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Petersen said he was hopeful workers would reach an agreement with hotel management by Labor Day weekend but that a settlement was by no means guaranteed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe association has tremendous leverage. Conventions are sought after in this world. They are coveted by cities,\u8221\'20\'1D said Petersen. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re the client. They have the power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The APSA did not respond to several requests for comment by time of publication.\par \par \uc2 Individual members have since announced they are withdrawing from the conference, and one member, Lauren Konken, a recent doctoral student at \uc2 Princeton University\uc2 , is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LKonken/status/1684984379930820608?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing an alternative conference}}}\uc2  for people to present papers and receive reviews.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI guess there\u8217\'20\'19s some irony in the fact that we all study politics, and we study power dynamics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Candis Smith, a professor of political science at \uc2 Duke University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI can see why many people would perceive that access leadership is not paying attention to the research of its members.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Smith, who said she will not be flying to Los Angeles but will attend panels and meetings online, does not think the group\u8217\'20\'19s leadership is doing anything with malicious intent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that people try to balance what they think is right for the membership, try to balance what they think is right for labor and try to balance what is right for the institution itself for it to, you know, continue on,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese clash sometimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a previous statement posted online, the APSA said its president and executive director had been \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in intense conversations with both the union and hotel management\u8221\'20\'1D and that the union had offered to help it relocate. It also honored requests for attendees to move events online.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re either in or you\u8217\'20\'19re not,\u8221\'20\'1D said Petersen. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd unfortunately they have denied the request that we have made to them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230814ej8e0018n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
