\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 Emmy awards 2023: event moved to 2024 as Hollywood strikes continue\b0\par\par\uc2 Sian Cain \par \uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par 13:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The highest honours in television will now happen in January next year, as Sag-Aftra and writers unions picket for better pay and protection against AI\par \par \uc2 The 2023 Emmy awards have been pushed back four months to 15 January 2024 due to the ongoing writers\u8217\'20\'19 and actors\u8217\'20\'19 strikes in Hollywood, the Television Academy and ceremony broadcaster Fox said in a joint announcement on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 This is the first time the Emmys, the highest honours in television, have been postponed since 2001, when the 9/11 terrorist attacks pushed the ceremony, normally held in September, to November.\par \par \uc2 The 2023 Emmy nominations were announced last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/jul/12/emmys-2023-nominations-succession-the-last-of-us-white-lotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Succession, The Last of Us, The White Lotus and Ted Lasso leading the nominees}}}\uc2 . The announcement fell 48 hours before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/jul/14/the-hollywood-actors-strike-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hollywood actors went on strike}}}\uc2 , joining {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/02/thousands-of-hollywood-film-and-tv-writers-to-go-on-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 film and television writers who have been on picket lines since May}}}\uc2 , after talks with the major studios broke down.\par \par \uc2 The Creative Arts Emmy awards, which honour artistic and technical achievements in television, have also been moved and will now take place on 6 and 7 January.\par \par \uc2 It first emerged last month that the 2023 Emmys would likely move from its 18 September date when vendors for the event revealed to Hollywood trade publications that they had been told to prepare for an imminent date change.\par \par \uc2 The four-month delay reflects the mood in Hollywood that any deal between the Writers Guild of America (WGA) and actors guild Sag-Aftra with the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) appears to not be imminent.\par \par \uc2 Actors and writers remain firm that they want residual payments to become viewership-based, to address the minuscule pay some have received from streaming services for huge hits. They also want to see higher minimum staffing levels on shows, and for studios to address their concerns about artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  continues to be unwilling to discuss overhauling residuals, maintaining a bullish line that writers and actors will run out of money before they do. Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/07/writers-strike-hollywood-studios-deal-fight-wga-actors-1235434335/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline quoted an unnamed studio executive}}}\uc2  who said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe endgame is to allow things to drag on until union members start losing their apartments and losing their houses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former Fox and Paramount boss \uc2 Barry Diller\uc2  has suggested that studio heads and A-listers should agree to a 25% pay cut to address inequality \u8211\'20\'13 a move met with silence from those who would take the hit.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Disney\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2022/film/finance/bob-iger-compensation-package-salary-bob-chapek-fired-1235439151/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is paid more than $70,000 a day}}}\uc2 , has been criticised for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/jul/13/disney-bob-iger-actors-writers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 describing the strikes as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and the actors\u8217\'20\'19 and writers\u8217\'20\'19 unions as having \u8220\'20\'1Ca level of expectation that they have that is just not realistic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  previously reported that any new date for the Emmys would be contingent on a resolution to disputes between the studios and guilds before then.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/aug/02/george-clooney-meryl-streep-and-matt-damon-among-a-listers-donating-1m-to-help-striking-actors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than a dozen film stars}}}\uc2 , including Dwayne \u8220\'20\'1CThe Rock\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson, Meryl Streep, Leonardo DiCaprio and Nicole Kidman, have donated a combined US$15m to \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s emergency hardship fund to support actors who are struggling without work.\par \par \uc2 The Sag-Aftra Foundation president, Courtney B Vance, said they were dealing with \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than 30 times our usual number of applications for emergency aid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230810ej8a001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
