\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 Marvel VFX artists take first step toward unionisation amid Hollywood strikes\b0\par\par\uc2 Andrew Pulver \par \uc2 433 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par 11:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 During a wave of action by actors and writers, the comic-book film giant faces calls to remedy its \u8216\'20\'18toxic relationship\u8217\'20\'19 with technical artists\par \par \uc2 Visual effects artists working for Marvel have taken the first step towards unionisation in a notoriously poorly represented area of the film industry. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iatse.net/marvel-studios-vfx-workers-file-for-unprecedented-union-election-at-national-labor-relations-board/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to a statement}}}\uc2  from the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees (IATSE) a group of on-set VFX artists employed by the studio have filed a petition with the US\u8217\'20\'19s National Labor Relations Board.\par \par \uc2 Hailing the move as \u8220\'20\'1Ca major shift in an industry that has largely remained non-union since VFX was pioneered during production of the first Star Wars films in the 1970s\u8221\'20\'1D, the IATSE said a supermajority of Marvel\u8217\'20\'19s 50-plus VFX crew had signed authorisation cards indicating they wished to be represented by the union, which already represents around 168,000 technicians and craftspeople in live theatre, film and TV and associated areas in the US and Canada.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the IATSE\u8217\'20\'19s VFX organiser Mark Patch said: \u8220\'20\'1CFor almost half a century, workers in the visual effects industry have been denied the same protections and benefits their coworkers and crewmates have relied upon since the beginning of the Hollywood film industry. This is a historic first step for VFX workers coming together with a collective voice demanding respect for the work we do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The petition, which is the first step to creating union recognition for Marvel\u8217\'20\'19s VFX artists, applies only to \u8220\'20\'1Con-set\u8221\'20\'1D crew, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vulture.com/2023/08/vfx-workers-vote-to-unionize-at-marvel-for-the-first-time.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which includes}}}\uc2  data wranglers, production managers, witness camera operators, and assistants on both film and TV productions.\par \par \uc2 The move comes during a surge of concerted activism in the US screen industry, with both the writers\u8217\'20\'19 guild and actors\u8217\'20\'19 union Sag-Aftra on strike simultaneously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/jul/25/hollywood-strikes-ai-barbie-oppenheimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the first time since 1960}}}\uc2 . In August 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/aug/03/marvel-disney-visual-effects-artists-speak-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports emerged}}}\uc2  of widespread discontent among Marvel VFX artists, with one posting on social media that Marvel is \u8220\'20\'1Ca horrible client\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe issue is #Marvel is too big, and can demand whatever they want. It\u8217\'20\'19s a toxic relationship\u8221\'20\'1D. Complaints included that Marvel, which is owned by \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1C[orders] changes late in the process, far in excess of a typical client\u8221\'20\'1D, overworking and underpaying staff, with huge workloads including multiple versions of scenes created in parallel.\par \par \uc2 IATSE VFX coordinator Bella Huffman said: \u8220\'20\'1CTurnaround times don\u8217\'20\'19t apply to us, protected hours don\u8217\'20\'19t apply to us, and pay equity doesn\u8217\'20\'19t apply to us. Visual Effects must become a sustainable and safe department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230808ej88001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
