\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Taylor Swift urged to cancel LA shows in solidarity with striking hotel workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 424 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2023\par 08:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lieutenant governor among officials calling for postponement as thousands on strike demanding better pay and benefits\par \par \uc2 California officials are urging Taylor Swift to postpone her Los Angeles concerts and stand in solidarity with striking hotel workers.\par \par \uc2 Eleni Kounalakis\uc2 , California\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, as well as dozens of other state and local politicians asked the singer in an open letter to support the hotel workers\u8217\'20\'19 plight.\par \par \uc2 Swift\u8217\'20\'19s sold-out concerts are a boost for the region\u8217\'20\'19s hotels, the officials argue, with some properties \u8220\'20\'1Cdoubling and tripling what they charge because you are coming\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the letter said, many housekeepers and other hotel workers cannot afford to live close to their jobs and some sleep in their cars and risk losing their homes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHotel workers are fighting for their lives. They are fighting for a living wage. They have gone on strike. Now, they are asking for your support,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CStand with hotel workers and postpone your concerts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Starting Thursday, Swift is scheduled to perform six sold-out shows at the SoFi Stadium outside Los Angeles. Her representatives did not immediately respond to an email seeking comment on the letter.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of southern California hotel workers walked off the job in early July, demanding higher pay, better healthcare benefits, higher pension contributions and less strenuous workloads.\par \par \uc2 Since then, members of the \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 11 union, which represents thousands of hotel workers across the regions have picketed outside major hotels in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2  and Orange counties.\par \par \uc2 Workers reached a tentative deal with Westin Bonaventure before the contract expires at the end of June, but negotiations with other employers have failed to result in an agreement.\par \par \uc2 The union argues its members can no longer keep up with the cost of living in one of the most expensive regions in the country. \u8220\'20\'1COur members were devastated first by the pandemic, and now by the greed of their bosses,\u8221\'20\'1D Kurt Petersen, co-president of \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 11, said in a statement at the start of the strike. \u8220\'20\'1CThe industry got bailouts while we got cuts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kounalakis, a Democrat who said she will run for governor in 2026, is the top official in the state to make the plea. She attended Swift\u8217\'20\'19s Eras tour in Santa Clara, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 Others who signed the letter include the mayors of several cities, Isaac Bryan, the assembly majority leader, and state senators Dave Min and \uc2 Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Elena Durazo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230804ej840010f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
