\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US healthcare workers focus on pay and understaffing in fight for new contracts\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 927 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2023\par 12:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Over 85,000 workers hold pickets at 50 facilities across US as union contracts set to expire on 30 September\par \par \uc2 Unions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unioncoalition.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representing  }}}\uc2  more than 85,000 healthcare workers have held pickets at 50 facilities across California, Washington, Oregon and Colorado amid new contract negotiations as their current union contracts are set to expire on 30 September.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  are the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/providers/coalition-12-kaiser-permanente-unions-picketing-50-facilities-amid-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third largest set  }}}\uc2  of contract negotiations in the US in 2023, behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ups-teamsters-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 340,000 workers  }}}\uc2  at UPS who will be voting on a tentative agreement this month that was reached days before planned strike action, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-auto-bargaining/generalmotors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 150,000  }}}\uc2  autoworkers at Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  whose contracts are set to expire on 14 September.\par \par \uc2 The Coalition of \uc2 Kaiser Permanente Unions\uc2  represents workers in seven states and Washington DC. The coalition said that in a recent bargaining session, \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  represents workers in seven states and Washington DC. The coalition said that in a recent bargaining session, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unioncoalition.org/2023-session4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed  }}}\uc2  workers at the non-profit \u8220\'20\'1Cmake too much money\u8221\'20\'1D while the CEO is paid a salary of $16m a year.\par \par \uc2 Workers fighting for a new contract have criticized \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  over chronic understaffing, high workloads that worsened during the Covid-19 pandemic and lagging wages as the cost of living and inflation has risen substantially in recent years.\par \par \uc2 Trayvonne Ross, a senior food service worker at Zion medical center in San Diego, California, for three years, claimed his department was understaffed and had trouble retaining workers due to low pay and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://voiceofsandiego.org/2022/03/14/what-it-takes-to-survive-in-our-region/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high cost of living  }}}\uc2  in the area.\par \par \uc2 He said the understaffing affects patients who aren\u8217\'20\'19t able to receive their meals on time, often having to wait for hours while Ross and his co-workers have to do the work of two to three people to try to keep up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m struggling,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ross, who is applying for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, the federal food assistance program, for his family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCurrently, I live in just a one-bedroom apartment with me, my wife and three kids just to be able to live close to where I work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ross. \u8220\'20\'1CI know that Kaiser is making a whole lot of money and I think it\u8217\'20\'19s just very sad that not only me, but some of my co-workers, are having to ask for government assistance just so we can keep up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  is one of the largest healthcare providers in the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/fast-facts#:~:text=Our%20company,plans%2C%20serving%2012.7%20million%20members."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving  }}}\uc2  12.7 million members in California, Washington, Oregon, Georgia, Hawaii, Washington DC, Maryland and Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The non-profit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/providers/kaiser-permanente-bounces-back-12b-gain-09-operating-margin-q1-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported  }}}\uc2  a profit for the first quarter of 2023 of $1.2bn after reporting losses in 2022. Over the past five years, \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courthousenews.com/kaiser-permanente-union-workers-picket-at-health-care-facilities-across-the-west/#:~:text=The%20coalition%20says%20that%20despite,and%202022%20to%20%2458.9%20billion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported  }}}\uc2  over $21bn in profit, while paying 49 corporate executives at least $1m each annually.\par \par \uc2 Megan Mayes, a patient access representative at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in Portland, Oregon, for 17 years, said when Covid-19 hit, she and many of her co-workers were putting in 60 to 70 hours a week to help keep up with the high demand.\par \par \uc2 Despite those extra hours, she said, the high cost of living and inflation have made it difficult for Mayes and her family to make ends meet financially.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have three kids. The grocery bills are a lot. We don\u8217\'20\'19t go out to eat, we meal prep, and it\u8217\'20\'19s still not sustainable. My husband is a journeyman carpenter, has a union, works full-time and has worked overtime since the pandemic as well and we\u8217\'20\'19re always operating in a deficit every single month,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mayes. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  then telling me that I\u8217\'20\'19m overpaid? And what does that look like for bargaining when we\u8217\'20\'19re saying well, we\u8217\'20\'19re very clearly not and here\u8217\'20\'19s the numbers that support it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayes said that even with new job openings, the company can\u8217\'20\'19t get enough applicants because the pay is lagging and no longer competitive. The union is asking for a $ 25-an-hour wage floor for all positions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe used to have applicants lined up for blocks to get training just to be at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  and I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen this ever in my 17 years here where we can\u8217\'20\'19t even get one single applicant for a job,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CKaiser used to be the best, they were always the gold standard, and they\u8217\'20\'19re not any more. We\u8217\'20\'19re all asking Kaiser to do the right thing, invest in your employees, invest in the people who have stuck with you for years, through a global pandemic. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to start taking care of your employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement \uc2 Kaiser Permanente{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/labor-relations/kaiser-permanente-hiring-10000-new-staff-members-for-coalition-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided  }}}\uc2  the company said it had filled 6,500 coalition jobs this year as part of plans to hire 10,000 new workers and claimed average staff turnover is 8.5% compared with 21.4% for the healthcare industry as a whole.\par \par \uc2 In a separate statement, a \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  spokesperson dismissed picketing as an attempt by the unions to gain leverage in bargaining and disputed the union\u8217\'20\'19s complaints about wages. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/labor-relations/alliance-bargaining-updates/our-statement-on-coalition-picketing-july-24-to-29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement  }}}\uc2  added: \u8220\'20\'1COur priority is to reach an agreement that ensures we can continue to provide market-competitive pay and outstanding benefits. We are confident we\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to reach an agreement that strengthens our position as a best place to work and ensures that the high-quality care our members expect from us remains affordable and easy to access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230803ej83001jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
