\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re all in this together\u8217\'20\'19: New Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s film industry strikes in fight for survival\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell in Albuquerque \par \uc2 928 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2023\par 10:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Film industry\u8217\'20\'19s importance grows in state as record 109 productions filmed across New Mexico in 2022\par \par \uc2 On a sweltering Wednesday morning last week, hundreds of protesters gathered outside of \uc2 Netflix\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s studio in Albuquerque, New Mexico, in support of the American actors\u8217\'20\'19 union on strike.\par \par \uc2 The strike \u8211\'20\'13 hundreds of miles from Hollywood \u8211\'20\'13 is a sign of the growing importance of the film industry for the south-western state. Although it was barely 9am, the temperature was already hovering around 90F (32C). Still, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  was far from alone on the picket line: members of the writers, directors, crew and background actors guilds had all turned out in support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew Mexico has a very tight and strong film community and we\u8217\'20\'19re all in this together,\u8221\'20\'1D said Diane Villegas, an actor, the Sag-Aftra media liaison and a lifelong New Mexican.\par \par \uc2 Although the heart of movie productions in the United States remains in Hollywood, a growing number are filmed in New Mexico \u8211\'20\'13 where tax incentives and rebates have lured production companies over the past two decades.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, a record 109 productions were filmed across the state. And in a July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.state.nm.us/2023/07/18/film-and-television-industry-sets-record-breaking-wages-for-new-mexicans-communities-outside-of-albuquerque-santa-fe-see-150-increase-in-spending/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2 , Governor \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  announced that \u8220\'20\'1Cfilm, television and digital media production spending in New Mexico surpassed $2.2bn over the past three fiscal years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over the past two years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abqjournal.com/news/local/netflix-forging-ahead-with-expansion-in-nm/article_40a313a2-2c2a-5ff0-b88f-0b203a86b73f.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Netflix}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cabq.gov/economicdevelopment/news/nbc-universal-announces-major-albuquerque-production-studio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBCUniversal}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 both companies represented by the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ), against which \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  is striking \u8211\'20\'13 have significantly increased their presence in New Mexico. More than 1,100 Sag-Aftra members call New Mexico home, and many others have passed through the state to film movies, television shows and even video games, like \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2 , Logan and Iron Man 2. Breaking Bad, The Avengers and Stranger Things\u8217\'20\'19s season 4 were all produced in \uc2 Netflix\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Albuquerque studios.\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  on strike, production has paused on 18 major projects that were being filmed in New Mexico. (Work has continued on 12 projects not affected by the strike, according to the New Mexico Film Office.)\par \par \uc2 Actors say that the strike is vital \u8211\'20\'13 not only to ensure members\u8217\'20\'19 demands around fair wages and artificial intelligence are met, but also to protect the future of the film industry in New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Brendan Fehr moved to New Mexico about 12 years ago when he started acting in the NBC medical drama The Night Shift. He remembers that the film industry in the state was relatively small back then \u8211\'20\'13 the military and medical fields were much larger employers \u8211\'20\'13 but found it exciting to think about this new field that kids growing up in New Mexico might be able to enter. He hoped that it made a difference \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the young people and kids of New Mexico to have some home-grown talent to watch\u8221\'20\'1D. And, in one of the poorest states in the country, he imagined that the film industry \u8220\'20\'1Ccould really change lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Shylo Molina was one of those kids who grew up in New Mexico as the film industry was coming of age; he was born just a few years before Fehr moved to Albuquerque. Now 14 years old, Molina stars in The Really Loud House, a Nickelodeon comedy show produced in Albuquerque. \u8220\'20\'1CNew Mexico is becoming like the new LA,\u8221\'20\'1D said Molina. The strike feels important, he says, as a way to secure the work he hopes to continue in his future.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  members in New Mexico have found support in other unions, including the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees and the \uc2 Directors Guild of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the unions are supporting each other, and that\u8217\'20\'19s very New Mexico,\u8221\'20\'1D said Villegas.\par \par \uc2 George RR Martin, a longtime Santa Fe resident, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://georgerrmartin.com/notablog/2023/07/22/actors-join-the-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed his support for the strike in a post }}}\uc2  on his personal blog last week: \u8220\'20\'1CI joined the WGA in 1986 and have been through several strikes with them \u8230\'20\'26 this year\u8217\'20\'19s strike is the most important of my lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D Referencing Sag-Aftra president Fran Drescher\u8217\'20\'19s speech announcing the strike, Martin wrote, \u8220\'20\'1CNot much I can add to that, except \u8216\'20\'18AMEN\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://baanm.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Background Actors Association of New Mexico}}}\uc2  turned out at Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s picket as well. Background actors, or extras, face challenges in the evolving media landscape that \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  is trying to address in its negotiations around artificial intelligence, said Villegas. Many production companies have begun taking AI scans of actors, which \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  says makes them \u8220\'20\'1Cvulnerable to having most of their work replaced by digital replicas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAI will take away everyone\u8217\'20\'19s job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fehr. The film industry \u8220\'20\'1Cinjects millions and millions into the economy\u8221\'20\'1D that hires not just actors and writers, but carpenters, caterers, costume designers and electricians. But if films are artificially generated, he says, all those jobs go away.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.state.nm.us/2023/03/29/new-mexico-media-academy-announces-albuquerque-headquarters-at-rail-yards/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March press release}}}\uc2  from the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office, the film industry supports about 8,000 jobs across New Mexico. That same month, the governor announced the creation of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.state.nm.us/2023/03/29/new-mexico-media-academy-announces-albuquerque-headquarters-at-rail-yards/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Mexico Media Academy}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Ca collaborative workforce development initiative that will equip New Mexico residents with the advanced skills they need to work in the film and television industry\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUndoubtedly, the industry strikes impact film and television production activity and spend,\u8221\'20\'1D Amber Dodson, director of New Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s film office, said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CThat being said, we are hopeful that fair resolutions will be reached among the parties, and we expect a swift rebound at that point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230802ej820015u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
