\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US labor department condemns surge in child labor after teen dies on the job\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 511 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 July 2023\par 17:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Duvan Tomas Perez killed at slaughterhouse while department found 4,474 children working illegally since start of fiscal year\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  has decried a national surge in child labor as the agency has found thousands of violations and is currently investigating the death of a 16-year-old boy from Guatemala, Duvan Tomas Perez, who was killed on the job at a slaughterhouse this month in Mississippi, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/27/us/migrant-child-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two other 16-year-olds have died on the job in the US this year. Michael Schuls was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-boy-dies-sawmill-child-labor-8ae0c9fc09b9355dd7f12640eaefff2d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed}}}\uc2  on 29 June while working for a sawmill in Wisconsin. He was attempting to unjam a wood stacking machine when he was caught and pinned by the conveyor belt. Will Hampton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/towards-the-tragic-death-of-will-hampton?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=unknown&utm_campaign=comms_lmgs+towards-the-tragic-death-of-will-hampton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died}}}\uc2  in Missouri on 8 June while working at a landfill when he was pinned between a tractor trailer rig and its trailer.\par \par \uc2 The department has noted it is currently pursuing more than 700 open cases and already found 4,474 children working illegally since the beginning of the fiscal year, a 44% increase over the previous year.\par \par \uc2 On 25 July, the Department of Labor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230725-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  child labor violations found at 16 \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s franchises in Louisiana and Texas, affecting 83 minors.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s locations were found to have permitted 14- and 15-year-olds to work longer hours than legally permitted and perform job tasks that children under the age of 16 are prohibited from performing. The department assessed penalties against two franchise operators for the violations.\par \par \uc2 The investigation follows a May 2023 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230502-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement }}}\uc2  of child labor violations found at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s locations in four states involving over 300 children at 62 restaurant locations.\par \par \uc2 In February 2023, the Department of Labor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osec/osec20230227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  a new interagency taskforce to combat child labor exploitation amid recent surges in violations, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwi2y4_F9q6AAxUIlWoFHSuJAjkQFnoECA0QAw&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pbs.org%2Fnewshour%2Fpolitics%2Fsome-lawmakers-propose-loosening-child-labor-laws-to-fill-worker-shortage%23%3A~%3Atext%3DThe%2520Department%2520of%2520Labor%2520reported%2Callow%2520larger%2520fines%2520against%2520violators.&usg=AOvVaw1sF6e4qjG76n6nV-KobUNs&opi=89978449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  nearly a 70%}}}\uc2  increase in violations since 2018, and an influx of migrant children from Latin America without parents.\par \par \uc2 The update from the Department of Labor comes in the wake of increasing pressure from members of Congress for government agencies to address the increase in child labor violations.\par \par \uc2 During a hearing on Wednesday, congressional members questioned the health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , over surges in child labor, accusing the agency of failing to protect migrant children from exploitation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some terrible things that are wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D the California Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Anna Eshoo\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/business/2023/07/18/kildee-scholten-launch-task-force-to-combat-child-labor/70422895007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  a taskforce last week aimed to fight child labor amid recent surges in cases and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats-edworkforce.house.gov/imo/media/doc/ranking_member_scott_et_al_letter_to_gao_on_child_labor_violations.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Government Accountability Office\uc2  conduct an audit and investigation into the extent of the problem.\par \par \uc2 Bills introduced in Congress in April 2023 would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shrm.org/resourcesandtools/legal-and-compliance/employment-law/pages/child-labor-legislation.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase}}}\uc2  civil penalties against employers for child labor violations.\par \par \uc2 Amid a nationwide surge in child labor violations, Republican lawmakers in states such as Arkansas and Iowa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/iowa-governor-signs-one-of-the-most-dangerous-rollbacks-of-child-labor-laws-in-the-country-14-states-have-now-introduced-bills-putting-children-at-risk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  legislation earlier this year to scale back child labor laws, expanding the scope of work and hours of work 14- and 15-year-olds can perform.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230727ej7r001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
