\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Bryan Cranston leads actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike rally in New York: \u8216\'20\'18We will not allow you to take away our dignity\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Adrian Horton \par \uc2 988 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2023\par 17:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Award-winning actor led a starry event with a fiery speech aimed at \uc2 Disney\uc2  CEO \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 : \u8216\'20\'18We will not be having our jobs taken away and given to robots\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Stars abounded at the Sag-Aftra rally in Times Square on Tuesday, as Hollywood actors continue their simultaneous strike with writers.\par \par \uc2 Actors including Bryan Cranston, Christine Baranski, F Murray Abraham, Wendell Pierce, Steve Buscemi, Christian Slater and Tituss Burgess spoke before a crowd at the \u8220\'20\'1CRock the City for a Fair Contract\u8221\'20\'1D rally, with numerous others \u8211\'20\'13 Michael Shannon, BD Wong, Brendan Fraser, Jessica Chastain, Matt Bomer, Corey Stoll and Chlo\u235\'00\'EB Grace Moretz \u8211\'20\'13 demonstrating their support on stage.\par \par \uc2 Cranston delivered a particularly fiery speech that included a message to the \uc2 Disney\uc2  chief, \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/jul/13/disney-bob-iger-actors-writers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the strikes \u8220\'20\'1Cvery disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D and said actors and writers were not being \u8220\'20\'1Crealistic\u8221\'20\'1D with their expectations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a message for Mr Iger,\u8221\'20\'1D the Breaking Bad and former Malcolm in the Middle star said. \u8220\'20\'1CI know, sir, that you look [at] things through a different lens. We don\u8217\'20\'19t expect you to understand who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we ask you to hear us, and beyond that to listen to us when we tell you we will not be having our jobs taken away and given to robots,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, referring to concerns around the studios\u8217\'20\'19 use of AI, which has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jul/22/sag-aftra-wga-strike-artificial-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major sticking point in negotiations}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ). \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not have you take away our right to work and earn a decent living. And lastly, and most importantly, we will not allow you to take away our dignity!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cranston began his remarks by noting one thing the guilds and \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  could agree on: \u8220\'20\'1COur industry has changed exponentially.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not in the same business model we were even 10 years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd yet, even though they admit that is the truth in today\u8217\'20\'19s economy, they are fighting us tooth and nail to stick to the same economic system that is outmoded, outdated! They want us to step back in time. We cannot and we will not do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baranski spoke \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonally\u8221\'20\'1D from her experience as a \u8220\'20\'1Cworking actor\u8221\'20\'1D as well as for the background and guest actors from her 13 years playing a lawyer on two shows \u8211\'20\'13 The Good Wife, on \uc2 CBS\uc2 , and The Good Fight, on \uc2 CBS\uc2  All Access and Paramount Plus. (Streaming platforms such as Paramount Plus pay much less in residuals than traditional networks, which is a major point of contention in negotiations.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn both shows, I consider these actors my colleagues and part of our creative family. Their contribution to the series\u8217\'20\'19 success was indispensable, and I am here today speaking on their behalf,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need fair and decent compensation, healthcare, retirement benefits and above all, respect and recognition for their contribution.\u8221\'20\'1D Baranski also called on executives with salaries in the millions to \u8220\'20\'1Cshare the wealth\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not live under corporate feudalism,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time, it is just simply time to make things right. Our contribution will not be undervalued, and we will not be robbed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Bear star Liza Col\u243\'00\'F3n-Zayas, who said she had been a Sag member since 1994, echoed many others in noting that her residuals had \u8220\'20\'1Cdwindled exponentially\u8221\'20\'1D and quoted Snoop Dogg: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere the fuck is my money?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abraham, most recently nominated for an Emmy for the second season of The White Lotus, put the importance of the actors\u8217\'20\'19 union bluntly: \u8220\'20\'1CWithout a union, there is no middle class. Without a middle class, there is no democracy. Unions are good for America,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery worker in this country should have these same benefits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Slater, star of Heathers and Mr Robot, touched on how the Sag union took care of his father when he struggled with mental illness toward the end of his life. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people gave up on him,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHis union never gave up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arguably the most passionate speech came from Duncan Crabtree-Ireland, Sag-Aftra\u8217\'20\'19s national executive director and chief negotiator, who spoke about the response from \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  negotiators during the final days before a strike was called on 14 July. Crabtree-Ireland said that when he and the Sag-Aftra president, Fran Drescher, spoke to three studio CEOs on the final day of bargaining in May, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe said: \u8216\'20\'18Here\u8217\'20\'19s all you have to do to make sure there\u8217\'20\'19s no strike. All you have to do is make this fair deal.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd their response was, \u8216\'20\'18No.\u8217\'20\'19 Just like their response to so many of our proposals that we\u8217\'20\'19ve said are essential for actors being treated in a respectful and fair way,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CDo actors get to have minimum wage increases that keep up with inflation? \u8216\'20\'18No.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo actors get to have a share of the streaming revenue that has been created because of their faces and their voices on these new platforms, these new businesses these companies are creating? \u8216\'20\'18No. We don\u8217\'20\'19t even want to talk about it.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre they willing to give actors true informed consent about the use of their own face, voice, body, likeness in the creation of artificial intelligence digital doubles of them? \u8216\'20\'18No.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike, he said, was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe result of big corporations that refuse to treat our members fairly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd until these companies come to the table and make a fair and respectful deal,\u8221\'20\'1D he later added, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are going to continue to be on the strike lines, we are going to continue to say \u8216\'20\'18No\u8217\'20\'19 to an unfair abuse of their power in trying to coerce us into accepting something that\u8217\'20\'19s wrong. There comes a time when you have to stand up for what\u8217\'20\'19s right, and that time is now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230725ej7p002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
