\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  slashes more than a third of staff as campaign flounders\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2023\par 19:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida governor and Republican presidential hopeful cuts 38 jobs, including two senior advisers\par \par \uc2 On a day on which he emerged uninjured from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ron-desantis-car-accident-presidential-campaign-florida-tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an actual car crash}}}\uc2  in Tennessee, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/25/desantis-lets-go-of-more-than-1-3-of-campaign-staff-as-reset-continues-00108046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  to have made his most drastic attempt yet to turn round a presidential campaign seen as in danger of coming off the road itself, announcing a deep slashing of staff numbers.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/25/desantis-lets-go-of-more-than-1-3-of-campaign-staff-as-reset-continues-00108046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  advisers to the Florida governor confirmed that more than a third of campaign staff were being cut, \u8220\'20\'1Ca total of 38 jobs shed across an array of departments\u8221\'20\'1D, two senior advisers among them.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, Generra Peck, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/25/desantis-lets-go-of-more-than-1-3-of-campaign-staff-as-reset-continues-00108046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing a top-to-bottom review of our organisation, we have taken additional, aggressive steps to streamline operations and put \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in the strongest position to win this primary and defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor DeSantis is going to lead the Great American Comeback and we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to hit the ground running as we head into an important month of the campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the first Republican debate a month away, DeSantis is still clearly the strongest challenger to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the former president enjoys {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national and key-state polling leads}}}\uc2  of about 30 points, regardless of the 71 criminal charges against him and the prospect of more.\par \par \uc2 No other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/mitt-romney-republican-candidates-trump-2024-withdraw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 candidate in the 13-strong field}}}\uc2  has made a significant move but DeSantis is widely held to be floundering, with donor sources maxed out and his policy proposals, often to the right even of Trump, falling flat with the public.\par \par \uc2 Politico also reported new hires including a \u8220\'20\'1Ctop political adviser\u8221\'20\'1D to the Georgia governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , a rising party figure who some Republican operatives have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/politics-blog/the-jolt-draft-kemp-chatter-begins-as-trump-dominates-gop-field/PXBSP47QTBALFECK4JMCV2ER4Y/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  could yet enter the primary.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/07/ron-desantis-reset-reboot-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 For Vanity Fair}}}\uc2 , the columnist Molly Jong-Fast gave voice to progressive glee over DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s struggles to connect with Republican voters.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/07/ron-desantis-reset-reboot-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jong-Fast wrote}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cis a terrible politician with negative charisma, and the chances of him riding into the White House are looking less likely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is aggressively dull and wooden, making his interactions with voters border on painful to watch. His head bobs in a strange and unnatural way, and he wears high-heeled cowboy boots.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referring to a previous high-profile Republican flop, the Wisconsin governor who wilted before Trump in 2016, Jong-Fast said DeSantis \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes Scott Walker look charming\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlus,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cvoters tend not to vote for people who seem like they\u8217\'20\'19re screaming at them all the time. No amount of donor dollars can make DeSantis, a Maga marionette traipsing across Iowa and New Hampshire, seem like a real human boy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230725ej7p002jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
