\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 Dwayne Johnson donates \u8216\'20\'18historic\u8217\'20\'19 amount of money to US actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike foundation\b0\par\par\uc2 Andrew Pulver \par \uc2 290 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2023\par 11:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The star of the Fast and Furious franchise has made a seven-figure donation to a Sag-Aftra Foundation Relief Fund, for actors who will face \u8216\'20\'18financial ruin\u8217\'20\'19 due to the strike in Hollywood\par \par \uc2 Dwayne Johnson, star of Black Adam and the Fast and Furious franchise, has made a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor, historic\u8221\'20\'1D financial contribution to the Sag-Aftra Foundation Relief Fund, which provides emergency assistance to union members during strike action.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/dwayne-johnson-donation-sag-aftra-foundation-strike-relief-fund-1235678671"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to a report in Variety}}}\uc2 , Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cseven-figure donation\u8221\'20\'1D arrived in response to a letter sent by the foundation\u8217\'20\'19s president Courtney B Vance to 2,700 of the highest-earning actors in the film industry.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s executive director Cyd Wilson said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the largest single donation that we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever received from one individual at one time. And what is amazing is that that one cheque is going to help thousands of actors keep food on their table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance added: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to thank Dwayne for his tremendous generosity, compassion, and initiative to step up in this significant and meaningful way for our community. On behalf of the thousands who will be helped by his historic donation, thank you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Sag-Aftra Foundation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sagaftra.foundation/about/history/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 originally established in 1985}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2 , is a non-profit organisation running a variety of assistance programmes for union members. Wilson said many \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  members face \u8220\'20\'1Cfinancial ruin\u8221\'20\'1D during the strike, and that even before the strike began the foundation was receiving \u8220\'20\'1Cfive to 10 times [the number of requests for financial aid] that we would normally process in a week and [we] think that is going to continue to increase\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230725ej7p001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
