\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 We last raised the US federal minimum wage 14 years ago. This is unacceptable\b0\par\par\uc2 William J Barber and A Kazimir Brown \par \uc2 948 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2023\par 18:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The minimum has been an unlivable $7.25 an hour under three presidents. Today\u8217\'20\'19s wage is worth less than at any point since 1956\par \par \uc2 Researchers at the \uc2 University of California-Riverside\uc2  recently released a study showing poverty is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bradydave.files.wordpress.com/2023/04/bradyetal_preprint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fourth leading cause of death}}}\uc2  nationwide. Poverty kills more people than homicide, respiratory disease, gun violence and opioid overdoses, the study showed.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s stress, it\u8217\'20\'19s starvation, it\u8217\'20\'19s disease. And it\u8217\'20\'19s all unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers have many tools to counter the death by poverty that is ravaging America. But they have neglected the simplest one in their toolkit for far too long: raising the federal minimum wage. Monday marks 14 years since the last federal minimum wage increase, the longest period America\u8217\'20\'19s lowest-paid workers have gone without a raise since the minimum wage was first put into effect in 1938.\par \par \uc2 The minimum wage has been stuck at an unlivable $7.25 an hour under three presidents. Adjusting for inflation, today\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage is now worth less than at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/the-value-of-the-federal-minimum-wage-is-at-its-lowest-point-in-66-years/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 any point since 1956}}}\uc2 . Nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ips-dc.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/2023-National-Fact-Sheet-8.5-%C3%97-11-in-4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a third of the workforce}}}\uc2 , or 52 million people, earn less than $15 an hour, including 47% of Black workers, 46% of Hispanic workers, 20% of Asian American and Indigenous workers, 40% of working women and 50% of working women of color. Raising the minimum wage to even $15 an hour would lift 7.6 million people \u8211\'20\'13 many of whom are women, immigrants, Black, Latinx or parents \u8211\'20\'13 out of poverty and give more than 50 million people a raise.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/the-value-of-the-federal-minimum-wage-is-at-its-lowest-point-in-66-years/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economic Policy Institute}}}\uc2 , a worker paid the $7.25 federal minimum wage earns 27.4% less in inflation-adjusted terms than what their counterpart was paid in July 2009 when the minimum wage was last increased, and 40.2% less than a minimum wage worker in February 1968, the historical high point of the minimum wage\u8217\'20\'19s value.\par \par \uc2 Courageous workers in the Fight for $15 and the union movement have pushed 14 states and the District of Columbia to adopt $15 minimum wage laws. We\u8217\'20\'19re proud to have marched with, prayed with, and even gotten arrested with these workers as they\u8217\'20\'19ve demanded living wages and a union. But the sad fact is that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.masslive.com/news/2022/11/these-states-use-the-federal-minimum-wage-of-725-per-hour.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20 states remain stuck at the federal minimum}}}\uc2  of $7.25 \u8211\'20\'13 and working people in those states, the majority of which are in the south, need help now. That\u8217\'20\'19s why, earlier this year, we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ncnewsline.com/2023/06/02/bernie-sanders-rev-william-barber-charge-north-carolina-activists-to-fight-for-livable-wages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit the road}}}\uc2  with Bernie Sanders and stood alongside workers across the south to demand living wages.\par \par \uc2 These workers are 46% more likely to be paid less than $15 than workers in the 30-plus states with minimums higher than $7.25, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/workers-are-46-more-likely-to-make-below-15-an-hour-in-states-paying-only-the-federal-minimum-wage/#:~:text=and%20Dave%20Kamper-,Workers%20are%2046%25%20more%20likely%20to%20make%20below%20%2415%20an,hardships%20of%20low%2Dwage%20workers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economic Policy Institute}}}\uc2 . And, according to EPI, there isn\u8217\'20\'19t a place in the country where even a single adult without children can get by on less than $15 an hour. There\u8217\'20\'19s no city, county or state where a full-time minimum-wage worker can afford a two-bedroom rental, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nlihc.org/sites/default/files/oor/2021/Out-of-Reach_2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 National Low Income Housing Coalition\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 Yet instead of raising pay for fast-food cooks, home care aides, warehouse workers, retail clerks and others, politicians push a false moral narrative of religious nationalism, trying to trick us into believing that poverty is a moral failing on the individual and that the real moral issues of our time are standing against LGBTQ+ people and a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose while defending tax cuts and gun rights.\par \par \uc2 We will not be duped: the real moral question for our country is where we stand in relation to the poor. Instead of pushing culture wars and partisanship, lawmakers should focus on the 800 people dying each day from poverty in the wealthiest nation on earth. Our politicians have failed to act, and leaders who stand silent in the face of these injustices are guilty of policy murder.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, our demand for a living wage is the moral issue politicians should be focused on. Isaiah 10 says, \u8220\'20\'1CWoe unto those who legislate evil and rob the poor of their rights, and make women and children their prey.\u8221\'20\'1D And President \uc2 Franklin D Roosevelt\uc2  adopted the moral argument of the Social Gospel when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://docs.fdrlibrary.marist.edu/odnirast.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cno business which depends for its existence on paying less than living wages to its workers has any right to continue in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D It is a moral travesty that as a nation we continue to expand the military budget in surplus, but refuse to guarantee basic human rights like healthcare and living wages.\par \par \uc2 We are putting our nation\u8217\'20\'19s leaders on notice, across party lines, that we need living wages now. If they don\u8217\'20\'19t act, we\u8217\'20\'19ll vote them out. Poor and low-wealth people make up nearly 40% of the electorate and have the ability to decide elections. We are calling for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.poorpeoplescampaign.org/join-us-as-we-build-the-third-reconstruction/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Third Reconstruction}}}\uc2  to lift our nation\u8217\'20\'19s 140 million poor and low-wealth people from the bottom up. This includes raising the outdated minimum wage to a living wage as well as updating the also-obsolete official poverty measure to reflect what it takes to secure a decent standard of living today.\par \par \uc2 America has gone 14 years without a raise. It\u8217\'20\'19s literally killing us. And it\u8217\'20\'19s time for it to change.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Rev D William J Barber II is founding director of the Center for Public Theology and Public Policy at Yale Divinity School\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Rev A Kazimir Brown is executive director of Repairers of the Breach\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230724ej7o0010g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
