\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They\u8217\'20\'19re fired up\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president on looming UPS strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2023\par 17:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien could be leading his union in one of the biggest \u8211\'20\'13 and costliest \u8211\'20\'13 strike at a single private employer in US history\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien has a long family legacy at the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 : his great-grandfather, grandfather and father were all Teamster union members in Boston. O\u8217\'20\'19Brien joined the union after dropping out of college at age 19 to haul equipment on construction sites in 1991. Thirty-two years later, he is on the verge of leading the union in one of the biggest \u8211\'20\'13 and costliest \u8211\'20\'13 strikes at a single private employer in US history.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have 1.2 million members, making it one of the largest unions in the world. Its membership is diverse, ranging from police to bakers, but it is most famous for representing freight drivers and warehouse workers. The shipping and logistics giant UPS is the single largest employer in the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, the Teamster\u8217\'20\'19s general president, the contract negotiations between the two have become a test case for a union giant that is flexing its muscles after corporations have stonewalled nascent labor movements at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  with long delays toward a first contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to set the tone \u8211\'20\'13 and we have \u8211\'20\'13 for how organized labor should deal with corporate America, with politicians, and how they should stand up and fight. We will set the example through this situation with UPS whether we get a deal or if UPS chooses not to do the right thing to strike themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien.\par \par \uc2 We are going to set the tone for how organized labor should deal with corporate America\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\par \par \uc2 UPS\u8217\'20\'19s 340,000 workers have authorized industrial action unless the two sides can agree on a new contract by the end of July. Talks have broken down and the US faces its largest strike since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1983/08/29/us/telephone-workers-begin-returning-from-strike.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 675,000 telephone workers}}}\uc2  walked off the job in 1983 \u8211\'20\'13 a strike that could cause chaos in a country still feeling the after-effects of the pandemic\u8217\'20\'19s supply chain crisis.\par \par \uc2 Economic estimates of a UPS strike\u8217\'20\'19s impact suggest it could be the costliest in at least a century, with an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.andersoneconomicgroup.com/potential-ups-strike-could-be-costliest-in-a-century/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated $7bn}}}\uc2  in losses for a 10-day work stoppage. Consumers reliant on home deliveries, medical supplies and business inventory will all be hit. But O\u8217\'20\'19Brien argued the responsibility for the effects of a strike on the public falls on UPS \u8211\'20\'13 and that other corporations should take note.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUPS knows what our members\u8217\'20\'19 wants, needs and demands are, and if there is a labor strike over this, I want to be clear: the public should know this and everybody else should know that UPS will be striking. They know what our members want. They know what our members deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The looming strike could lead off a summer of labor unrest in the US as thousands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/02/southern-california-hotel-workers-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hotel workers in California}}}\uc2 , TV and film writers, and most recently, thousands of TV and film actors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/jul/15/actors-writer-strike-stop-hollywood-what-movies-tv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked off the job}}}\uc2 . Additionally, 150,000 autoworkers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/oh/columbus/business/2023/07/12/uaw-are-prepared-to-strike-big-three-detroit-automakers-as-contract-talks-begin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prepping }}}\uc2  for a possible huge strike in the fall in the lead-up to new contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien had a meteoric rise at the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 . He was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.massport.com/massport/about-massport/leadership/board-executive-staff/sean-m-o-brien/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected}}}\uc2  president/principal officer of Local 25 in 2006 at the age of 34, the youngest to achieve that feat, and became eastern region vice-president of Teamsters International in 2011. But his career was almost derailed after a clash with \uc2 James Hoffa\uc2 , the longtime \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president and son of the notorious \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  boss and mafia associate \uc2 Jimmy Hoffa\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien had been the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 top negotiator with UPS during its union contract negotiations for 2018. But Hoffa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ttnews.com/articles/obrien-fired-top-teamsters-negotiator-ups-contract-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  him in 2017 after only six months in a move some saw as political payback for his championing of \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  members who had not supported Hoffa in his last presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 allegations that Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s supporters denied.\par \par \uc2 Discontent with the past UPS contract catalyzed a changing of the guard among the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 leadership. The following union leadership election in 2021 was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/hoffa-teamsters-for-a-democratic-union-reform-labor-militancy-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time}}}\uc2  in 25 years that \uc2 James Hoffa\uc2  was not on the ballot. O\u8217\'20\'19Brien ran for president of the union and won by a landslide after campaigning on taking a more aggressive approach toward UPS and new organizing efforts at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had weak leadership in the past administration, and we just wanted to make certain that we enrolled our members to fight for what is right and just,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien. \u8220\'20\'1CThe previous administration didn\u8217\'20\'19t have its members\u8217\'20\'19 best interests at hand and that\u8217\'20\'19s when I made my decision to run for general president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since assuming leadership of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , O\u8217\'20\'19Brien has taken a more aggressive approach toward anti-union animus from corporations and politicians. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are trying to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which has successfully fought grassroots labor movements {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/apr/08/long-fight-organize-us-workers-amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to a standstill.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CYou have an employer like \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  taking a joyride into space, and he bangs on his workers to be able to fund his trip,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/02/teamsters-president-sean-obrien-amazon-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year.}}}\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been shy in taking on Washington DC either. During a Senate hearing in March 2023, \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2 , a Republican senator from Oklahoma, got into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/09/republican-senator-teamsters-boss-markwayne-mullin-sean-obrien-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heated argument}}}\uc2  with O\u8217\'20\'19Brien over the senator\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to union organizing. Mullin called the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  boss a \u8220\'20\'1Cloudmouth bully\u8221\'20\'1D and challenged O\u8217\'20\'19Brien to a charity mixed martial arts cage match. \u8220\'20\'1CAnyplace, Anytime cowboy,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien replied on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a juvenile delinquent, he has a big ego and a small mind. He\u8217\'20\'19s one of 100 people in this country who should be setting an example, and unfortunately, he wants to be a schoolyard bully, and that\u8217\'20\'19s OK, at some point in time that will be addressed. But the cage fight I\u8217\'20\'19m more focused on right now is the cage fight on behalf of 340,000 members at UPS,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien.\par \par \uc2 Greedy CEO who pretends like he\u8217\'20\'19s self made. In reality, just a clown & fraud. Always has been, always will be. Quit the tough guy act in these senate hearings. You know where to find me. Anyplace, Anytime cowboy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/LittleManSyndrome?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #LittleManSyndrome}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JNvT7IsA6m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JNvT7IsA6m}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Sean M. O'Brien (@TeamsterSOB) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamsterSOB/status/1671556346246725638?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 As the 31 July deadline for a deal approaches, UPS workers around the US have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wlbt.com/2023/07/11/local-ups-employees-conduct-practice-runs-picket-line/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  practice pickets and rallies to highlight demands of the workforce and prepare for a possible strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re fired up, but most importantly they\u8217\'20\'19re fed up,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien. \u8220\'20\'1CTo say the least, it\u8217\'20\'19s one of the most impressive campaigns I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been involved in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union has secured {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freightwaves.com/news/ups-agrees-to-install-air-conditioning-in-package-cars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreements}}}\uc2  with UPS on some significant issues such as installing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/ups-drivers-union-heat-temperatures-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 air conditioners in delivery vehicles}}}\uc2 , but the union and UPS are still far apart on economic issues.\par \par \uc2 On 5 July, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  were in negotiations with UPS, pushing for higher wages for part-time employees, higher wages for new hires, higher wages for full-timers, an increase in more full-time jobs, and protecting and improving pensions and healthcare benefits. O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said about 95% of the contract was resolved when UPS walked away from the negotiating table, claiming it had nothing left to give.\par \par \uc2 UPS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsandtribune.com/news/a-strike-is-imminent-for-ups-union-members-heres-what-it-could-mean-for-national/article_21d9f176-2028-11ee-9313-975cbc78c472.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the union of walking away from the negotiating table. \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain focused on reaching an agreement with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  that is a win for UPS employees, our customers, our union, and our company before Aug 1. While we have made great progress and are close to reaching an agreement, we have a responsibility as an essential service provider to take steps to help ensure we can deliver our customers\u8217\'20\'19 packages if the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  choose to strike,\u8221\'20\'1D a UPS spokesperson said in a recent statement announcing that the company is currently training managers for business continuity plans if a strike occurs.\par \par \uc2 Talks are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/19/ups-workers-strike-teamsters-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back on}}}\uc2 , but as 1 August approaches, the issues remain.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said that UPS had reported record profits during the course of the current five-year contract, reaching a record $100bn in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/01/31/investing/ups-earnings/index.html#:~:text=UPS%20reports%20record%20profit%20but%20forecasts%20a%20slower%202023&text=UPS%20reported%20a%20record%20profit,since%20its%20founding%20in%201907."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revenue}}}\uc2  in 2022 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/business/ups-profit-soared-above-10b-in-21-sees-revenue-topping-100b-in-22/2H5Q5CCQ5RBFLKRDLGYLTTZNCM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  profits of $12.89bn in 2021 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investors.ups.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/2087/ups-releases-4q-2022-earnings#:~:text=Full%2DYear%202022%20Consolidated%20Results&text=Operating%20profit%20of%20%2413.1%20billion,on%20invested%20capital%20was%2031.3%25."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $13bn }}}\uc2  in 2022. With the recent strike threat looming, UPS has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-07-11/ups-will-post-earnings-later-than-usual-as-labor-deadline-looms#xj4y7vzkg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed}}}\uc2  back its second quarter earnings date to 8 August, the latest date it has ever posted mid-year earnings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat answer is unacceptable on behalf of our members, especially when you made $100bn and everyone else that didn\u8217\'20\'19t touch a package, didn\u8217\'20\'19t deliver a package especially during the pandemic, got rewarded with very, very lucrative stock options provided to upper management in the hundreds of millions of dollars, investors got paid dividends at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://seekingalpha.com/article/4592333-ups-may-be-boring-but-dividend-growth-immense"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50%}}}\uc2  higher than they were in January 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the while, everybody that touched and forwarded packages and provided goods and services to this company have yet to be rewarded and they just want our piece of the pie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230724ej7o00132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
