\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 Hollywood A-listers to quit British chatshows as US actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike hits\b0\par\par\uc2 Tara Conlan \par \uc2 777 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 July 2023\par 07:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ban on US stars promoting their new movies will force producers to use more homegrown guests\par \par \uc2 British chatshows are set to feature more homegrown stars in the wake of the US actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/jul/14/the-hollywood-actors-strike-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted filming on Hollywood blockbusters}}}\uc2  and TV dramas.\par \par \uc2 Producers on some of TV\u8217\'20\'19s biggest talk and daily magazine shows face a headache as actors follow in the footsteps of the cast of \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/video/2023/jul/14/hollywood-actors-walk-out-of-oppenheimer-premiere-as-strike-action-starts-video-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who walked out of its premiere}}}\uc2  when the strike began earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Stars promoting films are a regular feature of the chatshow circuit, with series such as \uc2 ITV\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s This Morning and BBC One\u8217\'20\'19s The Graham Norton Show, which airs in the autumn, renowned for attracting Hollywood A-listers \u8211\'20\'13 but the knock-on effect of the strike is being felt across British television.\par \par \uc2 One producer of a well-known show told the Observer : \u8220\'20\'1CWe are lucky as we had already filmed a couple of movie stars. Fortunately we have enough domestic stars to use and will use more of them.\u8221\'20\'1D Another on a popular chatshow said they would use \u8220\'20\'1Cmore homegrown celebrities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Screen Actors Guild-American Federation of Television and Radio Artists\uc2  (Sag-Aftra) began the industrial action, following a similar strike by writers, in a protest over pay and the use of AI to replicate voices.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s UK counterpart, Equity, is not taking part but some British actors, such as \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2  star Emily Blunt, are Sag-Aftra members. Some have Equity contracts, but are working on films that have been shut down due to US colleagues striking, such as an adaptation of the musical Wicked.\par \par \uc2 The issue has led to some confusion among British actors who are questioning whether they should publicise shows made for US-owned companies such as \uc2 Netflix\uc2  or Channel 5 owner Paramount.\par \par \uc2 Fraser Ayres, actor, writer and creator of \uc2 ITV\uc2  panel show Sorry, I Didn\u8217\'20\'19t Know, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think there are quite a few confused people out there who want to show solidarity and don\u8217\'20\'19t want to jeopardise their future. I\u8217\'20\'19m for the strikes. AI is a big thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Showbiz agent Jonathan Shalit, chairman of InterTalent, said actors were being cautious because they did not want to be labelled \u8220\'20\'1Cscabs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe wealthy can see through these strikes because they\u8217\'20\'19ve got savings, but \u8230\'20\'26 in the short term it\u8217\'20\'19s devastating for a lot of people and I suspect some will exit the industry. But people understand it\u8217\'20\'19s short-term pain for long-term gain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a scary time for everyone, including producers, with budgets going down and costs going up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Channel 4\u8217\'20\'19s The Lateish Show with Mo Gilligan has just finished filming, with stars including Jennifer Lawrence. Ben Wicks at production company Expectation said they \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not have got [them] if we were making that series this month, it would have a big effect\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wicks also oversees Channel 4\u8217\'20\'19s daytime chatshow Steph\u8217\'20\'19s Packed Lunch, which returns in September, and said the strike \u8220\'20\'1Cwill definitely affect it \u8230\'20\'26we\u8217\'20\'19ve [previously] had an impressive array of American talent on the show\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said, \u8220\'20\'1Cobviously it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame\u8221\'20\'1D but added \u8220\'20\'1Cthere are plenty of other people promoting things\u8221\'20\'1D and the Leeds-based series covers other subjects such as consumer issues, fashion and cookery.\par \par \uc2 In the US chatshows have been cancelled due to the strikes and Wicks said that an unintended consequence, if the action spread to the UK, could be an impact on diversity and working-class people being able to afford to work in TV.\par \par \uc2 Steph\u8217\'20\'19s Packed Lunch is filmed in Leeds and has boosted the city\u8217\'20\'19s economy, working with local colleges to ensure its team of more than 80 is made up of people from different backgrounds, which Wicks said brings a \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversity of stories that reflect the diversity of life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ayres, who also runs diversity company D and I, agreed: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about the wider picture and also talking about how actors and writers in the UK are usually paid less than in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Fleming, Equity\u8217\'20\'19s general secretary, predicted Sag-Aftra would win and said Equity had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.equity.org.uk/solidarity-statement-advice-regarding-sag-aftra-industrial-action-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued guidance}}}\uc2  to its members.\par \par \uc2 He told the Observer the union was \u8220\'20\'1Calive to the possibility that some projects will be recast\u8221\'20\'1D using British actors by studios looking to bypass the US strike. That, he warned, could prompt a UK strike as it \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be something we could look at taking action over\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The BBC declined to comment on the effect of the strikes on The Graham Norton Show.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230726ej7n002bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
