\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 US actors\u8217\'20\'19 union grants 39 film and TV productions exemption from strike action as UK and Australian works halted\b0\par\par\uc2 Kelly Burke \par \uc2 555 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2023\par 19:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 230 local actors and crew stood down at Village Roadshow Studios on the Gold Coast amid \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  and WGA industrial actionGet our weekend culture and lifestyle email\par \par \uc2 David Lowery\u8217\'20\'19s indie film Mother Mary and the television biopic The Chosen are among the 39 productions that have so far received the US actors\u8217\'20\'19 union\u8217\'20\'19s blessing to resume shooting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/jul/18/hollywood-stars-actors-strike-sag-aftra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite the ongoing strike}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 American actors walked off sets around the world at 5.01pm AEST last Friday, after a breakdown in negotiations between the Screen Actors Guild \u8211\'20\'13 American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (\uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 ) and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The strike is having global ramifications.\par \par \uc2 In the UK, the production of Wicked, starring Ariana Grande, has been shut down. Beetlejuice and Deadpool 3 are also reported to be significantly affected.\par \par \uc2 In Australia, about 150 local actors and crew have been stood down from the production of Mortal Kombat 2 and a further 80 Australian workers have been stood down from Universal Studio\u8217\'20\'19s film adaptation of Liane Moriarty\u8217\'20\'19s novel Apples Never Fall, after their US counterparts stopped work. Both productions were being filmed at Village Roadshow Studios on the Gold Coast.\par \par \uc2 The 24 August release of Australian film Force of Nature: the Dry 2 has been rescheduled \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil the actors are able to support the launch\u8221\'20\'1D, with the film\u8217\'20\'19s co-producer and star Eric Bana \u8211\'20\'13 a \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  member \u8211\'20\'13 saying the decision was made \u8220\'20\'1Cwith some regret, but a large amount of conviction... I stand in support of the changes that \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  are fighting for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/newsletters/2019/oct/18/saved-for-later-sign-up-for-guardian-australias-culture-and-lifestyle-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for the fun stuff with our rundown of must-reads, pop culture and tips for the weekend, every Saturday morning}}}\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, film industry publications Deadline and Variety both reported that US actors engaged by independent production companies not affiliated with the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  had been given the green light to resume work.\par \par \uc2 Two of the productions granted the waiver are the work of A24, the independent production company behind the Academy Award-winning films Everything Everywhere All At Once and Moonlight.\par \par \uc2 Mother Mary, starring Anne Hathaway and Michaela Coel, has been granted approval by the union to resume shooting, and Death of a Unicorn, starring Paul Rudd and Jenna Ortega, is now back on schedule to begin shooting in Hungary shortly.\par \par \uc2 The television biopic about the life of Jesus, The Chosen, and the crime thriller The Rivals of Amziah King, starring Matthew McConaughey, are among the 39 productions exempt from industrial action, on the proviso the independent production companies agree to the terms of whatever offer is finally agreed to by the union and the Hollywood studios.\par \par \uc2 The industrial action has caused upheaval in Hollywood, already reeling from the ongoing Writers Guild of America strike, now into its third month.\par \par \uc2 It is the first joint strike by the two unions in more than 60 years, with the issues of residuals from streaming services and the possible threat to jobs from artificial intelligence the main areas of dispute.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The caption to the top picture was amended on 20 July 2023 because an earlier version referred to the Canadian actor Tatiana Maslany as a US actor.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230719ej7j000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
