\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Chicago aims to boost pay for thousands of restaurant workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Leigh Giangreco in Chicago \par \uc2 905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2023\par 16:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Advocates hail potential for \u8216\'20\'18historic moment\u8217\'20\'19 as city council bill bids to increase pay from $9.48 an hour for tipped employees\par \par \uc2 The latest battle to raise the minimum wage for workers who rely on tips is set to kick off on Wednesday in Chicago with a bill being introduced in the city council that will boost pay \u8211\'20\'13 as labor activists herald the potential for \u8220\'20\'1Ca historic moment\u8221\'20\'1D for thousands of restaurant workers.\par \par \uc2 A step-change is in the air for the city, which has a culinary scene of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/food-wine-magazine-named-chicago-a-top-10-food-city-in-the-u-s-heres-who-beat-us/3124537/#:~:text=Chicago%20was%20named%20among%20Food,in%20the%20U.S.%20and%20abroad.%22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national renown}}}\uc2  and is taking advantage of fictional depictions such as Chicago being the setting for the popular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/oct/01/the-bear-television-so-good-it-might-actually-kill-you-disney-plus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TV food drama The Bear}}}\uc2 , as well acting as host for the annual James Beard Awards.\par \par \uc2 US cities were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/02/02/business/restaurants-pandemic-effects/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hard hit}}}\uc2  by the coronavirus and many are now working through the resulting shake-up in the restaurant business.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe industry is facing the worst crisis in its history,\u8221\'20\'1D Saru Jayaraman, president of the labor advocacy group One Fair Wage, said, noting the shortage of restaurant workers across the country: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd what is our response? Our response is: this is the most historic frickin\u8217\'20\'19 moment in the United States. This is the moment that could change everything in terms of income inequality and the way the economy works.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jayaraman and other members of One Fair Wage vowed at the Netroots progressive conference in Chicago last Friday to continue a legacy of labor wins in the city that stretch back to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2007/sep/03/lostinhistory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 1886 Haymarket Affair}}}\uc2 , the violent breakup of a workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike in support of an eight-hour work day.\par \par \uc2 The standard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chicago.gov/city/en/depts/bacp/supp_info/minimumwageinformation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 minimum wage in Chicago is $15.80 }}}\uc2  an hour for employers with 21 or more workers, but only $9.48 an hour for tipped workers, so those employees are expected to make up that gap with tips from patrons. Their employers are required to make up the difference if workers do not receive enough tips, but many restaurants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/more-employees-sue-restaurants-in-wage-disputes-1439856006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  fail to do so}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Critics condemn $9.48 as a \u8220\'20\'1Csub-minimum\u8221\'20\'1D wage and the battle is on to bring tipped workers\u8217\'20\'19 basic wage up to $15.80, too, with any tips they earn coming on top.\par \par \uc2 The proposed hike already has the support of the new, progressive Chicago mayor, Brandon Johnson, and city lawmaker Carlos Ramirez-Rosa, who rose from being primarily known as a progressive insurgent to the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blockclubchicago.org/2023/06/05/how-ald-carlos-ramirez-rosa-went-from-progressive-agitator-to-city-council-boss/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 powerful floor leader}}}\uc2  in the council. Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blockclubchicago.org/2023/07/14/mayor-brandon-johnson-alderpeople-call-to-end-subminimum-wage-for-tipped-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 served food and drinks for an hour at Netroots}}}\uc2  in an effort to promote the wage hike.\par \par \uc2 Ramirez-Rosa and fellow city lawmaker Jessie Fuentes are spearheading the legislation in the council.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a question of if but how we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get one fair wage,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramirez-Rosa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blockclubchicago.org/2023/07/14/mayor-brandon-johnson-alderpeople-call-to-end-subminimum-wage-for-tipped-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Block Club Chicago}}}\uc2  news website last week.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, campaigners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2023/05/25/dc-tipping-guidelines-after-initiative-82/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chalked up a major victory in Washington last year}}}\uc2 , where, after a protracted struggle, the tipped minimum wage will increase in stages until it reaches the standard rate for hourly workers in the capital, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/dc-politics/dc-council-takes-initial-vote-to-overturn-initiative-77-four-months-after-voters-approved-it/2018/10/02/da906320-c651-11e8-b1ed-1d2d65b86d0c_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite pressure}}}\uc2  from the Restaurant Association of Metropolitan Washington. And eight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/state/minimum-wage/tipped"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other states and territories}}}\uc2 , including California and Alaska, now require employers to pay tipped employees the full minimum wage before tips.\par \par \uc2 Activists in Chicago now hope to take advantage of a tight labor market for tipped workers amid recovery from the pandemic in a year in which the area\u8217\'20\'19s leisure and hospitality industry has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/regions/midwest/news-release/areaemployment_chicago.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced the largest employment gains}}}\uc2  of any sector, forging ahead of health services and manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 Service workers in the Chicago area such as Antoinette Simmons pointed out that an improved minimum wage would ease reliance on tips that leaves workers open to exploitation and harassment from customers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI had to deal with harassment, most of the time bartending, and during the pandemic, it got really ugly,\u8221\'20\'1D Simmons said. During the pandemic, policing customers who refused to wear a mask was difficult. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, yeah, you get cussed out, but I better make sure I make you a good drink and bring you food.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new legislation is not guaranteed passage through the council, despite support from the mayor and influential allies. Other lawmakers in Chicago, where city councillors are known as aldermen, who also wield significant power in their aldermanic fiefdoms, have quashed previous efforts to shake up the local restaurant industry.\par \par \uc2 In one of the most infamous cases, the recently retired alderman Tom Tunney spearheaded a law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicagoreader.com/food-drink/why-chicagos-once-promising-food-truck-scene-stalled-out/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effectively killed Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s food truck}}}\uc2  business by prohibiting trucks from parking within 200ft of brick-and-mortar businesses selling food, including convenience stores. He was the owner of a popular North Side neighborhood brunch spot and former chairman of the \uc2 Illinois Restaurant Association\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Previous efforts to raise the tipped minimum wage received pushback from \uc2 Sam Toia\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Illinois Restaurant Association\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/local/309/2019/09/18/761880725/chicago-may-fast-track-15-minimum-wage-phase-out-lower-tipped-wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that increasing tipped wages would strain restaurants.\par \par \uc2 In June, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chicagobusiness.com/politics/chicago-sub-minimum-wage-tipped-workers-target-johnson-allies-push"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toia told Crain\u8217\'20\'19s Chicago}}}\uc2  that he was open to negotiating once the new bill is introduced. Those comments made One Fair Wage\u8217\'20\'19s Jayaraman optimistic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing willingness to talk about ending the sub-minimum wage for tipped workers on the part of the Restaurant Association, I think is a reflection of the fact that the mayor has very publicly stated that he\u8217\'20\'19s prioritizing this issue. It gives us a very strong chance,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230719ej7j00236\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
