\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Guatemalan boy dies in Mississippi poultry plant accident\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2023\par 15:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Duvan Perez, 16, dies at Mar-Jac factory in Hattiesburg amid rollback of child labor laws across several US states\par \par \uc2 A 16-year-old from Guatemala died on Friday after sustaining a workplace injury at a poultry plant in Mississippi, authorities confirm.\par \par \uc2 The child, identified as Duvan Tomas Perez, died at \uc2 Mar-Jac Poultry\uc2  plant in Hattiesburg, Mississippi, about two hours outside of Jackson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/16-year-old-boy-dies-accident-mississippi-poultry-plant-rcna94963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2 . He migrated to the US six years ago from the town of Huispache and was a middle school student.\par \par \uc2 The accident occurred on Friday at about 8pm central time, the Forrest county coroner, Butch Benedict, told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 The teenager\u8217\'20\'19s death was caused by workplace equipment, Benedict confirmed. Benedict added that an autopsy had been completed and details would probably be released next week.\par \par \uc2 An employee who was working at the time of the incident told NBC that he heard the boy cry for help.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo times he began to scream, \u8216\'20\'18Help! Help!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said to NBC. \u8220\'20\'1CI knew he had died.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Minors in Mississippi are not allowed to be employed in poultry plants. The \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha) \uc2 and the labor department have launched investigations into the boy\u8217\'20\'19s death, NBC reported.\par \par \uc2 Companies in violation of labor rules could face fines of over $30,000 per incident.\par \par \uc2 Several employees have died at Mar-Jac over the years, Benedict said. Perez\u8217\'20\'19s was the third death since 2020, when a 33-year old worker died after being injured at the plant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hattiesburgamerican.com/story/news/local/2023/07/18/hattiesburg-ms-teen-killed-at-ms-chicken-processing-plant-mar-jac-poultry/70426376007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hattiesburg American reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A 48-year employee also died in June 2021 after sustaining injuries from heavy machinery, the American reported.\par \par \uc2 Several US states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/11/us-child-labor-laws-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently rolled back}}}\uc2  child labor protections, an effort mostly led by Republican lawmakers, despite child labor law violations increasing by 37% in 2022 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.columbia.edu/news/archive/qa-crisis-child-labor-professors-kate-andrias-and-elora-mukherjee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by 283% since 2015}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In May, the Iowa governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/27/republican-iowa-governor-rolls-back-child-labor-law-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received widespread criticism }}}\uc2  after signing legislation overturning several child labor protections including how many hours children can work and the type of industries.\par \par \uc2 The new legislation also provides employers with exemption from liability if minors are sickened, injured or killed at work.\par \par \uc2 Such rollbacks in protections often affect migrant children who can be at an increased risk of exploitation, said Elora Mukherjee, a professor of law at Columbia Law School.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRather than being in school and being generously supported by the communities they\u8217\'20\'19re in, many of these children are forced to work in exploitative conditions to try and support themselves and their family members,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mukherjee, emphasizing the need for migrant children to receive support.\par \par \uc2 Mukherjee said it was hard to pin down an exact figure on how many migrant minors are being employed illegally.\par \par \uc2 Federal investigations have been opened in at least 11 states to better understand the scope of the problem, Mukherjee added, calling those inquiries an important first step.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clearly just a first step. It\u8217\'20\'19s not enough,\u8221\'20\'1D Mukherjee said, adding that the government should be investing more into such investigations and targeting firms and employers who are hiring migrant children.\par \par \uc2 Monetary fines that companies face for violations can also be minuscule and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot sufficient to deter child labor violations\u8221\'20\'1D, especially for multinational corporations who make millions in profits, Mukherjee said.\par \par \uc2 Mukherjee called the death of Duval a \u8220\'20\'1Ctragedy\u8221\'20\'1D that reflects the difficult situations migrant minors face.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230719ej7j001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
