\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Striking Hollywood stars meet with union to discuss actors\u8217\'20\'19 walkout\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton in Los Angeles \par \uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2023\par 00:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meeting comes after strike announced on 13 July by actors\u8217\'20\'19 union, joining writers to negotiate for new contracts with producers\par \par \uc2 Some of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s biggest stars met on Monday to discuss the actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike as their union warned that without \u8220\'20\'1Ctransformative change\u8221\'20\'1D the entire profession is under threat.\par \par \uc2 Members of Sag-Aftra, a labor union for US actors, gathered over Zoom on Monday to go over talking points and answer questions about their ongoing strike, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/sag-actors-strike-meeting-1235672494/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Variety reported}}}\uc2  in an exclusive. The meeting was attended by about 500 agents, publicists and actors, including Lupita Nyong\u8217\'20\'19o, Laverne Cox and Melissa McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 The informational session came amid a strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on 13 July}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  executive director and chief negotiator Duncan Crabtree-Ireland and Fran Drescher, the Sag-Aftra president. Members of the union voted overwhelmingly to authorize a walkout, joining with industry writers who have been on strike since May.\par \par \uc2 They are asking for increases in base pay and residuals as film and TV shows have increasingly moved to online streaming platforms and assurances their work will not be replaced by artificial intelligence and their digital image will not be used without their permission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout a transformative change in \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s current contract with the [\uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 ], the acting profession will no longer be an option for future generations of performers, and actors already working in the industry will need to pursue other careers in order to survive,\u8221\'20\'1D a memo shared during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s Sag-Aftra Zoom meeting read, according to Variety.\par \par \uc2 The Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ), the trade association that represents studios, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disappointed that \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  has decided to walk away from negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D, and said it had offered the highest percentage increases in minimum pay levels in 35 years, \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial increases\u8221\'20\'1D in pension and healthcare contribution caps, a 76% increase in foreign residuals paid from big-budget streaming shows and \u8220\'20\'1Ca groundbreaking AI proposal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Drescher, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president, said last week: \u8220\'20\'1CThe companies have refused to meaningfully engage on some topics and on others completely stonewalled us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The actors\u8217\'20\'19 strike marks the first time in 63 years that Hollywood writers and actors are striking simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 In May, the Writer\u8217\'20\'19s Guild of America, which represents 11,500 television and film writers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/02/thousands-of-hollywood-film-and-tv-writers-to-go-on-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorized its first strike}}}\uc2  in 15 years. The WGA said the companies\u8217\'20\'19 behavior had \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated a gig economy\u8221\'20\'1D that aimed to turn writing into an \u8220\'20\'1Centirely freelance\u8221\'20\'1D profession. \u8220\'20\'1CFor the sake of our present and our future, we have been given no other choice,\u8221\'20\'1D it said. The last industrial action, in 2007, lasted 100 days and cost the California economy an estimated $2.1bn as productions shut down and striking writers, actors and producers cut back on spending.\par \par \uc2 According to Variety\u8217\'20\'19s exclusive report, there are two more Zoom Sag-Aftra meetings scheduled for Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230718ej7h00006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
