\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Hollywood grinds to a halt on first full day of joint actors\u8217\'20\'19 and writers\u8217\'20\'19 strikes\b0\par\par\uc2 Adrian Horton \par \uc2 988 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par 09:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra action sees actors and writers picketing together outside studios and pauses production and promotion of movies\par \par \uc2 The first full day of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike by Sag-Aftra}}}\uc2  had an immediate effect on Hollywood, as the industry ground to a halt over a contract with producers that would cover such wide-ranging issues as compensation and the future of AI in film and television.\par \par \uc2 Whereas the writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike, which has seen the guild\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 20,000 members out of work since early May, promptly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/may/03/writers-strike-tv-industry-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shuttered}}}\uc2  late-night variety programs and writers\u8217\'20\'19 rooms and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2023/06/15/wga-writers-strike-movie-tv-delays/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delayed release dates}}}\uc2  for many film and TV shows, a simultaneous strike by \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 160,000 members has the potential to bring Hollywood to a full standstill.\par \par \uc2 Actors and writers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/sag-actors-strike-begins-1235670214/#recipient_hashed=58e80303eb86ef6e1590496f3313a95182cb7e47e4431739bdb854b95b0768c7&recipient_salt=7e749829dd8fdacaf3affd4f51643a323740a6b6883a45b85c04133fdf95e512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began picketing}}}\uc2  outside various studio and streaming service headquarters on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 four locations in New York and eight more in Los Angeles, with such signs as \u8220\'20\'1CLogan Roy would pay us more\u8221\'20\'1D; \u8220\'20\'1CYour poor Montana ranch!\u8221\'20\'1D; \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m trying to pay my rent, not my third and fourth mortgage and fuel my private jet!\u8221\'20\'1D; and \u8220\'20\'1CChatGPT can suck my D.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike \u8211\'20\'13 the first time the actors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/jul/14/its-a-constant-hustle-actors-join-writers-on-the-picket-line"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined writers on the picket line}}}\uc2  since 1960 \u8211\'20\'13 immediately ceased promotional work for several major summer films, which was already hindered by the absence of talkshows. According to strike guidance, members will not be able to attend premieres, do interviews for completed work, attend award shows or film festivals, or promote projects on social media while the strike is in effect.\par \par \uc2 The strike canceled the New York red-carpet premiere of \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2 , Christopher Nolan\u8217\'20\'19s biopic about the creator of the atomic bomb. On Thursday, the film\u8217\'20\'19s cast, including Cillian Murphy, Emily Blunt and Matt Damon, left the film\u8217\'20\'19s London premiere early, when the strike was called. (Damon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/zachsilberberg/status/1679541297122533402?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Deadline that the strike will affect his new production company founded with Ben Affleck.) The cast of this month\u8217\'20\'19s other hotly anticipated film, Greta Gerwig\u8217\'20\'19s Barbie, also wrapped its promotional campaign early. \u8220\'20\'1CI very much am in support of all the unions and I\u8217\'20\'19m a part of Sag, so I would absolutely stand by them,\u8221\'20\'1D the film\u8217\'20\'19s lead, Margot Robbie, told reporters at the London premiere.\par \par \uc2 One of the first major productions affected was Deadpool 3, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/deadpool-3-stops-production-sag-strike-1235668880/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused filming}}}\uc2  on Thursday as the strike got under way, only days after Marvel revealed a first look at the set with photos of the stars Ryan Reynolds and Hugh Jackman costumed as Deadpool and Wolverine, respectively. As the script was already locked, Deadpool 3 was able to continue production during the writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike. But the film\u8217\'20\'19s original May 2024 release date now seems in jeopardy due to the production halt, a sign of the Hollywood stasis to come.\par \par \uc2 HBO\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s blockbuster series House of the Dragon, however, will continue filming in the UK due to local union rules, as first reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/tv/global/house-of-the-dragon-season-2-filming-sag-strike-hbo-1235669404/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Variety}}}\uc2 . The majority of the actors on the Game of Thrones prequel, currently filming its second season, are from the UK and thus under contracts governed by the UK local union, Equity. The series is technically allowed to continue filming as Equity members are not legally permitted to strike in solidarity with US actors. In strike guidance provided by Equity hours before Sag-Aftra officially declared a walkout, the union, the 12th largest trade organization in the UK, said it would \u8220\'20\'1Csupport Sag-Aftra and its members by all lawful means\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A strike could also torpedo major summer and fall film festivals, which are now in wait-and-see mode. Glitzy photo opportunity-oriented festivals like Venice, which is set to begin on 30 August, could be held without major Hollywood stars. The Toronto film festival, held in September, said in a statement to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/07/sag-aftra-strike-tiff-venice-film-festivals-1235437782/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline}}}\uc2  on Thursday that organizers will \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue planning for this year\u8217\'20\'19s festival with the hope of a swift resolution in the coming weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Broadway will remain open, as \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  does not represent stage actors. But on Friday, the president of Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity, which represents stage actors and stage managers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/07/actors-equity-sag-aftra-strike-avoid-breaking-kate-shindle-1235438177/#recipient_hashed=58e80303eb86ef6e1590496f3313a95182cb7e47e4431739bdb854b95b0768c7&recipient_salt=7e749829dd8fdacaf3affd4f51643a323740a6b6883a45b85c04133fdf95e512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  members to \u8220\'20\'1Cproactively and aggressively avoid breaking\u8221\'20\'1D the Sag-Aftra strike by inadvertently crossing the picket line. The guild president, Kate Shindle, encouraged members to contact Sag-Aftra with any questions about potentially struck work, and added: \u8220\'20\'1CKnow this: the other side will try to pit us against each other to keep churning out content. Don\u8217\'20\'19t fall for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the heart of the negotiations is what many members have referred to as an existential question over the future of AI in replacing writers or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/jul/13/joan-is-awful-black-mirror-striking-actors-nightmare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generating unapproved likenesses}}}\uc2  of actors, among other concerns. The Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) said it offered a \u8220\'20\'1Cgroundbreaking AI proposal which protects performers\u8217\'20\'19 digital likenesses, including a requirement for performer\u8217\'20\'19s consent for the creation and use of digital replicas or for digital alterations of a performance\u8221\'20\'1D. But Duncan Crabtree-Ireland, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief negotiator and national executive director, denounced that proposal on Thursday for only paying background performers for one day of work in exchange for the rights to their digital likeness \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the rest of eternity with no compensation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you think that\u8217\'20\'19s a groundbreaking proposal, I suggest you think again,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 In the hours after the strike was called, numerous Hollywood stars, including Jamie Lee Curtis, Bob Odenkirk, Cynthia Nixon, Sheryl Lee Ralph and Josh Gad, expressed public support for the dual work stoppages.\par \par \uc2 George Clooney has also backed the strike, and said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/07/george-clooney-sag-aftra-strike-wga-strike-1235437997/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Friday that \u8220\'20\'1Cactors and writers in large numbers have lost their ability to make a living\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an inflection point in our industry,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor our industry to survive that has to change. For actors, that journey starts now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230715ej7f000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
