\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Hollywood actors announce strike in first joint action with writers in more than 60 years\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,198 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 23:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Simultaneous strikes by WGA and Sag-Aftra are expected to halt the majority of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s film and TV production\par \par \uc2 The union representing Hollywood actors formally announced a strike on Thursday, expanding the standoff between Hollywood workers and studio executives over wages, AI technology and how to divide the profits of the new digital streaming era.\par \par \uc2 The strike by the Screen Actors Guild-American Federation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/television"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Television}}}\uc2  and Radio Artists (Sag-Aftra), which will begin on Friday, will mark the first time in 63 years that Hollywood writers and actors are striking simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood writers went on strike in early May. Now the 11,500 members of the Writers Guild of America (WGA) will be joined by some of \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 160,000 members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt some point you have to say no: we are not going to take this any more,\u8221\'20\'1D Fran Drescher, the \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  president, said in a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot change the business model as much as it has changed and not change the contract too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t stand tall right now, we are all in trouble,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The simultaneous strikes are expected to halt the majority of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s film and TV production, and have major effects on the broader Los Angeles economy. With some of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s biggest stars on strike, press junkets for summer and fall movie premieres will be cancelled, and the Emmy awards will probably be postponed. Workers across LA are gearing up to survive for weeks or months without wages.\par \par \uc2 The Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ), the trade association that represents studios, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disappointed that \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  has decided to walk away from negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRather than continuing to negotiate, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  has put us on a course that will deepen the financial hardship for thousands who depend on the industry for their livelihoods,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 As Sag-Aftra goes on strike, its president condemned a media report that studio executives planned to \u8220\'20\'1Cbleed out\u8221\'20\'1D writers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what? Eventually, the people break down the gates of Versailles. And then it\u8217\'20\'19s over. We\u8217\'20\'19re at that moment right now,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frandrescher?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @frandrescher}}}\uc2  said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jskY3BRE98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jskY3BRE98}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Lois Beckett (@loisbeckett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/loisbeckett/status/1679585273343266817?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Members of Sag-Aftra and the WGA voted overwhelmingly to authorize a strike if needed. Members are asking for increases in base pay and residuals as film and TV shows have increasingly moved to online streaming platforms, and assurances that their work will not be replaced by artificial intelligence or their digital image will not be used without their permission.\par \par \uc2 Major movie stars in recent days spoke out about how the transition to streaming has affected less famous union members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to make $26,000 a year to qualify for your health insurance and there are a lot of people who get across that threshold through their residual payments,\u8221\'20\'1D Matt Damon said at a promotional event held for the film \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2  on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s money being made and it needs to be allocated in a way that takes care of people who are on the margins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said it had offered the highest percentage increases in minimum pay levels in 35 years, \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial increases\u8221\'20\'1D in pension and healthcare contribution caps, a 76% increase in foreign residuals paid from big-budget streaming shows and \u8220\'20\'1Ca groundbreaking AI proposal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s top acting talent had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/30/sag-aftra-actors-union-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made it clear they were willing to strike}}}\uc2 . In late June, a letter from Hollywood A-listers, including Meryl Streep and Jennifer Lawrence, urged their union leaders not to settle for a mediocre deal in what they saw as a historically important contract negotiation.\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra and the studios had been negotiating for weeks, but failed to reach an agreement by the deadline of midnight on Wednesday. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/sag-aftra-television-theatrical-and-streaming-contracts-expire-without-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday, the actors\u8217\'20\'19 union said its negotiating committee had voted unanimously to recommend a strike, and that its national board would decide on the matter on Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 It said: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter more than four weeks of bargaining, the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 the entity that represents major studios and streamers, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 NBCUniversal\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , Paramount, \uc2 Sony\uc2  and \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 remains unwilling to offer a fair deal on the key issues that are essential to Sag-Aftra members.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Drescher, \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe companies have refused to meaningfully engage on some topics and on others completely stonewalled us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her message to studio executives, Drescher said at Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s press conference, was, \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re sitting on the wrong side of history. Shame on you.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what? Eventually, the people break down the gates of Versailles. And then it\u8217\'20\'19s over. We\u8217\'20\'19re at that moment right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Drescher said.\par \par \uc2 The strike is not only expected to shut down US-based productions, but will also hamper many overseas shoots involving members. Some production work not involving Sag-Aftra performers can proceed.\par \par \uc2 A strike is also expected to have an immediate impact on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/sag-strike-summer-movies-marketing-1235642983/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicity efforts}}}\uc2  for the summer\u8217\'20\'19s top films; the Thursday evening premiere of \uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2  in London was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/film/news/oppenheimer-london-premiere-sag-aftra-strike-1235668910/#recipient_hashed=9efeacc11e0abb466e9602c6f2c48adb25fb2de05957eef78c2203af41d46b7b&recipient_salt=731cd859db9f7c019c9fa188dbfa9c3560f62ed19ba1cf18b1cc89c2ad947160"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  moved to start an hour earlier}}}\uc2  so the cast could attend regardless of the outcome, but the actors left before the screening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/07/actors-strike-oppenheimer-cast-leaves-london-premiere-christopher-nolan-1235437291/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline reported}}}\uc2 . Other major commercial films including Barbie and Mission: Impossible \u8211\'20\'13 Dead Reckoning Part One have already hosted their world premieres, though their stars will be restricted from participating in further promotional events.\par \par \uc2 The strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/emmys-strike-delay-fox-tv-academy-january-november-1235667092/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may also delay the Emmy awards}}}\uc2  until late autumn, or even next year, industry publications reported.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  has announced that a 15 July premiere of its movie Haunted Mansion will still take place at Disneyland regardless of the strikes, though the film\u8217\'20\'19s actors \u8211\'20\'13 including LaKeith Stanfield, Tiffany Haddish, and Jamie Lee Curtis \u8211\'20\'13 will not be present.\par \par \uc2 San Diego Comic-Con, scheduled to begin on 20 July, will be affected as well.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood writers have been on strike since 2 May. The beginning of that strike was marked by strong solidarity from Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s other unionised workforces, including the powerful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/biz/news/wga-strike-lindsay-dougherty-teamsters-dga-1235602975/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters\u8217\'20\'19 union}}}\uc2 , and Sag-Aftra members showed up in solidarity at Writers Guild of America picket lines, even before their own strike was called.\par \par \uc2 Anonymous industry sources told Deadline this week that studio executives did not plan to resume negotiations with the striking writers until late October.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe endgame is to allow things to drag on until union members start losing their apartments and losing their houses,\u8221\'20\'1D an industry source was quoted as saying, with another saying the goal was to \u8220\'20\'1Cbreak the WGA\u8221\'20\'1D. A spokesperson for the studios denied those anonymous claims, telling Deadline in a statement that the companies \u8220\'20\'1Care committed to reaching a deal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Duncan Crabtree-Ireland, the union\u8217\'20\'19s chief negotiator, said \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1960 strike had won its members a health plan and television residuals. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the same kind of strike \u8211\'20\'13 a strike that makes sure our members\u8217\'20\'19 livelihoods are not taken away by artificial intelligence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230713ej7d0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
