\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 US actors: why are you striking?\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian community team \par \uc2 159 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 10:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 We want to hear from Hollywood actors, as well as writers, about their reasons for taking industrial action\par \par \uc2 The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representing Hollywood actors announced}}}\uc2  a strike on Thursday, joining writers who began taking industrial action in May.\par \par \uc2 The strike by the Screen Actors Guild-American Federation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/television"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Television}}}\uc2  and Radio Artists (Sag-Aftra), which begins on Friday, is the first time in 63 years that Hollywood writers and actors are striking simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 The action is being taken over wages, AI technology and how to divide digital streaming profits.\par \par \uc2 If you are an US actor who is striking, we want to hear from you. Why are you taking action and how have you been affected? How do you feel about it? What does the future of your profession look like to you?\par \par \uc2 We also want to hear from writers about their reasons for striking and hopes for the action.\par \par \uc2 Callout\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230714ej7e001bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
