\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Hollywood actors strike: hundreds of Australian film and TV workers to be stood down\b0\par\par\uc2 Kelly Burke \par \uc2 720 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 06:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 At least two feature films being shot on the Gold Coast expected to halt production for the duration of the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  strikeGet our weekend culture and lifestyle email\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of Australian workers are likely to be stood down from film productions as as result of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the strike by Hollywood actors and screenwriters.}}}\par \par \uc2 Screen Producers Australia\uc2  confirmed on Friday Australian cast and crew working on US-backed television series and films were expected to be stood down for the duration of the strike, which begins at 5.01pm AEST.\par \par \uc2 The union representing Australian screen workers signalled its support for the US strike but warned its members they would not be protected if they took similar industrial action.\par \par \uc2 Screen workers on foreign-backed documentaries, light entertainment and reality shows will not be affected.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Writers Guild of America (WGA) and the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild-American Federation of Television and Radio Artists\uc2  (\uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 ) voted to go on strike after negotiations with Hollywood studios broke down on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 It is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time in more than 60 years}}}\uc2  both sectors of the US film industry have walked off the set in unison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/newsletters/2019/oct/18/saved-for-later-sign-up-for-guardian-australias-culture-and-lifestyle-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for the fun stuff with our rundown of must-reads, pop culture and tips for the weekend, every Saturday morning}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Friday the chief executive of Australia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Media, Entertainment & Arts Alliance\uc2  (MEAA), Erin Madeley, said the union stood in solidarity with \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members. Fair compensation from streaming services and concerns by actors over artificial intelligence replacing jobs were universal, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStreaming services are raking in billions of dollars in revenue and earnings as their audiences continue to grow, but these profits are not being shared fairly with actors,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough series budgets are increasing, that increase is not being reflected in the share of the money going to performers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under current US arrangements, streaming services pay lower residuals to actors for repeats of films and television series than broadcast television. In Australia, the MEAA negotiated residual rights for actors in 2015, but payments can vary according to each production\u8217\'20\'19s contracts, across both streaming and TV broadcast platforms.\par \par \uc2 Madeley said rules covering the global screen industry were also needed to regulate the future potential use of artificial intelligence to replace actors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want robots telling our stories in place of humans,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Australian screenwriters are in an even more disadvantageous position than their American counterparts.\par \par \uc2 Claire Pullen, the executive director of the \uc2 Australian Writers\u8217\'20\'19 Guild\uc2  (AWG), said streaming services pay no residuals or royalties to Australian screenwriters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese agreements are essentially about having an ongoing relationship with your own work, but in Australia, once a streaming service pays for a work, that\u8217\'20\'19s it,\u8221\'20\'1D Pullen said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere in Australia, the streamers do not offer contracts unless you fully assign them all the rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pullen said although the AWG supported the action taken by the WGA, it was unlikely Australian screenwriters would strike in solidarity as the guild was not entering a period of renegotiation with the screen industry.\par \par \uc2 At least two feature films were set to halt production on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2  martial arts fantasy film Mortal Kombat 2 and the Universal Studios drama based on the Liane Moriarty novel Apples Never Fall, starring Sam Neill and Annette Bening.\par \par \uc2 Both have been shooting on the Gold Coast. \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2  and Universal Studios have been approached for comment.\par \par \uc2 Next month\u8217\'20\'19s Melbourne international film festival may also be affected, with a spokesperson saying management was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking through the sensitivities and obligations of attending guests\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The WGA strike, which began in early May, has already caused the cancellation of the remake of the 1927 Fritz Lang classic Metropolis. The \uc2 Apple\uc2  TV eight-part series was supposed to begin filming in Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s Docklands studios in October.\par \par \uc2 According to the Hollywood news site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2022/04/appletv-plus-sam-esmail-sci-fi-drama-metropolis-to-shoot-in-melbourne-australia-1235002252/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline}}}\uc2 , the series was expected to create almost 4,000 jobs in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 Screen Producers Australia\uc2  said in a statement on Friday Australian-scripted productions using Australian and imported \uc2 SAG\uc2  members would not be affected by the strike order if they were engaged under Australian industry contracts agreed to by \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  and the MEAA.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230714ej7e000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
