\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Fran Drescher\u8217\'20\'19s fiery speech against Hollywood studios goes viral as actors strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Sian Cain \par \uc2 729 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 05:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Nanny star turned Sag-Aftra union president wins praise for her passion as performers join writers in action expected to halt majority of US film and TV production\par \par \uc2 Fran Drescher has blasted Hollywood studios in a fiery speech after talks between the actors\u8217\'20\'19 union and studios failed to avert a strike, calling them \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusting\u8221\'20\'1D for claiming \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re losing money left and right when giving hundreds of millions of dollars to their CEOs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a speech that was widely circulated on Thursday \u8211\'20\'13 particularly among many who did not know The Nanny star was heading up Sag-Aftra, Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s biggest union \u8211\'20\'13 Drescher said actors were being \u8220\'20\'1Cmarginalised, disrespected and dishonoured\u8221\'20\'1D by a business model that has been drastically changed by streaming and artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens here is important because what\u8217\'20\'19s happening to us is happening across all fields of labor, when employers make Wall Street and greed their priority and they forget about the essential contributors that make the machine run,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the victims here. We are being victimised by a very greedy entity. I am shocked by the way the people that we have been in business with are treating us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot believe it, quite frankly, how far apart we are on so many things. How they plead poverty, that they\u8217\'20\'19re losing money left and right when giving hundreds of millions of dollars to their CEOs. It is disgusting. Shame on them. They stand on the wrong side of history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/hollywood-actors-union-recommends-strike-as-talks-deadline-passes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Thursday it was announced}}}\uc2  that 160,000 Sag-Aftra members \u8211\'20\'13 from big stars to background actors \u8211\'20\'13 will be joining the Writers Guild of America in a strike, marking the biggest shutdown of Hollywood since both unions last went on strike together in 1960.\par \par \uc2 The unions are fighting for better terms with the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 , an entity that represents major studios and streamers, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 NBCUniversal\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , Paramount, \uc2 Sony\uc2  and \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Drescher, who became union president in 2021, has long expressed concerns about corporate greed, captioning photos with slogans like \u8220\'20\'1CSTOP CAPITALIST GREED NOW\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frandrescher/status/1242455857087967232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeting sentiments including}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CCapitalism has become another word for Ruling Class Elite!\u8221\'20\'1D In 2017 New York Magazine ran the headline: \u8220\'20\'1CYour New Favorite Anti-Capitalist Icon Is Fran Drescher.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Drescher also described herself as \u8220\'20\'1Canti-capitalist\u8221\'20\'1D in an interview with Vulture that year, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not anti-making-money, don\u8217\'20\'19t get me wrong. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think making money is a bad thing, per se. But it has to be calibrated within the spectrum of what\u8217\'20\'19s a true value.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I really tell people is, \u8216\'20\'18you might be the first ones at a global-warming rally, but meanwhile, do you know what\u8217\'20\'19s in your investment portfolio?\u8217\'20\'19 We need to not be supporting these companies at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Drescher\u8217\'20\'19s speech on Thursday was off-the-cuff, with the 65-year-old actor shaking her fists and sometimes blinking away tears. \u8220\'20\'1CWake up and smell the coffee,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the studios. \u8220\'20\'1CWe demand respect! You cannot exist without us!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fran Drescher becoming one of the consequential union leaders of our time is an arc I am absolutely delighted by as both a union gal and a '90s kid.\u8212\'20\'14 Emily St. James (@emilystjams) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emilystjams/status/1679583452298084353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  members have been ordered to stop any work connected to productions, including red carpets and promoting their work on social media. The London premiere of Christopher Nolan\u8217\'20\'19s Oppenheimer was pulled forward one hour to avoid the start of the strike, with the cast leaving during the film as it was officially announced.\par \par \uc2 On Twitter Bette Midler criticised tech companies in a thread listing the many industries that were being hurt, before focusing on Hollywood. \u8220\'20\'1CThe actors are right to strike, as are the writers,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BetteMidler/status/1679590684112633857"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to devalue and destroy an industry, it\u8217\'20\'19s no longer a sustainable business model.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cynthia Nixon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CynthiaNixon/status/1679580330427072512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that she is \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to be standing tall\u8221\'20\'1D with the WGA and that studios that have been \u8220\'20\'1Creaping from our labor for far too long\u8221\'20\'1D. She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will win this!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jamie Lee Curtis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CupmkOmSRS4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared an Instagram post that read}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to take down the MASKS and pick up the SIGNS\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230714ej7e0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
