\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 Actors\u8217\'20\'19 union agrees to \u8216\'20\'18last-minute request\u8217\'20\'19 for federal mediator in contract negotiations\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett \par \uc2 479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2023\par 11:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 But Sag-Aftra says it will not extend Wednesday night deadline to reach deal before going on strike\par \par \uc2 As Hollywood was bracing for the possibility of the first simultaneous strike by Hollywood writers and actors in more than 60 years, the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2  said it had agreed to a \u8220\'20\'1Clast-minute request\u8221\'20\'1D to work with a federal mediator in contract negotiations with film and TV studios.\par \par \uc2 But the union said it would not extend its Wednesday night deadline to reach a deal before its 160,000 members go on strike, citing their frustration with the studios\u8217\'20\'19 negotiating tactics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be manipulated by this cynical ploy to engineer an extension when the companies have had more than enough time to make a fair deal,\u8221\'20\'1D the Screen Actors Guild \u8211\'20\'13 American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (Sag-Aftra) said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/sag-aftra-statement-regarding-request-federal-mediation-and-conciliation-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement on Tuesday evening}}}\uc2 , about 30 hours before the contract negotiation deadline. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not confident that the employers have any intention of bargaining toward an agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union representing Hollywood actors has already extended negotiations with film studios once, in late June, after a letter from some of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s A-list talent, including Meryl Streep and Jennifer Lawrence, urged union leaders not to settle for a mediocre deal in what they saw as a historically important contract negotiation.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s writers have already been on strike for more than two months, with no deal with the studios in sight.\par \par \uc2 If a strike becomes necessary, we're ready. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/62kUzNId4e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/62kUzNId4e}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  (@sagaftra) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sagaftra/status/1677473688604798976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Writers and actors are fighting over similar concerns in their contract negotiations with \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ), which includes legacy film companies such as Universal and \uc2 Disney\uc2 , and digital disruptors, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Netflix\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sticking points include how much compensation actors and writers receive when their work ends up on streaming platforms, rather than on television, and what rules and protections will exist for artists as studios continue to explore new uses of artificial intelligence technology \u8211\'20\'13 from AI-generated TV scripts to AI-generated likenesses of actors and celebrities.\par \par \uc2 Studio executives had discussed the possibility of calling in a federal mediator to assist with the negotiation during an internal call on Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/biz/news/sag-aftra-federal-mediators-amptp-1235667053/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Variety reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its Tuesday night statement, Sag-Aftra blasted \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  for what the union characterized as a deliberate effort to plant a story in the press before informing the union about it.\par \par \uc2 The union said it condemned \u8220\'20\'1Cinformation that was leaked to the press by the CEOs and their \u8216\'20\'18anonymous sources\u8217\'20\'19 before our negotiators were even told of the request for mediation,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  has abused our trust and damaged the respect we have for them in this process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230712ej7c000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
