\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Minimum hourly wage in swanky West Hollywood is the highest in the US\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 550 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2023\par 08:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Business owners are concerned about growing labor costs they say could force them into financial hardship\par \par \uc2 The swanky, celebrity-studded \uc2 city of West Hollywood\uc2  officially has the highest minimum wage of any US city after pay zoomed to $19.08 an hour on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Workers in West Hollywood welcomed the increase amid rising rent, gas and food prices, although employers grumbled about growing labor costs that they say could drive them out of business.\par \par \uc2 Lucian Tudor, chief executive of upmarket restaurant La Boheme, told the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  he has cut staff from 120 to 80 to trim costs. The city\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage climbed $1 in January to $17.50 an hour for businesses with at least 50 employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese pay increases are about superficiality and about opportunistic politicians who are just trying to make a name for themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Tudor, who would prefer a minimum wage that accounts for tips like what New York City has, told the news outlet.\par \par \uc2 A one-year waiver is available to employers who demonstrate that complying with the new minimum wage would result in financial hardship.\par \par \uc2 The city council approved the wage increase in 2021 with the stipulation that full-time employees are entitled to 12 days of paid personal time as well as 10 days of unpaid time.\par \par \uc2 The minimum wage increased in other cities across the US on Saturday, but none as high as West Hollywood, a city of 35,000 tucked between the cities of Beverly Hills and Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage increased more than a $1 to $18.07 an hour. Los Angeles\u8217\'20\'19 is now $16.78 an hour, and the minimum wage in Washington DC is $17, up from $16.10 an hour.\par \par \uc2 For workers in Los Angeles hotels with 60 rooms or more, the minimum pay increased to $19.73 an hour on Saturday, up from $18.86. Hotel workers in Santa Monica also saw their pay climb to $19.73.\par \par \uc2 Seattle had the highest minimum wage of any US city in January when its hourly rate increased to $18.69.\par \par \uc2 Norberto Ruiz, who works in a liquor store in West Hollywood, told the LA Times that a wage increase last summer allowed his family to buy a $150 air conditioner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think people understand how much an extra dollar or two can change people\u8217\'20\'19s lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Ruiz told the news outlet.\par \par \uc2 LA county supervisor Lindsey Horvath, who served as a West Hollywood council member in 2021, told the LA Times she was delighted by both the wage increase and the paid time off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very proud that we are looking for ways to ensure that people\u8217\'20\'19s mental and physical wellbeing is protected in their jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat we are not saying that people have to choose between being able to afford rent and taking time off to care for themselves or a loved one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage increased to $15.50 an hour as of 1 January. However, the federal minimum wage has been stalled at $7.25 an hour since 2009 despite efforts from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/23/fight-for-15-movement-10-years-old"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fight for $15}}}\uc2  movement to increase the rate as inflation has risen.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230703ej73000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
