\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Disney\uc2  owes female workers more than $150m in wages, pay gap suit alleges\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 772 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2023\par 21:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A salary analysis found that when controlled for other factors affecting pay, the disparities arose from gender discrimination\par \par \uc2 The Walt Disney Company\uc2  has systematically underpaid women, depriving female employees of more than $150m in wages in California since 2015, according to a new analysis of salary data carried out as part of a class-action lawsuit alleging widespread pay gaps at the company.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for a group of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/sep/18/disney-lawsuit-gender-pay-gap-abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women suing Disney}}}\uc2  alleged in state court in Los Angeles on Friday that the entertainment and media corporation has paid women on average 2% less than men doing equivalent jobs, in violation of California\u8217\'20\'19s Equal Pay Act.\par \par \uc2 The analysis is based on salaries for non-union employees below the vice-president level and includes workers at Disney Studios, parks and resorts, its music label, \uc2 Disney\uc2 +, ABC, \uc2 Lucasfilm\uc2 , Searchlight Pictures and other major entities that the lawsuit says are all subject to the same compensation system.\par \par \uc2 The estimate that women are owed $151.6m was revealed in the attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 motion for class certification for the more than 10,000 women employed by those \uc2 Disney\uc2  entities from 2015 to the present. The case excludes \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , \uc2 ESPN\uc2 , \uc2 Pixar\uc2 , \uc2 21st Century Fox\uc2  and several other brands that have distinct pay policies or were recently acquired and cannot be fairly compared to the rest of the corporation, the lawyers say.\par \par \uc2 The case was first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/apr/03/disney-company-women-pay-gap-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  in 2019 alleging an \u8220\'20\'1Cegregious gender pay gap that appears to be engrained in \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s culture\u8221\'20\'1D. LaRonda Rasmussen, a manager of product development for \uc2 Disney\uc2 , and the plaintiff who the case is named after, alleges that six men with the same title were receiving between $16,000 to nearly $40,000 more than her. A senior manager for \uc2 Disney\uc2  music publishing said she learned she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/jul/05/disney-lawsuit-discrimination-pay-gap-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earning $25,000 less}}}\uc2  than some men with equivalent titles. Other women allege that they faced discrimination when they were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/sep/18/disney-lawsuit-gender-pay-gap-abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied promotions}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/sep/18/disney-lawsuit-gender-pay-gap-abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 given smaller raises than men}}}\uc2 , or were classified in lower-ranking jobs compared with men doing similar work.\par \par \uc2 Out of nine named plaintiffs, five are women of color.\par \par \uc2 The new statistical analysis was conducted by David Neumark, a \uc2 University of California, Irvine\uc2  labor economist and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.socsci.uci.edu/newsevents/news/2022/2022-11-18-neumark-bloomberg.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay gap expert}}}\uc2  hired by the plaintiffs. His report filed with the court said his comparisons of men\u8217\'20\'19s and women\u8217\'20\'19s salaries controlled for job levels, tenure and other factors that could affect pay, meaning the disparities he uncovered stemmed from gender discrimination.\par \par \uc2 The pay disparities were due in part to \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s consideration of prior salary in setting starting pay for new hires and its practice of setting annual merit raises as a percentage of salary, further widening the gender gaps. Neumark reported that the gender pay gap was 4.36% when \uc2 Disney\uc2  relied on prior pay to set starting salary and after it stopped that practice in late 2017, the pay gap decreased.\par \par \uc2 Neumark wrote that the $151m estimate was significantly lower than the damages affected women would be owed, which would include significant interest charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis year is \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 100th anniversary and it\u8217\'20\'19s high time that \uc2 Disney\uc2  gets serious about addressing the persistent gender wage gap that we have now documented,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lori Andrus, attorney for the women, whose firm has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/18/business/media/disney-pay-discrimination-lawsuit.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken on Intel}}}\uc2  and previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/local/abcarian/la-me-abcarian-discrimination-settlement-20160624-snap-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  a $4m pay gap settlement against \uc2 Farmers Insurance\uc2 . For the plaintiffs, some of whom continue to work at \uc2 Disney\uc2 , she added, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pretty demoralizing and especially damaging when it\u8217\'20\'19s coming from a brand like \uc2 Disney\uc2  that women in America idolize. They love their jobs. They love the content that \uc2 Disney\uc2  produces and they just want to be paid fairly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shawna M Swanson, associate general counsel and head of the employment law function for \uc2 Disney\uc2 , denied the latest allegations in an email on Friday, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThe plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 assertions about an alleged pay gap between women and men are simply false, which we will demonstrate through the litigation.\u8221\'20\'1D Spokespeople did not address the specific claims in Neumark\u8217\'20\'19s analysis.\par \par \uc2 The company has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2019/apr/03/disney-company-women-pay-gap-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  its \u8220\'20\'1Crobust pay equity practices and policies\u8221\'20\'1D, and under pressure from some shareholders last year, released its own pay gap {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thewaltdisneycompany.eu/app/uploads/2022/04/TheWaltDisneyCompanyUK_DisneyStoreUK_GenderPayReport_2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , which said women are paid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-09-16/disney-shows-adjusted-pay-data-by-race-and-gender-for-first-time?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly identically}}}\uc2  to men.\par \par \uc2 The case is one of many pay gap class-actions against high-profile companies in recent years. \uc2 Google{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/12/business/google-discrimination-settlement-women.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled}}}\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jan/03/google-childcare-center-teachers-women-pay-pay-discrimination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 class-action}}}\uc2  gender {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2018/oct/26/google-gender-pay-gap-women-class-action-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discrimination case}}}\uc2  last year and agreed to pay $118m. In May, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  agreed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/goldman-pay-215-mln-settle-gender-discrimination-lawsuit-bloomberg-news-2023-05-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay $215m to settle a case}}}\uc2  alleging widespread gender discrimination in salary and promotions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230701ej71001eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\