\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US actors union agrees to extend talks as A-list stars show they are ready to strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett in Los Angeles \par \uc2 581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2023\par 02:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meryl Streep, Jennifer Lawrence and others lend their names to demand a strong deal as writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike enters third month\par \par \uc2 The US actors\u8217\'20\'19 union and Hollywood studios announced in a statement on Friday that the two sides had agreed to extend their current labor deal through 12 July, hours before a midnight deadline.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe parties will continue to negotiate under a mutually agreed upon media blackout,\u8221\'20\'1D the parties said.\par \par \uc2 According to the Hollywood Reporter, this move will allow for more time for negotiations and for ongoing projects to continue operating under Screen Actors Guild \u8211\'20\'13 American Federation of Television and Radio Artists (Sag-Aftra) agreements until the new expiration date.\par \par \uc2 If the two parties do not reach an agreement by the end of the day on 12 July, the union can still call a strike \u8211\'20\'13 which, if it came to pass, would be its first targeting major film and television companies in four decades.\par \par \uc2 Fran Drescher, the \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2  president, struck an optimistic note in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iQv94Odx7DI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video to members}}}\uc2  released last week, saying negotiations with the studios were \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely productive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A strike by \uc2 Sag-Aftra\uc2 , which represents 160,000 actors, would come as Hollywood studios are already grappling with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/02/thousands-of-hollywood-film-and-tv-writers-to-go-on-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a nearly two-month work stoppage}}}\uc2  by the Writers Guild of America (WGA), who have been picketing over issues including wages, streaming royalties and the use of artificial intelligence in their work. It would represent the first two-union strike in the industry in more than six decades, with huge consequences for film and television production.\par \par \uc2 The actor Phoebe Waller-Bridge, speaking to Reuters at the Indiana Jones premiere in London, noted that she was already on strike as a member of the WGA.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m on the edge of my seat hoping that Sag will follow suit and stand up in support of the writers, and just really hope we can get this sorted,\u8221\'20\'1D Waller-Bridge said.\par \par \uc2 This week, news outlets reported, more than 300 actors, including some of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent stars, circulated a letter to their union leaders urging them to fight for a strong deal, rather than compromise too soon.\par \par \uc2 Meryl Streep, Jennifer Lawrence, Quinta Brunson, Ben Stiller, Neil Patrick Harris and other celebrities signed the letter telling their leadership, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an unprecedented inflection point in our industry, and what might be considered a good deal in any other years is simply not enough,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rolling Stone{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/meryl-street-top-actors-sag-aftra-prepared-to-strike-1235524973/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One of the key concerns the actors highlighted in the letter to their union leaders this week was how their work may be changed by artificial intelligence technologies, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/hollywood-writers-strike-artificial-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issue that has also become central}}}\uc2  to the ongoing Hollywood writers\u8217\'20\'19 strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe think it is absolutely vital that this negotiation protects not just our likenesses, but makes sure we are well compensated when any of our work is used to train AI,\u8221\'20\'1D the actors wrote to union leaders, according to \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In early June, nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/sag-aftra-members-approve-strike-authorization-9791-yes-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 98% of Sag members}}}\uc2  voted to authorise a strike if needed, a sign of the ongoing tensions between talent and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  as Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s business model has shifted increasingly towards digital and streaming models.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Sag, which agreed to a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/sag-aftra-and-amptp-agree-media-blackout-2023-contract-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 media blackout}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D during its contract negotiations with the studios, did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230630ej6u000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
