\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Workers at over 150 US Starbucks stores to strike over Pride decorations\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 297 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2023\par 14:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 3,500 employees to take part in nationwide strike, led by company\u8217\'20\'19s Seattle Roastery\par \par \uc2 More than 150 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores and 3,500 workers will be on strike next week across the US, the union representing the coffee chain\u8217\'20\'19s baristas said on Friday, after it claimed the company had banned gay Pride month decorations at its cafes.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United union said earlier this month the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jun/14/starbucks-workers-pride-month-no-decorations-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took down}}}\uc2  LGBTQ+ Pride decorations and flags at several stores, while some workers took to social media to report the same.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  on Friday denied the claims as \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse information\u8221\'20\'1D. It said last week there had been \u8220\'20\'1Cno change to any policy on this matter\u8221\'20\'1D and that it was still encouraging store managers to celebrate Pride month.\par \par \uc2 US companies have faced growing criticism {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/24/target-stores-us-withdraw-some-pride-collection-lgbtq-products-items"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the right}}}\uc2  over Pride month celebrations. Last month, retailer Target pulled some LGBTQ-themed products off its shelves following confrontations between some customers and employees.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Workers United said on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBWorkersUnited/status/1672186968707325952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a tweet}}}\uc2  the company\u8217\'20\'19s Seattle Roastery \u8211\'20\'13 located just nine blocks from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 first ever store at the Pike Place Market \u8211\'20\'13 was leading the nationwide strike.\par \par \uc2 STRIKE WITH PRIDE! Seattle Roastery leads nationwide \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  strike over \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 hypocritical treatment of LGBTQIA+ workers. Over 150+ stores and 3,500 workers will be on strike over the course of the next week.\u8212\'20\'14 Starbucks Workers United (@SBWorkersUnited) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBWorkersUnited/status/1672186968707325952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Shares of the company were down about 2% at $99.02 in premarket trading.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , which runs about 9,000 US company-owned locations, has seen employees at more than 300 stores vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/may/12/starbucks-union-busting-nlrb-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to unionize}}}\uc2  since late 2021 demanding better pay and benefits.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230623ej6n001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
