\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rallies with union workers in Philadelphia: \u8216\'20\'18You built America\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and Maya Yang \par \uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2023\par 12:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President enlists support of union members against GOP tax cuts for the wealthy at first political rally of 2024 re-election campaign\par \par \uc2 At his first political rally since announcing his re-election campaign for president in April, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/biden-make-re-election-pitch-unions-pennsylvania-2023-06-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a crowd of labor union supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWall Street didn\u8217\'20\'19t build America \u8211\'20\'13 you did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the investment bankers of this country went on strike tomorrow, no one would notice,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said on Saturday during a speech which alluded to his blue-collar childhood roots in Scranton, Pennsylvania. Renewing his longstanding vocal support for labor unions, he continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIf this room didn\u8217\'20\'19t show up to work tomorrow, the whole country would come to a grinding halt, so tell me \u8211\'20\'13 who matters more in America?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s rally was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1R-rXHWEMk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hosted}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , a federation of 60 labor unions representing 12.5 million workers in the US, which has endorsed Biden and the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , for re-election in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Other unions that have endorsed Biden ahead of his rally included the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers\uc2  as well as the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are the most pro-labor, pro-public education leaders our country has seen in modern history,\u8221\'20\'1D the teachers federation president, \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aft.org/press-release/american-federation-teachers-endorses-joe-biden-and-kamala-harris-democratic-primary#:~:text=WASHINGTON%E2%80%94The%20American%20Federation%20of,in%20the%202024%20Democratic%20primary."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CJoe and Kamala understand in their souls the challenges families face, and how important it is to their dignity to earn a decent living and have a shot at owning a home, or securing a retirement, or affording college. They know union membership can be transformative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lee Saunders\uc2 , the state, county and municipal employees federation president, echoed similar sentiments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/press/releases/2023/afscme-endorsement-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the most pro-worker president of our lifetime. He respects and protects working people \u8211\'20\'13 especially frontline public service workers \u8211\'20\'13 and the essential work they do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Saunders added, \u8220\'20\'1CJoe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just thank us for keeping our communities running; he prioritizes our issues and defends our freedoms \u8211\'20\'13 the freedom to organize, to earn a living wage, to build thriving communities and to have a seat at the table. And he will help us solve the staffing crisis that is pushing millions of public service workers to their breaking point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden began the rally by mentioning that his wife, Jill Biden, belongs to the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2  union and that she is from the Philadelphia-area community of Hammonton, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of politicians in this country who can\u8217\'20\'19t say the word \u8216\'20\'18union\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. But on Saturday he declared himself the most pro-union president in history.\par \par \uc2 Biden cited the jobs recovery under his administration and affirmed an end to trickle-down economics during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll it had done was hollow out the middle class, blow up the deficit, ship jobs overseas, strip the dignity and pride and hope out of community one after another all across America has factories shut down,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden asserted.\par \par \uc2 He continued by outlining his efforts to oppose Republican legislative policies such as social security cuts and what he called unfair tax codes and loopholes utilized by the largest corporation and the wealthy, including tax rates for billionaires that are low when compared with those levied on other workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust pay your fair share man,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden quipped. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about time the super wealthy start paying their fair share.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He concluded his appearance at the rally by enlisting the support of union members in his re-election campaign to fight against Republican efforts to reinstate tax cuts for the wealthy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re coming for your jobs \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re coming for your future,\u8221\'20\'1D he warned. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for everyone, no matter how rich or powerful they are, to start paying their fair share, you\u8217\'20\'19ve carried this country on your back long enough, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for millionaires and billionaires and big corporations to pay their fair share. I can get that done, but I need you badly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s address on Saturday echoed September 2021 remarks in which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2021/09/08/remarks-by-president-biden-in-honor-of-labor-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI intend to be the most pro-union president leading the most pro-union administration in American history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his victorious 2020 presidential run, he had also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=654501604985268"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a union man. Period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In February, the Biden administration announced a new plan to encourage further union membership across the country. The plan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/07/biden-union-labor-white-house-organizing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 includes}}}\uc2  70 recommendations that would make it easier for federal employees to join unions and remove barriers for union organizers to talk with workers on federal property.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s itinerary on Saturday included taking an aerial tour of the interstate 95 bridge collapse during the previous weekend in Philadelphia, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsWire_US/status/1669757009414041607?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . An elevated section of the bridge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/11/vehicle-fire-interstate-95-collapse-philadelphia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapsed}}}\uc2  on 11 June after a vehicle caught on fire, prompting transportation officials to warn of extensive delays and street closures.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230617ej6h001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
