\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Workers sue secretive elite club Bohemian Grove for wage theft\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,056 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2023\par 16:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 27\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The private club, which has included Reagan and Nixon among its members, is accused of failing to pay overtime and not giving breaks\par \par \uc2 Workers at Bohemian Grove, one of the most elite and secretive clubs in the US, have filed a lawsuit alleging numerous unfair labor practices, including 16-hour workdays without breaks, and a failure to pay overtime and minimum wages to the workers.\par \par \uc2 Bohemian Grove, which attracts some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful people to a mysterious gathering in the woods north of San Francisco, has long been the subject of fascination and conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfgate.com/local/article/san-francisco-bohemian-club-sued-by-valets-18148391.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  lawsuit}}}\uc2  was brought by former valets who worked for several years at the club\u8217\'20\'19s Monte Rio summer camp in Sonoma county, California. The secretive 2,700-acre camp near the Russian River has operated every summer for 150 years and is rumored to end in a ritual involving a human effigy and burning of a giant sacrificial owl.\par \par \uc2 The club was purportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfgate.com/lifestyle/travel/article/what-is-bohemian-grove-the-secretive-camp-17884488.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  visited}}}\uc2  by the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and billionaire donor Harlan Crow, and has been rumored over the years to be the site where Richard Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s successful 1968 presidential election campaign was launched, and where J Robert Oppenheimer first discussed the Manhattan Project.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfgate.com/lifestyle/travel/article/what-is-bohemian-grove-the-secretive-camp-17884488.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  club}}}\uc2  currently has a list of 2,600 active members and a sizable wait list. Members have included individuals such as \uc2 Henry Kissinger\uc2 , Richard Nixon, Ronald Reagan, \uc2 Charles Schwab\uc2  and several other powerful political and economic leaders around the world.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit alleges about 100 separate camps that comprise the club each have one or more captains who violate numerous labor laws every summer. The complaint includes an allegation that Bohemian Grove treasurer, Bill Dawson, has personally directed valets to \u8220\'20\'1Cfalsify payroll records and to work off-the-clock\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit alleges valets were paid only eight hours despite working 16-plus hours a day without breaks for the duration of a 14-day summer camp.\par \par \uc2 Another allegation in the lawsuit claims a worker was directed to hide from a payroll employee when they made a surprise visit to the camp, as they were being paid under the table.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just want this to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D said a former valet at the camps, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation from the club or members.\par \par \uc2 The worker described members as obscenely wealthy, with private jets, million-dollar cars, $200,000 watches and homes on billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s beach in Malibu. They said they would have to perform tasks beyond their job duties for some members, such as one instance where a billionaire member forgot to bring underwear to the camp and valets were asked to hand-wash it.\par \par \uc2 They explained over the years, the conditions, overworking and lack of pay for overtime, lack of breaks, would worsen despite promises to workers to do otherwise. Those promises, kind words from some of the very wealthy members, friendship with co-workers, kept them coming back year after year to the job, the worker added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s still going on, the payroll stuff, the unpaid overtime. The rates if the day is set, but even if you work 23.5 hours a day, your daily rate is your daily rate. This was all kind of conceived to save money, which is kind of comical,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said, referring to the immense wealth members had.\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe club really struggled hiring staff the last few years because they\u8217\'20\'19re just not getting with the program of modern labor, modern food service labor where you have to pay a better wage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They argued the isolation of the camps and demanding environment amplified some of the typical poor working conditions in the restaurant and hospitality industry, because there is no internet, no cell service, and the pressure from the club to meet the demands of members and keep enticing new, very wealthy members into the club.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of these kind words and supposed good gestures were only available to me if I kept my mouth shut, and if I worked around the clock and didn\u8217\'20\'19t complain, so I feel used,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CI gave them a lot of good years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is seeking class-action status, affecting 300 employees who work outside of camps that use a staffing firm for hiring, and seek {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/article/news/former-valets-suing-over-wages-at-bohemian-grove/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  up to $1.5m}}}\uc2  in damages from the all-male club Bohemian Grove.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/article/news/former-valets-suing-over-wages-at-bohemian-grove/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  claim}}}\uc2  the club and its partners had agreed to pay the remainder of what was owed to the workers, but never followed through in doing so.\par \par \uc2 Due to the secrecy of the club, the lawsuit refers to several defendants as \u8220\'20\'1CJohn Doe\u8221\'20\'1D because their names are unknown to the workers.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit also alleges work rules imposed on the workers, such as restricting their ability to make phone calls from the camp, prohibiting workers from working in or visiting any camp where a blood relative is a member, prohibiting workers from accepting any tips, and prohibiting attendance by workers of any \u8220\'20\'1Crehearsals, plays, speeches, or any performances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A previous lawsuit was filed by former workers of Bohemian Grove over similar allegations between 2015 and 2019. A lawyer representing those workers said the court approved a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.simpluris.com/websites/f5c46828-be10-4c11-9207-41da51d1f930/documents/d1c0b13d-432d-487b-a55c-866bb04a8512/BohemainClub_Ulucan_Long%20Form%20Notice%20v4%20-%20clean.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  settlement}}}\uc2  in that lawsuit in late 2021 of $3.535m.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, the Bohemian Club {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfgate.com/bayarea/article/SF-s-Bohemian-Club-to-pay-workers-7-million-in-8337685.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  paid $7m}}}\uc2  in a similar case where wage theft was alleged. The Bohemian Club {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfgate.com/local/article/bohemian-club-responds-to-california-lawsuit-18150720.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  responded}}}\uc2  to the lawsuit claiming they should not be party to this action because the workers were not directly employed by the club.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough the Club has not been served with this lawsuit, we have reviewed the allegations and it is clear the claims appearing in the lawsuit are brought by individuals who were never employed by the Bohemian Club and therefore the Club should not be a party to this action,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson for the club and they denied allegations of wage theft.\par \par \uc2 Tony Nunes, the, attorney representing workers rejected the claim.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit noted: \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiffs believe that Defendant Bohemian Club will likely attempt to shield itself from legal liability by asserting that the camps operate autonomously. Nevertheless, the camps are not independent legal entities making their own hiring decision, but a part of a joint venture as designed by Bohemian Club.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230618ej6i000p4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
