\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Directors union reaches tentative deal with Hollywood studios as writers strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and agencies \par \uc2 364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par 10:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Agreement comes as writers remain on strike and actors are currently holding a strike authorization vote\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Directors Guild of America\uc2  (\uc2 DGA\uc2 ) which represents film and television directors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/directors-guild-reaches-tentative-deal-with-hollywood-studios-2023-06-04/#:~:text=June%204%20(Reuters)%20%2D%20Hollywood's,to%20settle%20with%20striking%20writers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  late on Saturday that it had reached a tentative agreement with Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s major studios, averting a possible work stoppage.\par \par \uc2 The development comes as Hollywood writers are currently on strike and actors represented by the Sag-Aftra union are currently holding a strike authorization vote.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 DGA\uc2  union will proceed to ask its 19,000 members to vote on the tentative three-year contract, which includes gains in wages, residuals and protections around the use of artificial intelligence. The agreement stipulates, \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerative AI cannot replace the duties performed by members\u8221\'20\'1D. The agreement came after several weeks during which Hollywood writers have been on strike. Previous negotiations between directors and the studios took place earlier this year without reaching an agreement, but bargaining {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikeRoyce/status/1665378917618778113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restarted }}}\uc2  three weeks ago once writers began their strike.\par \par \uc2 A ratification vote is scheduled for Tuesday 6 June.\par \par \uc2 Writers and actors have also been seeking protections included in contracts around the use of artificial intelligence. Writers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KirkWrites79/status/1665324495672942592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized }}}\uc2  the rejection of their proposals around artificial intelligence by the studios, instead only being offered annual meetings to discuss the issue. Prior to the directors reaching a tentative agreement, the Writers Guild of America {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/06/wga-amptp-gaslighting-lie-contract-talks-1235398467/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized }}}\uc2  Hollywood studios over the anticipation of using an agreement with the directors to force writers to accept similar terms to end their strike.\par \par \uc2 The Sag-Aftra national board unanimously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/strike-authorization-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked }}}\uc2  members to vote to authorize a strike, with voting open until late on Monday 5 June. Negotiations with Hollywood studios for their new TV/theatrical agreement are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sagaftra.org/sag-aftra-strike-authorization-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set}}}\uc2  to begin on 7 June.\par \par \uc2 Over 11,000 film and television writers have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/may/04/writers-on-why-theyre-standing-up-to-hollywood-this-is-fundamentally-broken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  since 1 May, over what writers say have been dwindling compensation and residuals amid the rise of streaming services.\par \par \uc2 The strike has halted production of several television and film projects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/05/08/hollywood-writers-strike-halts-stranger-things-severance-production.html#:~:text=Entertainment-,Hollywood%20writers'%20strike%20halts%20production%20of%20'Stranger%20Things%2C',Severance%2C'%20Marvel's%20'Blade'&text=Members%20of%20the%20Writers%20Guild,is%20already%20hurting%20Hollywood%20productions."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  season 2 of Severance, the final season of \uc2 Netflix\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Stranger Things, and Marvel\u8217\'20\'19s Blade.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed\par \par \uc2 reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230605ej650015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
