\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Afternoon Update: minimum wage rises; education minister looks at Hecs debt changes; and a glitzy royal wedding\b0\par\par\uc2 Jordyn Beazley \par \uc2 874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2023\par 07:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Want to get this in your inbox every weekday? Sign up for the Afternoon Update here, and start your day with our Morning Mail newsletter.\par \par \uc2 Happy Friday! Almost 2.75 million {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/jun/02/minimum-wage-rise-award-australia-lowest-paid-workers-5-75-per-cent-increase-wages-from-july-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australians will receive a pay rise}}}\uc2  of 5.75% from 1 July after the \uc2 Fair Work Commission\uc2  announced its decision for those on minimum and award wages.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fwc.gov.au/documents/resources/2023fwcfb3500.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 annual wage review decision}}}\uc2 , released today, indicates the minimum wages will increase to $882.80 per week or $23.23 per hour. For some workers on the lowest award rate, the rise will be 8.6%.\par \par \uc2 The increase is about midway between the 3.8% some business groups such as AiGroup called for, and the 7% sought by the \uc2 ACTU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a critical increase during this cost of living crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Sally McManus\uc2 , secretary of the \uc2 ACTU\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 Top news\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ben Roberts-Smith\uc2  resigns from Seven |\par \par \uc2 The former soldier has resigned from \uc2 Seven West Media\uc2  a day after a judge dismissed his defamation action against three newspapers who he found had proven in their defence that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/jun/02/ben-roberts-smith-resigns-from-seven-network-queensland-general-manager-after-losing-defamation-case-trial-verdict-against-nine-newspapers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roberts-Smith murdered unarmed civilians}}}\uc2  while serving in the military in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Yamba shooting treated as murder-suicide |\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/jun/02/shooting-deaths-of-boy-15-and-his-father-being-treated-as-a-murder-suicide-nsw-police-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting deaths}}}\uc2  of a 15-year-old boy and his 58-year-old father, Wayne Smith, in Yamba on the New South Wales north coast are being treated by police as a murder-suicide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Minister may change Hecs debt pile-on |\par \par \uc2 The education minister, Jason Clare, says there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2023/jun/02/australia-news-live-ben-roberts-smith-defamation-case-fallout-minimum-wage-rise-interest-rates-cost-of-living-regional-security-online-gambling?page=with:block-647929eb8f08403f1d17eeba#block-647929eb8f08403f1d17eeba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be merit in changing how Hecs interest is calculated}}}\uc2  after thousands of current and former students woke up to higher debt. Clare has ordered the team conducting a review into education reform to look at the issue.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 State of Origin throat injury |\par \par \uc2 The New South Wales women\u8217\'20\'19s State of Origin side is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/02/isabelle-kelly-womens-state-of-origin-2023-nsw-blues-hospital-throat-injury-game-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuming after match officials allowed play to continue }}}\uc2  following a serious throat injury that hospitalised co-captain Isabelle Kelly in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2023/jun/01/womens-state-of-origin-2023-game-1-live-score-updates-qld-maroons-vs-nsw-blues-team-list-what-time-is-kickoff-start-queensland-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s series opener}}}\uc2 . Kelly has been cleared of a throat fracture but remained in hospital on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Taiwan and US sign trade deal |\par \par \uc2 The United States and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taiwan}}}\uc2  have signed a trade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/02/taiwan-hails-comprehensive-trade-deal-with-us-as-china-issues-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deal aimed at deepening economic relations}}}\uc2  between both sides \u8211\'20\'13 in a move that has sparked a warning from Beijing. Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s government has described the deal as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most comprehensive\u8221\'20\'1D trade agreement signed with Washington since 1979.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US AI drone killed its operator |\par \par \uc2 In a simulated test staged by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US military}}}\uc2 , an air force drone controlled by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/01/us-military-drone-ai-killed-operator-simulated-test"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI killed its operator to prevent it from interfering}}}\uc2  with its efforts to achieve its mission, an official said last month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fox News edits Trump |\par \par \uc2 Fox News hosted a town hall event in Iowa with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  on Thursday night, but the pre-taped hour-long prime-time special hosted by \uc2 Sean Hannity{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/01/trump-fox-news-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excluded any mention of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy theory}}}\uc2  that the 2020 election was stolen from him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US fines \uc2 British Airways\uc2  |\par \par \uc2 British Airways\uc2  has been fined US$1.1m by the US over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jun/01/us-fines-british-airways-11m-for-failing-to-refund-covid-cancellations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims it failed to pay refunds for cancelled flights}}}\uc2  during the coronavirus pandemic. The US Transportation Department said in a legal document the airline did not \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide timely refunds to passengers\u8221\'20\'1D for abandoned or rescheduled flights to and from the country in 2020.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s royal wedding\par \par \uc2 |\par \par \uc2 Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s monarchy has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/01/jordan-crown-prince-hussein-royal-wedding-rajwa-alseif-saudi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cemented the role}}}\uc2  of its 28-year-old crown prince with a wedding attended by global royalty, including Britain\u8217\'20\'19s Prince and Princess of Wales, in a glittering show seeking to buttress the succession and move on from a painful family scandal.\par \par \uc2 Full Story\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s most decorated living soldier has lost his defamation case against the Sydney Morning Herald, the Age and the Canberra Times. A federal court judge has found that the newspapers proved in their defence that \uc2 Ben Roberts-Smith\uc2  either murdered or was complicit in and responsible for the murder of unarmed civilians while serving in the Australian military in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Ben Doherty reports from court, sifting through the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and what it means for public interest journalism.\par \par \uc2 What they said \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe best decision for workers we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 minister for employment and workplace relations, Tony Burke.\par \par \uc2 Burke was commenting on the annual wage review\u8217\'20\'19s decision to boost the minimum wage by 5.75%.\par \par \uc2 Before bed read\par \par \uc2 Whether you\u8217\'20\'19re a cat lover or staunch dog person, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a story for each camp to help understand the behaviours of their pets.\par \par \uc2 Lili Chin has broken down the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/jun/01/kitty-confidential-13-secret-signals-all-cat-owners-need-to-know-from-a-quivering-tail-to-aeroplane-ears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 secret signals cat owners need to know}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 from a quivering tale to aeroplane ears.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Susan Hazel and Joshua Zoanetti {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/jun/02/why-do-dogs-eat-grass-and-when-is-it-not-safe-for-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have answered a question}}}\uc2  that may have long intrigued dog and cat lovers alike: Why do dogs eat grass? And is it safe?\par \par \uc2 Daily word game\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s starter word is: INTI . You have five goes to get the longest word including the starter word. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Play Wordiply}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive this Afternoon Update to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/oct/13/afternoon-update-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 . And start your day with a curated breakdown of the key stories you need to know. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/23/morning-mail-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up-inbox-subscribe?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for our Morning Mail news