\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling makes it easier for companies to sue striking workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe and agency \par \uc2 496 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2023\par 17:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  is sole dissenter as court sides with Washington state concrete firm in ruling seen as blow to unions\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Thursday made it easier for employers to pursue lawsuits against striking workers, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/22pdf/21-1449_d9eh.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a decision}}}\uc2  seen as a setback to labor unions.\par \par \uc2 The opinion, written by Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  and backed by not just conservative colleagues but all except one on the nine-member bench, sided with a concrete business in Washington state that sued the union representing its truck drivers after a work stoppage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ketanji-brown-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2 , the bench\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/08/black-lawmakers-ketanji-brown-jackson-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recently}}}\uc2  confirmed associate member, was the lone dissenter, noting \u8220\'20\'1Ctoday the court falters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The decision in the case of \uc2 Glacier Northwest Inc\uc2  against a local affiliate of the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  overturned a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in the union\u8217\'20\'19s favor.\par \par \uc2 Glacier had accused the union of intentional property destruction during a 2017 strike when a group of drivers went on strike on a day when their mixing trucks were filled with concrete for delivery to customers. The company had been forced to discard the unused product at a financial loss. If the concrete is left in the trucks to harden, the vehicles can sustain serious damage.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court overruled the Washington state supreme court ruling that the loss was incidental to a strike that could be considered arguably protected under the \uc2 National Labor Relations\uc2  Act (NLRA).\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration urged the justices to reverse the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, Reuters reports. The decision allows Glacier\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit to proceed.\par \par \uc2 It also extends the panel\u8217\'20\'19s recent trend of curtailing the power of labor unions. In 2021, justices struck down a California agricultural regulation aimed at helping unions organize workers, the agency said.\par \par \uc2 And in 2018 it ruled that non-members cannot be forced, as they are in certain states, to pay fees to unions representing public employees such as police and teachers that negotiate collective bargaining agreements with employers.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Barrett said the union\u8217\'20\'19s actions had not only destroyed the concrete but had also \u8220\'20\'1Cposed a risk of foreseeable, aggravated and imminent harm to Glacier\u8217\'20\'19s trucks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause the union took affirmative steps to endanger Glacier\u8217\'20\'19s property rather than reasonable precautions to mitigate that risk, the NLRA does not arguably protect its conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 Jackson, in a 27-page dissent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/22pdf/21-1449_d9eh.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included with}}}\uc2  the court\u8217\'20\'19s published opinion, wrote that the ruling \u8220\'20\'1Crisks erosion of the right to strike\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cis likely to cause considerable confusion among the lower courts\u8221\'20\'1D about how pre-emption under the National Labor Relations Act should apply in future cases.\par \par \uc2 None of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/us-supreme-end-contentious-2022-23-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bigger decisions expected}}}\uc2  from the court as it concludes its term came on Thursday. Those, covering affirmative action in higher education, LGBTQ+ equality and the rights of Native American tribes, are now expected later this month.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230601ej61001xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
