\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican Iowa governor rolls back state\u8217\'20\'19s child labor law protections\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 487 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 May 2023\par 18:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Change in law allows teenagers to serve alcohol in restaurants and could allow children to operate heavy machinery like power saws\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , has signed a bill that rolls back several child labor law protections in the midwestern state, including how many hours children can work and at what type of establishments.\par \par \uc2 Iowa and several other states in the US have loosened regulations on child labor in response to some businesses complaining about a workforce shortage. The moves have been met with widespread criticism by Democrats and labor groups.\par \par \uc2 Reynolds signed the legislation on Friday, which was approved by lawmakers in May with only Republican support, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/iowa-governor-child-labor-laws-e8cb29e2a45b956489c4a192b7ddeba5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the Associated Press}}}\uc2 . Democrats and other critics warned that the bill could causes businesses to exploit children and distract minors from school.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this legislation Iowa joins 20 other states in providing tailored, common sense labor provisions that allow young adults to develop their skills in the workforce,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.iowa.gov/press-release/2023-05-26/gov-reynolds-signs-several-bills-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reynolds said in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s new law, 14- and 15-year-olds are allowed to work two extra hours per day during the school year, a total of six hours. 14- and 15-year olds are also allowed to do certain type of works that were previously banned, including work in industrial laundry services, freezers, and meat coolers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/26/politics/iowa-child-labor-law-kim-reynolds/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the same time 16- and 17-year-olds will be permitted to work the same hours as adults. Teenagers as young as 16 can also now serve alcohol in restaurants, as long as employers have permission from the minor\u8217\'20\'19s parent or guardian. The change in law could allow children to operate heavy machinery such as power saws, or join in on demolition projects, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 Two adults are required to be present when children are serving alcohol. Minor employees also have to complete a \u8220\'20\'1Ctraining on prevention and response to sexual harassment\u8221\'20\'1D, reported CNN.\par \par \uc2 Children as young as 16 can now also work in areas including manufacturing, with an exemption from the Iowa department of education or Iowa workforce development as long as its part of a work-based learning program.\par \par \uc2 Reynolds also signed several other laws on Friday, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wowt.com/2023/05/26/gov-reynolds-signs-education-reform-law-including-ban-books-teaching-lgbtq-topics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on school materials }}}\uc2  about sexual orientation and gender identity in classrooms from kindergarten through sixth grade.\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s loosening of child labor laws comes amid high-profile cases in several states, as Republicans across the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/11/us-child-labor-laws-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempt to roll back child labor laws}}}\uc2  amid increasing violations.\par \par \uc2 A May investigation by the \uc2 US Department of Labor{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/03/kentucky-mcdonalds-child-labor-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that several \uc2 McDonalds\uc2  franchises in Kentucky violated child labor laws, including using at least two 10-year-olds for unpaid labor, often until 2am.\par \par \uc2 In February, a separate investigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/feb/17/underage-child-labor-working-slaughterhouse-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that over 100 children were illegally employed at a slaughterhouse cleaning plant, working with dangerous chemicals and equipment, including saws.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230527ej5r001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
